g","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#cdn-and-caching","content":"CDN and caching"},"4":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Put an nginx cache in front of chop. Responses depend on the `Accept` header, and `Vary: Accept` alone makes nginx cache a separate copy for every distinct `Accept` string. Browsers send dozens of them, but chop only produces three variants of an image: AVIF, WebP and the source format. Collapse the header into those three buckets, use the bucket in the cache key, and send the same bucket upstream, so that the body in the cache always matches its key:"},"5":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"How it works:"},"6":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"A request without `image/avif` or `image/webp`, or with `q=0` for them, is the `original` bucket, and chop answers in the source format, as it would for any client without `Accept`."},"7":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"`image/*` and `*/*` don't select a bucket, the same as in chop, so a client that only accepts wildcards gets a format that it can display."},"8":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"A cached response always has the format that its bucket gets from chop, since the key and the upstream header come from the same variable."},"9":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Only the `Accept` header and the URL select a variant, so a purge needs three keys per URL, one for each bucket, like `$host$uri$is_args$args|avif`."},"10":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"chop's strong `ETag` and `If-None-Match` handling work through the cache, and the `ETag` of an image is the same for every `Accept` that gets the same bytes."},"11":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Cache only `200` and `404`, as the recipe does, and not `any`. A `502` or `504` means that the origin failed for a moment, and caching it would keep a broken image for as long as the `proxy_cache_valid` time. chop sends `Cache-Control: no-store` with every error, which nginx respects unless you ignore that header."},"12":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"For remote originals, `proxy_cache_lock on` makes concurrent requests for the same variant wait for one fetch, and `proxy_cache_min_uses 2` keeps one-off requests for unusual sizes out of the cache. See Securing remote origins."},"13":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"If you disable AVIF in chop (`CHOP_AVIF=false`), the `avif` bucket holds WebP, which is correct but caches the same image twice. Remove the AVIF line from the first `map` then."},"14":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Pass the `Accept` buckets on to any CDN in front of nginx in the same way, with a custom cache key built from a normalized header, and see CDN and caching."},"15":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#cdn-and-caching","content":"The nginx recipe covers the cache next to chop. Responses depend on the `Accept` header, so the CDN must use it in the cache key, or at least whether it lists `image/avif` and `image/webp`. Every response has `Vary: Accept`, but many CDNs ignore `Vary` unless configured, and without it a cached AVIF can be sent to a browser that can't display it. Normalizing `Accept` at the edge to a small set of values (`image/avif,image/webp`, `image/webp` and none) keeps the number of cached variants low."},"16":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/caching.html#cdn-and-caching","content":"The responses are immutable by design (`Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000` by default and a strong `ETag`), so change the URL, for example with `?ver=3`, when an original changes, which also holds for a remote origin, since chop doesn't cache originals and doesn't look at the cache headers of the origin. Set `allowedWidths` to the widths of your `srcset` so that the server can't be used to generate unbounded variants, and put the server behind the CDN only. Use `/healthz` for health checks."},"17":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","type":"page","content":"CLI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html"},"18":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"The `chop` command runs the server. Give it a data directory or an origin, and a port:"},"19":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"| Argument             | Description                                                                                                       | Example                   |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `-d`, `--data <dir>` | Directory with the original images. Defaults to `CHOP_DATA_DIR`, then `/data`. Can't be combined with `--origin`. | `chop --data /srv/images` |","table":"table-0"},"20":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"| Argument               | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | Example                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `-o`, `--origin <url>` | Serve the images of this `https://` origin, like `https://uploads.example.com/base`, or of an S3 bucket, like `s3://my-bucket/uploads`, instead of a directory. Defaults to `CHOP_ORIGIN`. See Sources and S3 and S3-compatible storage. | `chop --origin https://uploads.example.com` |","table":"table-0"},"21":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"| Argument           | Description                                                                                    | Example        |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `-p`, `--port <n>` | Port to listen on. Defaults to `PORT`, then `CHOP_PORT`, then `8080`. Use `0` for a free port. | `chop -p 3000` |","table":"table-0"},"22":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"| Argument           | Description                                                    | Example                 |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `--host <address>` | Address to listen on. Defaults to `CHOP_HOST`, then `0.0.0.0`. | `chop --host 127.0.0.1` |","table":"table-0"},"23":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"| Argument          | Description                                                                                                                                         | Example                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `--scheme <name>` | URL scheme, `query` or `cloudflare`. Repeat it to enable several, tried in order, and list `query` last. Overrides `CHOP_SCHEMES`. See URL schemes. | `chop --scheme cloudflare --scheme query` |","table":"table-0"},"24":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"| Argument       | Description     | Example       |\n| -------------- | --------------- | ------------- |\n| `-h`, `--help` | Show the usage. | `chop --help` |","table":"table-0"},"25":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"Flags override environment variables, and `--origin` replaces `CHOP_DATA_DIR` while `--data` replaces `CHOP_ORIGIN`, so the flag works in an environment that sets the other one. Setting both a data directory and an origin is an invalid setting. The other settings are read from `CHOP_*` environment variables (see Settings), and a number or boolean that can't be parsed is reported with the name of the variable. Startup prints one line with the address and the data directory or origin, and a warning line on the standard error for each risky setting (`CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=*`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` and an S3 origin without credentials). When an origin refuses a request or fails, the reason is written to the standard error as `origin <code>: <reason>`, since the client only gets a plain `404`, `502` or `504`. `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG=1` prints one JSON line per request to the standard output, with `method`, `path`, `status`, `duration` (milliseconds) and `bytes`."},"26":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/cli.html","content":"The exit code is `0` after a clean shutdown, `1` when the server can't start (a missing data directory or a port that is in use), and `2` for invalid options or settings. On `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` the server stops accepting connections, closes idle ones, waits for running requests and exits with `0`."},"27":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","type":"page","content":"Configuration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html"},"28":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"Settings come from the `CHOP_*` environment variables of the command, from the options of `createConfig()`, or from a few command line flags. A number or boolean that can't be parsed is reported with the name of the variable, and a value that can't be used is an invalid setting."},"29":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable | Default | Description                                              |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dataDir` | `CHOP_DATA_DIR`      | `/data` | Directory with the originals, when there is no `origin`. |","table":"table-0"},"30":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable             | Default | Description                                                                      |\n| --------- | -------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `schemes` | `CHOP_SCHEMES` (comma separated) | `query` | Names of the URL schemes, tried in order. An unknown name is an invalid setting. |","table":"table-0"},"31":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default    | Description                          |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `maxAge` | `CHOP_MAX_AGE`       | `31536000` | Seconds in `Cache-Control: max-age`. |","table":"table-0"},"32":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable   | Default        | Description                        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `maxConcurrency` | `CHOP_MAX_CONCURRENCY` | number of CPUs | Images processed at the same time. |","table":"table-0"},"33":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                        |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `maxQueue` | `CHOP_MAX_QUEUE`     | `64`    | Requests that wait for a slot, in arrival order. More are a `503`. |","table":"table-0"},"34":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable   | Default    | Description                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------- |\n| `maxInputBytes` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_BYTES` | `52428800` | Largest original in bytes. |","table":"table-0"},"35":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable    | Default     | Description                                                  |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `maxInputPixels` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_PIXELS` | `120000000` | Largest original in pixels, which stops decompression bombs. |","table":"table-0"},"36":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default | Description                     |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `maxOutputDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_OUTPUT_DIMENSION` | `8192`  | Largest output width or height. |","table":"table-0"},"37":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable         | Default | Description                                              |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `maxUpscaleDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_UPSCALE_DIMENSION` | `4096`  | Largest long side of an enlarged image with `upscale=1`. |","table":"table-0"},"38":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default | Description           |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `jpegQuality` | `CHOP_JPEG_QUALITY`  | `82`    | Default JPEG quality. |","table":"table-0"},"39":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default | Description                 |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | --------------------------- |\n| `webpQuality` | `CHOP_WEBP_QUALITY`  | `80`    | Default lossy WebP quality. |","table":"table-0"},"40":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default | Description           |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `avifQuality` | `CHOP_AVIF_QUALITY`  | `55`    | Default AVIF quality. |","table":"table-0"},"41":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                                                                              |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `avif`  | `CHOP_AVIF`          | `true`  | Whether AVIF output is enabled. `false` removes `avif` from `autoFormats`, and doesn't affect an explicit `format=avif`. |","table":"table-0"},"42":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default | Description                                     |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `avifEffort` | `CHOP_AVIF_EFFORT`   | `4`     | AVIF encoder effort from 0 (fast) to 9 (small). |","table":"table-0"},"43":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                    | Default | Description                                                      |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedWidths` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_WIDTHS` (comma separated) | unset   | When set, the output width of every request must be in the list. |","table":"table-0"},"44":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `origin` | `CHOP_ORIGIN`        | unset   | Base URL that plain paths are appended to, instead of the data directory, or `s3://bucket[/prefix]` for an S3 bucket. Can't be combined with an explicit `dataDir`. |","table":"table-0"},"45":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting           | Environment variable     | Default | Description                                         |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originAllowHttp` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP` | `false` | Allow `http://` for the origin and for URL sources. |","table":"table-0"},"46":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default | Description                                                                                             |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originAllowPrivate` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` | `false` | Allow the configured origin at a loopback, private or link-local address. Never applies to URL sources. |","table":"table-0"},"47":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                  |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `originAuth` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH`   | unset   | `Authorization` header value for the configured origin only. |","table":"table-0"},"48":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                                  |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Endpoint` | `CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`   | unset   | Base URL of an S3-compatible service for an `s3://` origin. Unset means AWS. |","table":"table-0"},"49":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable           | Default | Description                                                                       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Region` | `CHOP_S3_REGION`, `AWS_REGION` | unset   | Region to sign for. Required on AWS, `us-east-1` with an endpoint, `auto` for R2. |","table":"table-0"},"50":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default                                 | Description                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3PathStyle` | `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE` | `true` with an endpoint, `false` on AWS | Put the bucket in the path instead of the host. Buckets with dots on AWS are always path-style. |","table":"table-0"},"51":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                         | Default | Description                                                   |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3AccessKeyId` | `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | unset   | Access key. Without a key and a secret requests are unsigned. |","table":"table-0"},"52":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting             | Environment variable                                 | Default | Description                                               |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3SecretAccessKey` | `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | unset   | Secret of the access key. Environment only, never logged. |","table":"table-0"},"53":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable                         | Default | Description                                                                            |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3SessionToken` | `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN`, `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` | unset   | Token of temporary credentials, which isn't refreshed. Environment only, never logged. |","table":"table-0"},"54":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting                | Environment variable          | Default | Description                                             |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originConnectTimeout` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONNECT_TIMEOUT` | `3000`  | Milliseconds to connect, including TLS, before a `504`. |","table":"table-0"},"55":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable  | Default | Description                                         |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originTimeout` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_TIMEOUT` | `10000` | Milliseconds for the whole download before a `504`. |","table":"table-0"},"56":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting             | Environment variable      | Default | Description                                                  |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `originConcurrency` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY` | `4`     | Downloads at the same time, outside of the processing slots. |","table":"table-0"},"57":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default | Description                                       |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originQueue` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_QUEUE`  | `32`    | Downloads that wait for a slot. More are a `503`. |","table":"table-0"},"58":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting        | Environment variable                   | Default | Description                                                                                               |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedHosts` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (comma separated) | unset   | Hosts that URL sources may name: `host`, `*.example.com`, `host:port` or `*`. Unset means no URL sources. |","table":"table-0"},"59":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable                           | Default                  | Description                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedInputFormats` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_INPUT_FORMATS` (comma separated) | `jpeg,png,gif,webp,avif` | The formats of the originals that are processed (`jpeg` or `jpg`, `png`, `gif`, `webp`, `avif`). Others are a `415`. An empty list or an unknown name is an invalid setting. |","table":"table-0"},"60":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable                             | Default     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `autoFormats` | `CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS` (comma separated, or `none`) | `avif,webp` | The formats that `format=auto` can negotiate, in order of preference (`avif`, `webp`). An empty list (`none` in the environment) disables the upgrades. Unknown or repeated names are an invalid setting. |","table":"table-0"},"61":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html","type":"page","content":"Development","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/development.html"},"62":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/development.html#license","content":"License"},"63":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/development.html","content":"Run these from the repository root:"},"64":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/development.html","content":"The source runs directly with Node's type stripping through the `wpelevator-source` export condition, and `dist` is only for publishing. Tests are co-located `*.test.ts` files that use `node:test`, and each test name starts with the requirement ID of the specification that it covers, like `R-FMT-3`. `src/test-fixtures.ts` creates temporary data directories and generates the images with sharp, so there are no binary fixtures."},"65":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/development.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/development.html#license","content":"MIT. chop was implemented from a written behavior specification and the repository conventions, without reference to the source code of any other image server. The reference summarizes that behavior."},"66":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","type":"page","content":"Formats and quality","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html"},"67":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#restricting-formats","content":"Restricting formats"},"68":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"Quality and size"},"69":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"Choices where the specification is silent"},"70":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","content":"With `format=auto` (the default), the format is chosen from the `Accept` header for a still image among the formats of `autoFormats` (`avif,webp` by default): AVIF if it's listed and the output is lossy, or WebP if it's listed and the output fits the 16383 pixel limit of WebP, otherwise the fallback format. When the client lists both, the format with the highest `q` is used, and the earlier format of `autoFormats` wins a tie. Browsers send no `q` for image types, so they get the first format of `autoFormats` that they accept, as before, while a header like `image/avif;q=0.5,image/webp` now gives WebP. The fallback is GIF for a GIF source, PNG for lossless or transparent output, and JPEG otherwise."},"71":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","content":"The header is parsed per RFC 9110, ignoring whitespace and case, and a type with `q=0` is not accepted. `image/*` and `*/*` never make AVIF or WebP acceptable: only a listed `image/avif` or `image/webp` does, so clients that don't list them get a format that they can display. An explicit `format` is used even if `Accept` doesn't list it, and it isn't restricted by `autoFormats`, which only governs the negotiation."},"72":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","content":"| Source                 | `Accept` lists `image/avif` and `image/webp` | `Accept` lists `image/webp` | No `Accept`, or `image/*`    |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| JPEG, lossy WebP, AVIF | AVIF                                         | WebP                        | JPEG (PNG with transparency) |","table":"table-0"},"73":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","content":"| Source             | `Accept` lists `image/avif` and `image/webp` | `Accept` lists `image/webp` | No `Accept`, or `image/*` |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| PNG, lossless WebP | Lossless WebP                                | Lossless WebP               | PNG                       |","table":"table-0"},"74":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","content":"| Source | `Accept` lists `image/avif` and `image/webp` | `Accept` lists `image/webp` | No `Accept`, or `image/*` |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| GIF    | Lossless WebP                                | Lossless WebP               | GIF                       |","table":"table-0"},"75":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","content":"| Source               | `Accept` lists `image/avif` and `image/webp` | `Accept` lists `image/webp` | No `Accept`, or `image/*` |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Animated GIF or WebP | Animated WebP                                | Animated WebP               | GIF                       |","table":"table-0"},"76":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","content":"PNG, GIF and lossless WebP sources stay lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given. Lossy output of a lossless source is AVIF, WebP or a palette PNG. A JPEG, lossy WebP or AVIF source always gives lossy output. An animated source is never AVIF. With an explicit format that can't hold the image (JPEG for an image with transparency, or any format other than WebP and GIF for an animation), transparency is flattened onto white and only the first frame is kept. Sources are detected from the content, not the extension. Other content is a `415` and an unreadable or corrupt file is a `422`."},"77":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","content":"Every successful response has `Vary: Accept`, also when it ends up in the source format."},"78":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#restricting-formats","content":"`CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS=webp` never negotiates AVIF, which avoids its encode cost. `CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS=none` disables all upgrades, so `auto` always gives the fallback format. `CHOP_AVIF=false` is a shorthand that removes `avif` from the list, also when `autoFormats` lists it. An explicit `format=avif` still works with either."},"79":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#restricting-formats","content":"`CHOP_ALLOWED_INPUT_FORMATS=jpeg,png,webp` is for a site that only serves those. The format is detected from the content of the file, never the extension, and `jpg` is accepted as an alias of `jpeg`. A source in another format is a `415` with the message of any unsupported file, which doesn't tell which formats are allowed. It's rejected after the header is read and before any pixel is decoded or processed."},"80":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"`quality` is raised to 20 when it's lower, for lossy encoders. `quality=100` on WebP is lossless WebP."},"81":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"Without `quality` the defaults are JPEG 82, WebP 80 and AVIF 55 (configurable). A palette PNG uses `quality` or 80. PNG output of a lossless source is lossless with maximum compression."},"82":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"A JPEG source isn't re-encoded with a higher quality than it has: the quality of the source is estimated from its luminance quantization table, and the default is lowered to it when it's lower."},"83":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"When a request changes nothing about the pixels (no `crop`, size or `lb`, and no orientation to apply), the output format equals the source format and the source has no metadata that `strip` would remove, the original bytes are sent if the re-encoded image isn't smaller. With `strip=none` an untouched request in the source format sends the original bytes without re-encoding."},"84":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"Pixel values are never converted to another color space because of `strip`: the ICC profile is kept or dropped, and the pixels stay as they are. CMYK sources are always converted to sRGB."},"85":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"Responses have `X-Bytes-Saved` when the output is smaller than the original."},"86":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"An explicit `quality` or `lossy=1` turns off the `strip=none` shortcut that sends the original bytes, because the client asked for a re-encoding. The \"never larger\" check still applies."},"87":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The source quality cap of a JPEG applies when `quality` is absent. An explicit `quality` is used as given (with the floor of 20)."},"88":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"Transparency means that the source has an alpha channel, even if every pixel is opaque."},"89":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"An explicit `format=png` is lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given, also for a JPEG source. An explicit `format=avif` or `format=jpeg` is always lossy."},"90":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"`contrast`, `brightness` and `filter` arguments are not parsed at all, so a malformed value of one of them is not an error."},"91":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"Repeated arguments use the first value. Crop numbers are non-negative and `zoom` may have up to three decimals."},"92":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"An empty segment in the path (`//` or a trailing slash) is a `400`."},"93":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"With `strip=none`, EXIF, XMP, IPTC and the profile are kept when the encoder can write them. CMYK sources only keep EXIF and XMP."},"94":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The `Accept` entries that have an invalid `q` are ignored. A listed type counts as accepted only if every entry of it has `q` above 0."},"95":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The encoders use the sharp defaults, except for progressive JPEG, WebP `effort` 4 and PNG `compressionLevel` 9."},"96":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"`maxConcurrency` defaults to the number of CPUs and `CHOP_PORT`, `CHOP_HOST` and `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG` are CLI-only variables."},"97":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"A first path segment of `http:` or `https:` always starts a URL source, so a directory with that name can't be addressed by a plain path, and with an empty allow-list it is a `404`."},"98":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The credentials of `CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH` are never sent to a URL source, not even to the host of the configured origin. A URL source of that host is fetched like any other, with the address checks."},"99":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"`*` allows every host on the default ports, and a custom port needs its own entry. An allow-list entry is a name or an IPv4 address and not an IPv6 literal, so only `*` allows an IPv6 literal, and the address checks still apply to it."},"100":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-33","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"An empty segment inside a URL source (`//` in its path) is sent to the origin as it is, while it's a `400` in a plain path."},"101":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-34","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The `Accept` header of the client is not forwarded to the origin, so the origin can't vary its answer, and the bytes of an original don't depend on who asked."},"102":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html-35","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"A `HEAD` request downloads and processes the original like a `GET`, since it has the same headers, including `Content-Length`, which depend on the output bytes. Don't forward `HEAD` requests for remote originals or URL sources from a proxy unless you need them, since each one costs a download and a conversion."},"103":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","type":"page","content":"chop","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html"},"104":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","content":"An HTTP image server for responsive images, with AVIF and WebP chosen from the Accept header."},"105":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#install","content":"Install"},"106":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#start-the-server","content":"Start the server"},"107":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Guides"},"108":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","content":"`@wpelevator/chop` is an HTTP image server for responsive images. It serves resized, converted and optimized copies of originals from a local data directory, from an HTTP(S) origin or from an S3 bucket, and chooses AVIF, WebP or the original format from the `Accept` header of each request. It's built on sharp, which is its only runtime dependency, and works as a command line server or as a library with a request handler that doesn't depend on an HTTP framework."},"109":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","content":"It's read-only: it never writes to the data directory or any other directory. With a data directory, which is the default, it makes no network requests. Remote originals are opt-in, are fetched with strict safeguards, and only from the configured origin or from hosts that you list. Authentication, URL signing and per-client rate limits are left to a CDN or a reverse proxy. The behavior is summarized in the reference."},"110":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#install","content":"Requires Node.js 22.12 or later. There is also a container image, `ghcr.io/wpelevator/chop`, described in the chop Docker README."},"111":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#start-the-server","content":"Then request `http://localhost:8080/2026/05/photo.jpg?w=300` to get `<data>/2026/05/photo.jpg` at 300 pixels wide, as AVIF or WebP when the `Accept` header of the client lists them. The CLI page lists the options and exit codes."},"112":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"CLI"},"113":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Requests and query arguments"},"114":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"URL schemes"},"115":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Sources: data directory, HTTP origin and URL sources"},"116":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"S3 and S3-compatible storage"},"117":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Securing remote origins"},"118":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Formats and quality"},"119":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Responses and errors"},"120":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Caching with nginx and a CDN"},"121":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Configuration"},"122":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Library API"},"123":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Development"},"124":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Reference"},"125":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","type":"page","content":"Library API","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html"},"126":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"The request handler doesn't depend on an HTTP framework, so it can run in a `node:http` server, a serverless function or a test. Install the package as described in the overview."},"127":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                       | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createHandler( settings? )` | Returns `( request ) => Promise< Response >`. The request is `{ method, url, headers }`, where `url` is the path and query string and `headers` is a plain object with lower-case names. The response is `{ status, headers, body }` with a `Buffer` body. It doesn't depend on `node:http`, never throws for a request (errors become responses) and takes optional callbacks, because the library never logs: `onError( error )` for unexpected errors, `onWarning( message )` for each risky setting (like `allowedHosts: [ '*' ]`) when the handler is created, and `onOriginError( error )` for a refused or failed origin, where `error.detail` says why and has no credentials. Give it the same settings that you give `createConfig()`: a settings object that `createConfig()` returned has a `dataDir`, which counts as set. |","table":"table-0"},"128":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                                                     | Description                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createConfig( overrides? )`, `configWarnings( settings )` | Settings with defaults, checked, and the list of warnings for the risky settings in them. Throws a `ChopError` with `ERR_INVALID_SETTING` for a value that can't be used. |","table":"table-0"},"129":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                 | Description                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `configFromEnv( env )` | The settings that the `CHOP_*` variables in an environment object set. It doesn't read `process`. |","table":"table-0"},"130":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                       | Description                                       |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parseQuery( searchParams )` | Parses a `URLSearchParams` into typed operations. |","table":"table-0"},"131":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                                                    | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `queryScheme`, `cloudflareScheme`, `SCHEMES`, `UrlScheme` | The built-in URL schemes, the registry of them by name, and the type of a scheme: `{ name, parse( url, options ) }`, where `parse` returns `{ segments, ops }`, with `url` set instead of `segments` for a URL source, or `null` for a URL that it doesn't recognize. `options.urlSources` tells whether URL sources are enabled. |","table":"table-0"},"132":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                                                                            | Description                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createOrigin( settings )`, `createLocalOrigin()`, `createHttpOrigin()`, `Origin` | The sources of originals: an `Origin` has `open( reference )`, which finds an original and returns its size and a `read()` for its bytes. The HTTP origin does the downloads and their checks. |","table":"table-0"},"133":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                                                                                        | Description                                                                          |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `isBlockedAddress( address )`, `createBlockList()`, `parseAllowedHosts()`, `parseSourceUrl()` | The building blocks of the safeguards, for code that wants to apply the same checks. |","table":"table-0"},"134":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                      | Description                                                                                        |\n| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createServer( settings? )` | A `node:http` server around the handler, with an `onResponse( summary )` callback for access logs. |","table":"table-0"},"135":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export            | Description                                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `run( args, io )` | The command, which returns an exit code. `io` has `stdout`, `stderr`, `env`, `cwd` and `signals`, all replaceable in tests. |","table":"table-0"},"136":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Export                                                                       | Description                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ChopError`, `isChopError( value )`, `CHOP_ERROR_CODES`, `CHOP_ERROR_STATUS` | Errors with a `code`. `isChopError` checks the code instead of `instanceof`. |","table":"table-0"},"137":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code            | HTTP status |\n| --------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_INVALID_REQUEST` | 400         |","table":"table-1"},"138":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code      | HTTP status |\n| --------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_NOT_FOUND` | 404         |","table":"table-1"},"139":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code               | HTTP status |\n| ------------------------ | ----------- |\n| `ERR_METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED` | 405         |","table":"table-1"},"140":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code            | HTTP status |\n| --------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_INPUT_TOO_LARGE` | 413         |","table":"table-1"},"141":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code             | HTTP status |\n| ---------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE` | 415         |","table":"table-1"},"142":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code             | HTTP status |\n| ---------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_UNREADABLE_IMAGE` | 422         |","table":"table-1"},"143":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code     | HTTP status |\n| -------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_UPSTREAM` | 502         |","table":"table-1"},"144":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code             | HTTP status |\n| ---------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT` | 504         |","table":"table-1"},"145":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code | HTTP status |\n| ---------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_BUSY` | 503         |","table":"table-1"},"146":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code            | HTTP status                                       |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ERR_INVALID_SETTING` | 500 (reported by the CLI at startup, exit code 2) |","table":"table-1"},"147":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/library.html","content":"| Error code     | HTTP status |\n| -------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_INTERNAL` | 500         |","table":"table-1"},"148":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"page","content":"Reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html"},"149":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#requests","content":"Requests"},"150":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"Sources"},"151":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"S3 origin"},"152":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Query scheme arguments"},"153":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"URL schemes"},"154":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"`cloudflare`"},"155":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"Output format"},"156":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"Quality and size"},"157":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#responses","content":"Responses"},"158":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#caching","content":"Caching"},"159":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#limits","content":"Limits"},"160":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"Settings"},"161":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Interfaces"},"162":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","content":"How chop behaves, in short. The guides describe each area in more detail: requests, sources, URL schemes, formats and quality, responses and configuration. The IDs in parentheses, like `R-OP-8`, are what the tests refer to in their names. chop is MIT licensed and was implemented from a written behavior specification and the repository conventions, without reference to the source code of any other image server."},"163":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#requests","content":"`GET` and `HEAD` are answered, other methods get `405` with `Allow: GET, HEAD` (R-REQ-1)."},"164":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#requests","content":"The path selects the original under the data directory or the configured origin, and a URL scheme selects the operations (R-REQ-2, S-1). Unknown arguments are ignored, so cache busters like `ver=3` are harmless."},"165":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#requests","content":"`/healthz` answers `200 ok` without touching the data directory or the origin (R-REQ-3)."},"166":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#requests","content":"The same URL and `Accept` header give the same bytes (R-REQ-4)."},"167":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#requests","content":"Path segments are percent-decoded once. `.`, `..`, empty segments and segments with `/`, `\\` or a NUL byte are a `400`, and a broken escape is a `400` (R-PATH-1). This is for plain paths: in a URL source the embedded URL path is sent to the origin as written, so `//` in it is allowed, but dot segments and broken escapes are still a `400` (R-SRC-14)."},"168":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#requests","content":"The real path, with symbolic links resolved, must be inside the real data directory. A missing file, a directory and an escape are all the same `404` (R-PATH-2)."},"169":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#requests","content":"A file over `maxInputBytes` is a `413`, checked before the read and again after it (R-PATH-3). These checks are for the local data directory."},"170":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"Where the original comes from. The data directory is the default and its behavior is the one above."},"171":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"Plain paths go to the configured origin (`origin`, `CHOP_ORIGIN`) when there is one, and to the data directory when there isn't. A URL source goes to the HTTP fetcher with the allow-list (R-SRC-1)."},"172":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"The URL of a plain path is the origin base URL, its path without a trailing slash and the path segments, each percent-encoded again, so a segment can't change the host, the port, the query string or the path of the base (R-SRC-2)."},"173":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"The origin is `https://`, or `http://` with `originAllowHttp`, without user information, a query string or a fragment, and not an IP literal in a blocked range unless `originAllowPrivate` is set. The same scheme rule applies to URL sources, and a bad origin is an invalid setting at startup (R-SRC-3)."},"174":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"Before connecting, the address literal in the URL is checked, or the name is resolved, every address is checked and the socket only gets the addresses that were checked. If any address is blocked nothing is connected, and the connection is made to one of the addresses that were checked and not to a second DNS answer, so DNS rebinding can't swap the address. Blocked addresses are loopback, unspecified, private, link-local (including `169.254.169.254`), carrier-grade NAT, documentation, multicast and reserved ranges for IPv4 and IPv6, with IPv4-mapped and NAT64 addresses checked as the IPv4 address that they contain, 6to4 and Teredo blocked, and anything that can't be parsed blocked (R-SRC-4)."},"175":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"Redirects are not followed, and a `3xx` is a `502` (R-SRC-5)."},"176":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"The request is a `GET` with `Accept: image/*`, `Accept-Encoding: identity` and `User-Agent: chop`, and without any header of the client. `originAuth` is sent as `Authorization` to the configured origin only. A response with a `Content-Encoding` is a `502` (R-SRC-6)."},"177":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"The body is limited to `maxInputBytes` while it is read, whether or not there is a `Content-Length`, and a `Content-Length` over the limit is a `413` before the body is read (R-SRC-7)."},"178":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"Connecting must finish within `originConnectTimeout` and the whole download within `originTimeout`, or the answer is a `504`. Upstream failures, a `5xx` or other unexpected status, a redirect and a body that ends early are a `502`, and the body of a response that is not a `200` is dropped without being read. A name that can't be resolved is a `502` for the configured origin, so the operator sees a broken origin, and a plain `404` for a URL source, so that a client can't tell which names exist (R-SRC-8)."},"179":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"An upstream `404` or `410`, an upstream `401`, `403` or `407`, a URL source that is not allowed and a blocked destination are all the same plain `404`. The reason is only given to the `onOriginError` callback, which the command writes to the standard error, and it is made of the host, a status code or an error code and never an error message (R-SRC-9)."},"180":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"The type is found from the content, and the `Content-Type` of the origin is not used (R-SRC-10)."},"181":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"The headers of the origin, like `Cache-Control` and `ETag`, don't change the response, and the original is not cached (R-SRC-11)."},"182":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-33","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"A `HEAD` request downloads and processes the original like a `GET`, since it must have the same headers, including `Content-Length` (R-REQ-1), so a proxy should not forward `HEAD` requests for remote originals unless it needs them (R-SRC-12)."},"183":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-34","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"At most `originConcurrency` downloads run at once and `originQueue` more wait, outside of the processing slots, and a full queue is a `503` with `Retry-After: 1` (R-SRC-12)."},"184":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-35","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"A URL source is a URL after `/` in the `query` scheme or after the options in the `cloudflare` scheme, written `https://host/path`, `https:/host/path` or `https%3A//host/path`. It is a `404` unless `allowedHosts` is not empty and names its host, and the match is on the lower case host without a trailing dot, and the port (R-SRC-13)."},"185":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-36","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"A URL source with user information, a fragment, or a query string of its own (a `400` in the `cloudflare` scheme, and not possible in the `query` scheme where the query is chop's arguments) is a `400`, and dot segments are a `400` as for any path. A port other than the default of the scheme must be in the entry (R-SRC-14)."},"186":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-37","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"`allowedHosts` entries are `host`, `*.example.com` (subdomains on a dot boundary, not the apex), either with `:port`, or `*` for every host on the default ports. `*` can't be mixed with other entries, and it is a warning at startup. Even with `*` everything else of this section applies, and `originAllowPrivate` never applies to a URL source (R-SRC-15)."},"187":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-38","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#sources","content":"A data directory that is set explicitly and an origin together are an invalid setting (R-SRC-16)."},"188":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-39","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`origin` set to `s3://bucket[/prefix]` reads the originals from an S3 bucket or an S3-compatible service. It is the HTTP origin of the section above for requests of the bucket, with signed requests, and every rule of that section applies unless it is changed here."},"189":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-40","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`origin` is parsed into a bucket and a prefix: the bucket has 3 to 63 lower case letters, digits, dots and hyphens and isn't an IP address, and the prefix can't have empty, `.` or `..` segments, a query string or a fragment. `http://` and `https://` origins are unchanged, and a data directory that is set explicitly together with an `s3://` origin is an invalid setting (R-S3-1)."},"190":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-41","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The region is `s3Region` (`CHOP_S3_REGION`, then `AWS_REGION`). On AWS, which is without `s3Endpoint`, it is required and a missing one is an invalid setting at startup. With an endpoint it defaults to `us-east-1`, and `auto` is allowed for R2 (R-S3-2)."},"191":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-42","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"On AWS the bucket is in the host, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`, unless `s3PathStyle` is true or the bucket name has dots, which use `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`. A custom endpoint is `endpoint/bucket/key` unless `s3PathStyle` is false, which uses `bucket.endpoint-host`. The endpoint is checked like the origin: https, or http with `originAllowHttp`, no user information, query string or fragment, and no blocked address without `originAllowPrivate` (R-S3-3)."},"192":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-43","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"With `s3AccessKeyId` and `s3SecretAccessKey` every request to the bucket is signed with AWS Signature Version 4 with a fresh date, and the signed host is the `Host` header that is sent, with its port. A session token is sent and signed as `x-amz-security-token`. Without a key and a secret requests are unsigned and there is a warning at startup, and a key without a secret, a secret without a key and a token alone are invalid settings (R-S3-4)."},"193":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-44","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The key is the prefix and the validated segments of the path, and each segment is percent-encoded once, keeping only `A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~`, and sent exactly as it is signed. The path is not normalized (R-S3-5)."},"194":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-45","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The errors are those of the HTTP origin: `404` and `403` from the bucket are a plain `404`, a `5xx`, a network or TLS error and a redirect are a `502`, a timeout is a `504`, and an object over `maxInputBytes` is a `413` (R-S3-6)."},"195":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-46","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"For the operator only, the first 2048 bytes of the body of an error from the bucket are read (for at most two seconds), and the `<Code>` of the XML, like `SignatureDoesNotMatch`, `AccessDenied`, `RequestTimeTooSkewed`, `ExpiredToken` or `InvalidAccessKeyId`, is given to `onOriginError` in the detail of the error. `NoSuchKey` is not reported, since it is an ordinary miss. A `301` or `307` is a `502` with the detail `bucket is in another region (check CHOP_S3_REGION)` and isn't followed. The body of an error of any other origin is still dropped without being read (R-S3-7)."},"196":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-47","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"Requests for URL sources are never signed and never get the credentials, and the URL sources of `allowedHosts` keep working (R-S3-8)."},"197":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-48","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The secret key and the session token are only read from the environment by the command, and are not in any error message, warning or log line (R-S3-9)."},"198":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-49","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`, `CHOP_S3_REGION`, `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE`, `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` and `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN` are read, with `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` and `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` as the fallbacks, and `--origin s3://bucket` works. Credentials are read once at startup and aren't refreshed (R-S3-10)."},"199":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-50","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"This is the default scheme, named `query`. All arguments are optional, and a malformed value of a known argument is a `400` that names it."},"200":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-51","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `w`, `h` | Width or height in pixels. With one, scale to it. With both, fit inside the box without cropping or padding (R-OP-2). |","table":"table-0"},"201":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-52","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                           |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit=w,h` | The same as `w` and `h` together, and it wins over them (R-OP-3). |","table":"table-0"},"202":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-53","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument     | Meaning                                                                    |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resize=w,h` | Cover the box and crop to exactly `w` by `h`. It wins over `fit` (R-OP-4). |","table":"table-0"},"203":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-54","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                                             |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | Where `resize` crops: `center` (default), `north`, `south`, `east`, `west` or `attention` (R-OP-5). |","table":"table-0"},"204":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-55","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument       | Meaning                                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `crop=x,y,w,h` | A region of the oriented original, before scaling. Numbers are percentages, or pixels with a `px` suffix. The region is clipped to the image (R-OP-6). |","table":"table-0"},"205":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-56","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument         | Meaning                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lb=w,h[,color]` | Fit inside the box and pad to exactly `w` by `h`. `color` is 3 or 6 hex digits, default `ffffff` (R-OP-7). |","table":"table-0"},"206":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-57","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `zoom`   | Device pixel ratio from 1 to 10, which multiplies the sizes (R-OP-9). |","table":"table-0"},"207":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-58","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument    | Meaning                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `upscale=1` | Allow enlarging, up to `maxUpscaleDimension` (R-OP-8). |","table":"table-0"},"208":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-59","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                   |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `quality` | 1 to 100, with values below 20 raised to 20 for lossy encoders (R-QLT-1). |","table":"table-0"},"209":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-60","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                             |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `auto` (default), `jpeg`, `png`, `webp`, `avif` or `gif` (R-FMT-2). |","table":"table-0"},"210":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-61","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                            |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lossy=1` | Allow lossy output for lossless sources (R-QLT-5). |","table":"table-0"},"211":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-62","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `strip`  | `metadata` (default, keeps the ICC profile), `all` or `none` (R-QLT-6). |","table":"table-0"},"212":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-63","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Operations run in a fixed order, whatever the order in the URL: orientation, `crop`, size, `lb`, then encoding. Sizes always refer to the displayed (oriented) image (R-OP-1)."},"213":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-64","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Without `upscale=1` nothing is enlarged: sizes clamp to the original, `resize` crops at the largest size with the requested aspect ratio, and `lb` pads without enlarging (R-OP-8). The output can't exceed `maxOutputDimension` (R-OP-12)."},"214":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-65","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Animated sources keep all frames for `crop` and sizes. `lb` and `gravity=attention` are ignored for them (R-OP-13). Image adjustments (R-OP-10) and filters (R-OP-11) aren't supported, and their arguments are ignored."},"215":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-66","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme turns a URL into the path of the original and the operations. All the schemes produce the same operations, so every scheme gets the same negotiation, limits and path safety."},"216":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-67","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Schemes are tried in the configured order, and the first one that recognizes the URL wins. The default is `query` only (S-1). The `query` scheme recognizes every URL, so it has to be listed last when it's enabled with others. The `cloudflare` scheme only recognizes URLs that start with `/cdn-cgi/image/`."},"217":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-68","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme's path segments go through the same checks as any other path, so no scheme can read outside the data directory (S-2)."},"218":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-69","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A URL that no enabled scheme recognizes is a `404` (S-3)."},"219":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-70","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme ignores the options that chop doesn't support, and a malformed value of one that it supports is a `400` (S-4)."},"220":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-71","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Different schemes that give the same operations give the same bytes and `ETag` (S-5)."},"221":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-72","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"The `/cdn-cgi/image/<options>/<path>` form of Cloudflare Image Resizing, with comma separated `name=value` options."},"222":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-73","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option            | Maps to         |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `width`, `height` | `w`, `h` (S-6). |","table":"table-1"},"223":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-74","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit`  | `scale-down` (default) is `w`/`h` that never enlarges, `contain` is the same with `upscale`, `cover` is `resize` with `upscale`, `crop` is `resize`, and `pad` is `lb` with `upscale` (S-7). |","table":"table-1"},"224":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-75","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | `left`, `right`, `top`, `bottom` are `west`, `east`, `north`, `south`, and `auto` and `face` are `attention`. Coordinates like `0.5x0.3` are ignored (S-8). |","table":"table-1"},"225":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-76","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to          |\n| --------- | ---------------- |\n| `quality` | `quality` (S-9). |","table":"table-1"},"226":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-77","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option   | Maps to                                                                                                |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `format` | `auto`, `avif`, `webp`, `jpeg`, `png`, `gif`, and `baseline-jpeg` as `jpeg`. `json` is a `400` (S-10). |","table":"table-1"},"227":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-78","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to        |\n| ------ | -------------- |\n| `dpr`  | `zoom` (S-11). |","table":"table-1"},"228":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-79","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option     | Maps to                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `keep` is `strip=none`, `copyright` is `strip=metadata`, `none` is `strip=all` (S-12). |","table":"table-1"},"229":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-80","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option       | Maps to                                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `background` | The `lb` color for `fit=pad`, as hex digits (S-13). |","table":"table-1"},"230":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-81","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"Other Cloudflare options, like `trim`, `rotate`, `blur`, `sharpen` and `onerror`, are ignored. A source that starts with `http://` or `https://` is a URL source (see Sources) and is a `404` without `allowedHosts`."},"231":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-82","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"`Accept` is parsed per RFC 9110. Only a listed `image/avif` or `image/webp` makes those formats acceptable, so `image/*` and `*/*` don't (R-FMT-1)."},"232":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-83","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"An explicit `format` is used even when `Accept` doesn't list it. Transparency is flattened onto white for formats that can't hold it (R-FMT-2)."},"233":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-84","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"With `auto`, a still image is the negotiated format from `autoFormats` (R-FMT-10): AVIF if the output is lossy, or WebP if the output is within its size limit. Without an accepted candidate it is the fallback format: GIF for GIF sources, PNG for lossless or transparent output, and JPEG otherwise (R-FMT-3)."},"234":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-85","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"An animated source becomes an animated WebP if accepted and in `autoFormats`, otherwise a GIF, and never AVIF (R-FMT-4)."},"235":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-86","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"PNG, GIF and lossless WebP sources stay lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given (R-FMT-5). JPEG, lossy WebP and AVIF sources produce lossy output (R-FMT-6)."},"236":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-87","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"Every response that depends on `Accept` has `Vary: Accept` (R-FMT-7)."},"237":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-88","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP and AVIF are read, detected from the content. Other content is a `415`, and unreadable or corrupt files are a `422` (R-FMT-8)."},"238":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-89","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"A source whose detected format isn't in `allowedInputFormats` is a `415` with the same message as other unsupported content, which doesn't tell which formats are allowed. The check follows the header detection and comes before any pixel decoding or processing (R-FMT-9)."},"239":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-90","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#output-format","content":"`autoFormats` lists the formats (`avif`, `webp`) that `auto` can negotiate, in order of preference. Among the listed formats that `Accept` lists with `q` above 0 (and that pass the checks of R-FMT-3), the one with the highest `q` is used, and the earlier entry of `autoFormats` wins a tie. An empty list disables the upgrades. An explicit `format` is not restricted by `autoFormats`, and `avif: false` removes AVIF from the list (R-FMT-10)."},"240":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-91","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"The defaults are JPEG 82, WebP 80 and AVIF 55, lowered to the estimated quality of a JPEG source, so that a recompressed JPEG never gets a higher quality than it has. The estimate compares the file's luminance quantization table with the standard table scaled for each quality. An explicit `quality` is used as given (R-QLT-2, R-QLT-3)."},"241":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-92","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"A request that changes nothing about the pixels and keeps the source format sends the original bytes when the re-encoded image isn't smaller, and with `strip=none` it always sends them (R-QLT-4)."},"242":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-93","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#responses","content":"`200` has the output `Content-Type`, `Content-Length`, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=<maxAge>`, `Vary: Accept`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a strong SHA-256 `ETag` (R-RES-1). `X-Bytes-Saved` appears when the output is smaller than the original (R-RES-3)."},"243":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-94","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#responses","content":"`If-None-Match` that matches, including weak comparison, lists and `*`, gets a `304` without a body (R-RES-2)."},"244":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-95","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#responses","content":"Errors are plain text with `Cache-Control: no-store` and no file system paths: `400` invalid request, `404` not found, `405` method, `413` original too large, `415` unsupported type, `422` unreadable image, `500` unexpected, `502` the origin failed, `503` busy and `504` the origin was too slow (R-RES-4)."},"245":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-96","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#caching","content":"Responses depend on `Accept` and the URL only, so a cache can key on the URL and a bucket of `Accept`: `image/avif`, `image/webp` or neither. Send the bucket as `Accept` upstream so that the body matches the key. The caching guide has an nginx recipe."},"246":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-97","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#limits","content":"At most `maxConcurrency` images are processed at once and `maxQueue` more wait in order. A request that finds the queue full gets `503` with `Retry-After: 1`, and a failing request frees its slot (R-LIM-1, R-LIM-2)."},"247":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-98","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#limits","content":"Decoding is limited by `maxInputPixels` (R-LIM-3)."},"248":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-99","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#limits","content":"`allowedWidths` optionally restricts the output widths to a list (R-LIM-4)."},"249":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-100","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#limits","content":"chop never writes to disk, and makes no network requests unless an origin or `allowedHosts` is configured, and then only to those hosts (R-LIM-5)."},"250":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-101","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `dataDir` | `CHOP_DATA_DIR`      | `/data` |","table":"table-2"},"251":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-102","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable             | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `schemes` | `CHOP_SCHEMES` (comma separated) | `query` |","table":"table-2"},"252":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-103","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default    |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxAge` | `CHOP_MAX_AGE`       | `31536000` |","table":"table-2"},"253":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-104","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable   | Default        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | -------------- |\n| `maxConcurrency` | `CHOP_MAX_CONCURRENCY` | number of CPUs |","table":"table-2"},"254":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-105","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable | Default |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxQueue` | `CHOP_MAX_QUEUE`     | `64`    |","table":"table-2"},"255":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-106","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable   | Default    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxInputBytes` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_BYTES` | `52428800` |","table":"table-2"},"256":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-107","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable    | Default     |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | ----------- |\n| `maxInputPixels` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_PIXELS` | `120000000` |","table":"table-2"},"257":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-108","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxOutputDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_OUTPUT_DIMENSION` | `8192`  |","table":"table-2"},"258":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-109","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable         | Default |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxUpscaleDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_UPSCALE_DIMENSION` | `4096`  |","table":"table-2"},"259":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-110","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                     | Environment variable                                          | Default          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `jpegQuality`, `webpQuality`, `avifQuality` | `CHOP_JPEG_QUALITY`, `CHOP_WEBP_QUALITY`, `CHOP_AVIF_QUALITY` | `82`, `80`, `55` |","table":"table-2"},"260":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-111","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avif`  | `CHOP_AVIF`          | `true`  |","table":"table-2"},"261":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-112","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avifEffort` | `CHOP_AVIF_EFFORT`   | `4`     |","table":"table-2"},"262":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-113","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                    | Default |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `allowedWidths` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_WIDTHS` (comma separated) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"263":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-114","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable                                        | Default |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `origin` | `CHOP_ORIGIN` (an `https://` URL or `s3://bucket[/prefix]`) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"264":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-115","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                 | Environment variable                                  | Default          |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `originAllowHttp`, `originAllowPrivate` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` | `false`, `false` |","table":"table-2"},"265":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-116","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default     |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ----------- |\n| `s3Endpoint` | `CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`   | unset (AWS) |","table":"table-2"},"266":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-117","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable           | Default                                               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Region` | `CHOP_S3_REGION`, `AWS_REGION` | unset (required on AWS), `us-east-1` with an endpoint |","table":"table-2"},"267":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-118","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default                                 |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `s3PathStyle` | `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE` | `true` with an endpoint, `false` on AWS |","table":"table-2"},"268":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-119","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                                | Environment variable                                                                                      | Default |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `s3AccessKeyId`, `s3SecretAccessKey`, `s3SessionToken` | `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN`, with the `AWS_*` fallbacks | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"269":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-120","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `originAuth` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH`   | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"270":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-121","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                 | Environment variable                                 | Default         |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `originConnectTimeout`, `originTimeout` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONNECT_TIMEOUT`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_TIMEOUT` | `3000`, `10000` |","table":"table-2"},"271":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-122","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                            | Environment variable                           | Default   |\n| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | --------- |\n| `originConcurrency`, `originQueue` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_QUEUE` | `4`, `32` |","table":"table-2"},"272":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-123","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting        | Environment variable                   | Default |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `allowedHosts` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (comma separated) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"273":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-124","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable                           | Default                  |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `allowedInputFormats` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_INPUT_FORMATS` (comma separated) | `jpeg,png,gif,webp,avif` |","table":"table-2"},"274":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-125","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable                             | Default     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ----------- |\n| `autoFormats` | `CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS` (comma separated, or `none`) | `avif,webp` |","table":"table-2"},"275":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-126","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createHandler( settings? )` returns `( request ) => Promise< Response >` with `{ method, url, headers }` in and `{ status, headers, body }` out. It never throws for a request, never uses `node:http` and reports unexpected errors to an optional `onError`, risky settings to `onWarning` and the failures of an origin to `onOriginError` (R-API-1)."},"276":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-127","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createConfig()`, `configFromEnv( env )`, `configWarnings()`, the `Origin` interface with `createOrigin()`, `createLocalOrigin()` and `createHttpOrigin()`, `createS3Origin()`, `isBlockedAddress()`, `parseQuery()`, `createServer()`, the URL schemes `queryScheme` and `cloudflareScheme` with their `SCHEMES` registry and the `UrlScheme` type (`{ name, parse( url, options ) }`, where `parse` returns `{ segments, ops }`, with `url` set for a URL source, or `null`), and the other types are exported too (R-API-2, S-1)."},"277":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-128","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Errors are `ChopError` with a `code` from `CHOP_ERROR_CODES`, checked with `isChopError()` (R-API-3)."},"278":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html-129","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/reference.html#interfaces","content":"The CLI is `chop [--data <dir> | --origin <url or s3://bucket>] [--port <n>] [--host <address>] [--scheme <name>] [--help]`, with flags overriding `CHOP_*` variables. A flag replaces the other source from the environment (`--origin` over `CHOP_DATA_DIR`, `--data` over `CHOP_ORIGIN`). Warnings about risky settings and the reasons for refused origin requests go to the standard error. Exit codes are `0`, `1` for a failure and `2` for invalid options. `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` stop it gracefully, and `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG=1` prints one JSON line per request (R-CLI-1 to R-CLI-4)."},"279":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","type":"page","content":"Requests","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html"},"280":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"Differences from Photon query arguments"},"281":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"The URL path selects the original, like `/2026/05/photo.jpg` for `<data>/2026/05/photo.jpg` or for `<origin>/2026/05/photo.jpg` when an origin is configured, and a URL scheme selects the operations. The default `query` scheme reads them from the query string. Unknown arguments are ignored, so cache-busting arguments like `ver=3` are harmless. A malformed value of a known argument is a `400` with a message that names the argument. `GET /healthz` answers `ok` without touching the data directory or the origin. Only `GET` and `HEAD` are allowed."},"282":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"Operations run in a fixed order, whatever the order in the URL: orientation, `crop`, size, `lb`, then encoding. The EXIF orientation is always applied to the pixels first, so every size and offset refers to the displayed image, and the output has no orientation tag."},"283":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument | Description                                                                                                  | Example                  |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------ |\n| `w`, `h` | Width and height in pixels. One keeps the aspect ratio, both fit inside the box without cropping or padding. | `?w=800`, `?w=800&h=600` |","table":"table-0"},"284":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument  | Description                                           | Example        |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `fit=w,h` | The same as `w` and `h` together, and wins over them. | `?fit=800,600` |","table":"table-0"},"285":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument     | Description                                                                                               | Example           |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `resize=w,h` | Cover `w` by `h` and crop the overflow, so the result is exactly that size. Wins over `fit`, `w` and `h`. | `?resize=400,400` |","table":"table-0"},"286":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument  | Description                                                                                          | Example                         |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | Where `resize` keeps the image: `center` (default), `north`, `south`, `east`, `west` or `attention`. | `?resize=400,400&gravity=north` |","table":"table-0"},"287":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument       | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Example                                          |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `crop=x,y,w,h` | A region of the oriented original, applied before scaling. Numbers are percentages of the width (`x`, `w`) or the height (`y`, `h`), with decimals allowed, or pixels with a `px` suffix. A region past the edge is clipped, and one with no area is a `400`. | `?crop=10,10,50,50`, `?crop=0px,0px,600px,400px` |","table":"table-0"},"288":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument         | Description                                                                                                                                                                       | Example                    |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `lb=w,h[,color]` | Letterbox: fit the image in the box, then pad it with `color` (3 or 6 hex digits, optional `#`, default `ffffff`) to exactly `w` by `h`, centered. Runs after the size operation. | `?w=300&lb=400,400,f5f5f5` |","table":"table-0"},"289":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument    | Description                                                    | Example             |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `upscale=1` | Allow enlarging, up to `maxUpscaleDimension` on the long side. | `?w=1200&upscale=1` |","table":"table-0"},"290":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument | Description                                                                                                         | Example         |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `zoom=N` | Device pixel ratio from 1 to 10, which multiplies `w`, `h`, `fit`, `resize` and `lb` sizes before the limits apply. | `?w=300&zoom=2` |","table":"table-0"},"291":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument | Description                                               | Example        |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `format` | `auto` (default), `jpeg`, `png`, `webp`, `avif` or `gif`. | `?format=webp` |","table":"table-0"},"292":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument  | Description            | Example       |\n| --------- | ---------------------- | ------------- |\n| `quality` | Integer from 1 to 100. | `?quality=70` |","table":"table-0"},"293":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument  | Description                                                        | Example    |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------- |\n| `lossy=1` | Allow lossy output of a lossless source (PNG, GIF, lossless WebP). | `?lossy=1` |","table":"table-0"},"294":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"| Argument | Description                                                                                                                                         | Example      |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `strip`  | `metadata` (default) removes EXIF, XMP and IPTC and keeps the ICC profile, `all` removes everything, `none` keeps everything the encoder can write. | `?strip=all` |","table":"table-0"},"295":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"Nothing enlarges the image unless `upscale=1`. When a requested size is larger than the image, `w`, `h` and `fit` clamp to the original size, `resize` crops to the requested aspect ratio at the largest size that fits, and `lb` pads without enlarging the image inside. With `upscale=1` the long side of a result may be as large as `maxUpscaleDimension`, but never less than the long side of the image itself. The output may not exceed `maxOutputDimension` in either dimension, which is checked after clamping and is a `400` when a request asks for more. When `allowedWidths` is set, the width of the output must be in the list or the request is a `400`."},"296":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","content":"For an animated source (GIF or animated WebP), `crop`, `w`, `h`, `fit` and `resize` apply to every frame and keep all frames and their timing, while `lb` and `gravity=attention` are ignored."},"297":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"chop has its own small set of arguments, and it isn't a drop-in replacement for the Photon image service. These arguments are not supported, are not an error and are ignored like any unknown argument:"},"298":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"`brightness` and `contrast` (no image adjustments)."},"299":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"`filter`, with its `grayscale`, `sepia`, `negate`, `blur` and `sharpen` names (no image filters)."},"300":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"`colorize` and `smooth`, and `ulb` (a letterbox with a color that is also scaled), which the specification doesn't have."},"301":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"`webp` and `ssl`: the output format follows the `Accept` header, or `format`, and the server is not a proxy for other hosts."},"302":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"Originals are only read from the data directory, the configured origin and the hosts that you allow, and `strip` has the values `metadata`, `all` and `none`."},"303":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","type":"page","content":"Responses","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html"},"304":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"A success is `200` with the `Content-Type` of the output, `Content-Length`, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=<maxAge>`, `Vary: Accept`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a strong `ETag` that is a SHA-256 of the body. An `If-None-Match` that matches the `ETag` (weak comparison, lists and `*`) gets `304` with the same `ETag`, `Cache-Control` and `Vary` and no body. A `HEAD` response has the headers of the `GET` response, including `Content-Length`, and no body."},"305":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"Errors are plain text with a short message that doesn't reveal file system paths, `Cache-Control: no-store` and `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`."},"306":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                                                                                           |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `400`  | Invalid request: an unsafe path, a malformed argument, a size over `maxOutputDimension` or a width that isn't in `allowedWidths`. |","table":"table-0"},"307":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `404`  | Not found: a missing file, a directory, or a path that resolves outside the data directory, which all look the same. For a remote origin also an upstream `404`, `410`, `401`, `403` or `407`, a URL source that isn't allowed and a destination at a blocked address. |","table":"table-0"},"308":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                        |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `405`  | A method other than `GET` and `HEAD`, with `Allow: GET, HEAD`. |","table":"table-0"},"309":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                                         |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `413`  | The original is over `maxInputBytes`, which is checked before the file is read. |","table":"table-0"},"310":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                               |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `415`  | The file is not a JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP or AVIF image. |","table":"table-0"},"311":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                         |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `422`  | The image is corrupt, or has more than `maxInputPixels` pixels. |","table":"table-0"},"312":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `502`  | The origin failed: it couldn't be reached, it answered with a `5xx` or another unexpected status, it redirected, or it sent a compressed or incomplete body. |","table":"table-0"},"313":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                        |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `504`  | The origin was too slow to connect or to send the whole image. |","table":"table-0"},"314":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning              |\n| ------ | -------------------- |\n| `500`  | An unexpected error. |","table":"table-0"},"315":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                             |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `503`  | The queue of images or of downloads is full, with `Retry-After: 1`. |","table":"table-0"},"316":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/responses.html","content":"The error statuses `502` and `504` also have `Cache-Control: no-store`, as every error does. Each path segment is percent-decoded once, and a segment that is `.` or `..`, is empty, or contains `/`, `\\` or a NUL byte after decoding is a `400`. The real path of the file, with symbolic links resolved, must be inside the real path of the data directory."},"317":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","type":"page","content":"S3 and S3-compatible storage","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html"},"318":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"`CHOP_ORIGIN=s3://bucket` or `CHOP_ORIGIN=s3://bucket/prefix` reads the originals from a bucket, and `--origin s3://bucket` works too. The path of a request is appended to the prefix to make the key, so with `s3://my-bucket/uploads` the request `/2026/05/photo.jpg` reads the key `uploads/2026/05/photo.jpg`. Each segment is percent-encoded once, which is what S3 signs, so spaces, `+`, `!`, `*`, `'`, `(`, `)` and non-ASCII names work. The bucket name follows the S3 rules (3 to 63 lower case letters, digits, dots and hyphens), and a prefix can't have empty, `.` or `..` segments. An `s3://` origin can't be combined with an explicit `CHOP_DATA_DIR` or `--data`."},"319":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"chop signs every request to the bucket with AWS Signature Version 4, using only `node:crypto`. Everything else is the same as for an HTTP origin: the pinned DNS lookup and address checks, no redirects, the size cap while reading, the timeouts, and the fetch limit and queue. `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP` and `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` apply to the endpoint, and URL sources from `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` still work next to an S3 origin. They are fetched without a signature, and the credentials are never sent to them."},"320":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Endpoint` | `CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`   | Base URL of an S3-compatible service, like `http://seaweedfs:8333`. Unset means AWS. It is checked like an origin: `https://`, or `http://` with `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP`, without user information, a query string or a fragment, and a loopback, private or link-local address needs `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE`. |","table":"table-0"},"321":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable                | Description                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Region` | `CHOP_S3_REGION`, then `AWS_REGION` | Region that requests are signed for. Required for AWS, and an invalid setting at startup without it. With an endpoint it defaults to `us-east-1`, and Cloudflare R2 uses `auto`. |","table":"table-0"},"322":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Description                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3PathStyle` | `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE` | `true` puts the bucket in the path (`https://host/bucket/key`), `false` in the host (`https://bucket.host/key`). Defaults to `true` with an endpoint and `false` for AWS. |","table":"table-0"},"323":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                              | Description |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `s3AccessKeyId` | `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, then `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | Access key. |","table":"table-0"},"324":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"| Setting             | Environment variable                                      | Description                                                                           |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3SecretAccessKey` | `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, then `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | Secret of the access key. Environment only, there is no flag, and it is never logged. |","table":"table-0"},"325":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable                              | Description                                                                                                          |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3SessionToken` | `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN`, then `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` | Token of temporary credentials, sent and signed as `x-amz-security-token`. Environment only, and it is never logged. |","table":"table-0"},"326":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"On AWS the default is the virtual-hosted form, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`. A bucket name with dots falls back to the path-style form, `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`, because the wildcard certificate of AWS doesn't cover dotted names, and `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE=true` forces it. With an endpoint the default is `endpoint/bucket/key`, and `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE=false` uses `bucket.endpoint-host` instead, which needs a host name that can have subdomains and not an IP address."},"327":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"Credentials need both a key and a secret. With only one of them, or with a session token alone, chop doesn't start (an invalid setting, which names the settings and not their values). With neither, requests are sent unsigned, which only works for a bucket with public read access, and chop prints a warning on startup that there are no credentials."},"328":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"AWS or Lambda, with the credentials of the execution role that Lambda puts in the environment:"},"329":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"SeaweedFS with its S3 gateway on the private network, over plain http:"},"330":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"Cloudflare R2:"},"331":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"A public bucket, without credentials (and with the warning):"},"332":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"SeaweedFS can also serve a bucket through its filer over plain HTTP, which needs no signature and no S3 settings. That is the HTTP origin with the filer URL, `CHOP_ORIGIN=http://seaweedfs:8888/buckets/<bucket>`, together with `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP=1` and `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE=1`. Use it when the filer isn't exposed to anyone else, and the S3 origin when you want access keys."},"333":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"Errors are answered like those of an HTTP origin. A missing key (`NoSuchKey`), a `403` and a `404` are a plain `404` for the client, a `5xx`, a network or TLS error and a redirect are a `502`, a timeout is a `504` and an object over `maxInputBytes` is a `413`. S3 explains an error in an XML body, and because a signature problem, a wrong key and a missing permission all look like a missing image to the client, chop reads at most the first 2048 bytes of the body of an error (and waits at most two seconds for them) and writes the `<Code>` to the standard error, like `origin ERR_NOT_FOUND: s3.example.com answered 403 SignatureDoesNotMatch`. Look there first when images are missing. Other codes to know are `AccessDenied`, `InvalidAccessKeyId`, `ExpiredToken`, `RequestTimeTooSkewed`, `NoSuchBucket` and `AuthorizationHeaderMalformed` (the region is wrong). The codes never reach the client, and neither do the credentials, which are not in any log, warning or error message. A `301` or `307` from S3 means that the bucket is in another region, which chop reports as `bucket is in another region (check CHOP_S3_REGION)` and doesn't follow."},"334":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"**Clock skew.** S3 rejects a signature when the clock of the server is more than 15 minutes off, with `RequestTimeTooSkewed` or a `403`. That looks like a permission error, so check the code in the standard error and the time of the container."},"335":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"**Credentials from the environment.** They are for Lambda and for static keys. chop reads them once at startup and doesn't refresh them, so temporary credentials with a session token stop working when they expire in a long-running process. Restart chop when they rotate, or use static keys for a server. It doesn't read instance metadata, shared credential files or web identity."},"336":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"**Interface VPC endpoints.** A private endpoint for S3 resolves to private addresses, which chop blocks unless `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE=1` is set. With a custom endpoint that is a host name, set it together with the endpoint."},"337":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/s3.html","content":"**GET only.** chop reads whole objects with a signed `GET`. It doesn't list buckets, use ranges or presigned URLs."},"338":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","type":"page","content":"Securing remote origins","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html"},"339":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"Putting chop behind a trusted proxy or a CDN limits who can send requests to it, and that's worth having. It doesn't decide where chop connects: the proxy still passes the path of the request to chop, so the protection against reaching internal hosts has to be in chop, and it is. Don't assume that a proxy rule is the only thing between a client and an internal address."},"340":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"Prefer the configured origin. The host is fixed by you, so a client can only choose a path under it, and there is nothing to allow-list. Use `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` only when a client has to choose the host, and list the hosts that you mean. Every host on the list is reachable by every client that can reach chop."},"341":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"`CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=*` makes chop an open image proxy: anyone who can send a request to chop can make it fetch and process images from any public host. The address checks, https, the size and time limits and the fetch limit still apply, but they can't stop someone from using your server and your bandwidth to fetch from the public internet, or from reaching a service that only accepts connections from your server's network, at a public address. The protection that matters then is outside of chop. If you use `*`:"},"342":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"Run chop with an egress firewall that only allows what it needs, so that a mistake in an address range can't reach your network."},"343":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"Set `allowedWidths` to the widths of your `srcset`, so that the output sizes are bounded, and keep `maxInputBytes`, `maxInputPixels` and the `CHOP_ORIGIN_*` limits low."},"344":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"Cache in front: `proxy_cache_min_uses 2` in the nginx recipe keeps one-off URLs out of the cache, and `proxy_cache_lock on` limits the fetches to one for each variant."},"345":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"Let only the proxy reach chop, and authenticate or sign the URLs there."},"346":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"More to know about remote originals:"},"347":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"chop doesn't cache originals. The proxy caches the output, and a request that isn't cached downloads the original again. An original that changes at the same URL stays stale until the cached outputs expire or are purged, so use new URLs for new versions (WordPress uploads do), or a short `CHOP_MAX_AGE`. The upstream `Cache-Control`, `ETag` and `Last-Modified` headers are ignored, and the output headers are the same as for local files."},"348":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"A `502` and a `504` have `Cache-Control: no-store`, and the proxy must not cache them. The nginx recipe only caches `200` and `404`."},"349":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"Redirects are not followed, so an origin that redirects (a CDN that moves an object, a trailing slash redirect) needs the final URL in `CHOP_ORIGIN`."},"350":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"Only HTTP/1.1 is used and TLS certificates are always verified. A private CA is added to Node.js with `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`."},"351":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/security.html","content":"An alternative that keeps chop local-only is to let nginx `proxy_pass` to the origin and store the files in a directory that chop serves, or to mount the bucket with rclone or s3fs (or to use the S3 origin, which needs no mount). That needs a second hop and a shared directory, but chop makes no network requests then."},"352":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","type":"page","content":"Sources","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html"},"353":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"What chop does for every remote fetch"},"354":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"An original comes from one of four places, and every request reads exactly one of them:"},"355":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"**The data directory.** The default. A plain path like `/2026/05/photo.jpg` is a file under `dataDir`, with the path checks of Responses."},"356":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"**The configured origin.** With `CHOP_ORIGIN=https://uploads.example.com/base`, the same plain path is appended to the base URL: `/2026/05/photo.jpg` is fetched from `https://uploads.example.com/base/2026/05/photo.jpg`. Clients never supply a host. This is the recommended way to use a remote origin, and plain paths go to the origin instead of the data directory, so `CHOP_ORIGIN` can't be combined with an explicitly set `CHOP_DATA_DIR` or `--data`. The origin must be an `https://` URL without user information, a query string or a fragment, or `http://` with `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP=1`."},"357":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"**An S3 bucket.** With `CHOP_ORIGIN=s3://my-bucket/uploads`, the plain path `/2026/05/photo.jpg` is the object `uploads/2026/05/photo.jpg` of the bucket, which chop reads with signed `GET` requests. It works with AWS S3 and with services that have an S3 API, like SeaweedFS, MinIO and Cloudflare R2, and it follows all the rules of the configured origin. See S3 and S3-compatible storage."},"358":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"**URL sources.** With `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` set, a request can name the full URL of the original, and chop fetches it if the host is on the list. Plain paths keep their meaning, and only a path that starts with `http://` or `https://` is a URL source. Without the setting, which is the default, these URLs are a `404`."},"359":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"URL sources work in both schemes. In the `query` scheme the URL is the path and the query string is chop's arguments, and in the `cloudflare` scheme the URL comes after the options:"},"360":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"A proxy that merges slashes turns `https://` into `https:/`, and some clients escape it as `https%3A//`. chop understands all three forms, with any number of slashes after the colon. A URL source can't have user information, a fragment or a query string of its own: the query string of the `query` scheme is chop's arguments, so the source can't have one, and in the `cloudflare` scheme a query string on a URL source is a `400` rather than a guess about which part it belongs to. User information and fragments are a `400` too. Ports other than 80 and 443 must be named in the allow-list."},"361":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"Each entry of `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` is a comma separated list item:"},"362":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"| Entry                 | Matches                                       |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `uploads.example.com` | That host, on the default port of the scheme. |","table":"table-0"},"363":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"| Entry           | Matches                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `*.example.com` | Any subdomain at any depth, on a dot boundary, so `a.example.com` and `a.b.example.com` match, but `example.com` and `evilexample.com` don't. List the apex too if you need it. |","table":"table-0"},"364":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"| Entry                      | Matches                                              |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `uploads.example.com:8443` | That host on that port, and not on the default port. |","table":"table-0"},"365":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"| Entry | Matches                                                                                                                                  |\n| ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `*`   | Every host, on the default ports. It can't be mixed with other entries, and it prints a warning on startup. See Securing remote origins. |","table":"table-0"},"366":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"Hosts are compared in lower case and without a trailing dot. International names must be written in punycode (`xn--...`). An empty list means no URL sources."},"367":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","content":"Whatever the source, the original is downloaded into memory, up to `maxInputBytes`, before it is processed. `X-Bytes-Saved` is measured against the downloaded size, the `ETag` is still a hash of the output, and when re-encoding doesn't make the image smaller, the downloaded bytes are sent as they are. The type of the image is found from its content, and the `Content-Type` that the origin states is ignored."},"368":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"These apply to the configured origin and to URL sources, with any allow-list, including `*`:"},"369":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"Only `https` is used, unless `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP` is set."},"370":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"The request is a `GET` with fresh headers: `Accept: image/*`, `Accept-Encoding: identity` and `User-Agent: chop`. No cookie, `Authorization`, `Referer` or other header of the client is forwarded. A compressed response is a `502`."},"371":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"Redirects are not followed. A `3xx` from the origin is a `502`."},"372":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"The host name is resolved once, every address is checked, and the connection is made to one of the addresses that were checked, so DNS rebinding can't swap the address between the check and the connection. An address literal in a URL is checked too, in any notation (`2130706433`, `0x7f.1`, `[::ffff:7f00:1]`). Loopback, private, link-local (including the cloud metadata address `169.254.169.254`), carrier-grade NAT, documentation, multicast and reserved ranges are never connected to, for IPv4 and IPv6, including IPv4-mapped and NAT64 forms. If a name resolves to several addresses and any of them is blocked, the request is not made."},"373":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"The body is cut off at `maxInputBytes` while it is read, whether or not the origin sends `Content-Length`, and a larger `Content-Length` is a `413` before the body is read."},"374":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"Connecting, including the TLS handshake, must finish within `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONNECT_TIMEOUT` (3000 ms) and the whole download within `CHOP_ORIGIN_TIMEOUT` (10000 ms), or the answer is a `504`."},"375":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"At most `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY` downloads (4) run at the same time and `CHOP_ORIGIN_QUEUE` (32) wait. More are a `503` with `Retry-After: 1`. Downloads don't use a processing slot, so a slow origin doesn't stop images from being processed, but the memory in use can reach `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY` times `maxInputBytes`, so lower one of them on a small machine."},"376":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"The body of a response that isn't a `200` is dropped without being read. The only exception is an S3 bucket, where chop reads the first 2048 bytes of the body of an error, for at most two seconds, to find the error code for the operator."},"377":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"A host name that can't be resolved is a `502` for the configured origin and the same plain `404` for a URL source, so that a client can't tell which names exist. The reason is only written to the standard error, as a host and an error code, never an error message."},"378":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"Upstream `404` and `410` are a `404`. A `401`, `403` or `407` from the origin and a destination that isn't allowed are the same plain `404`, so that a client can't tell which hosts exist, which are blocked or whether the origin needs credentials. The reason is only written to the standard error. An origin that fails or answers with another status is a `502`."},"379":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"`CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH` is the value of an `Authorization` header, like `Bearer <token>`, for a private origin. It is only sent to the configured origin and never to URL sources, it is read from the environment only, and it is never logged. A value with a line break or a control character is an invalid setting."},"380":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"`CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE=1` lets the configured origin be at a loopback, private or link-local address, like another container or a service on your private network. It applies only to the configured origin, never to a URL that a client supplied, and chop prints a warning on startup. Without it, an origin whose address is an IP literal in a blocked range is an invalid setting, and one whose name resolves to a blocked range is a `404`."},"381":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","type":"page","content":"URL schemes","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html"},"382":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#query","content":"`query`"},"383":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"`cloudflare`"},"384":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","content":"A URL scheme turns the URL of a request into the path of the original and the operations to run on it. All the schemes produce the same operations, so every scheme gets the same format negotiation, limits and path safety, and different schemes that give the same operations give the same bytes and `ETag`. Enable them with `schemes` in the settings, `CHOP_SCHEMES` or `--scheme`, which can be repeated."},"385":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","content":"The schemes are tried in the configured order, and the first one that recognizes the URL wins. A URL that none of them recognizes is a `404`. `/healthz` doesn't depend on the schemes. The `query` scheme recognizes every URL, so when it's enabled together with other schemes, list it last. The path of a scheme goes through the same checks as any path: dot segments, empty segments, slashes, backslashes and NUL bytes in a decoded segment are a `400`, and the real path must stay inside the data directory. A scheme can also find a URL source in the URL."},"386":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","content":"With `Accept: image/avif`, both of these URLs give the same AVIF bytes."},"387":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#query","content":"The default scheme. The path is the path of the original and the arguments in Requests are in the query string. A path that starts with `http://` or `https://` (also `https:/` and `https%3A//`) is a URL source, like `/https://uploads.example.com/photo.jpg?w=300`, and the query string is still chop's arguments, so the source URL can't have its own."},"388":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"The `/cdn-cgi/image/<options>/<path>` form of Cloudflare Image Resizing, with comma separated `name=value` options. It only recognizes URLs that start with `/cdn-cgi/image/`. Options that chop doesn't support, like `trim`, `rotate`, `blur`, `sharpen` and `onerror`, are ignored, and a malformed value of a supported option is a `400` that names the option. The first value wins when an option repeats. A source after the options that starts with `http://` or `https://` (also `https:/` and `https%3A//`) is a URL source, which is a `404` unless `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` is set. A query string on a URL source is a `400`, and on a path under the origin it is ignored."},"389":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option            | Maps to   |\n| ----------------- | --------- |\n| `width`, `height` | `w`, `h`. |","table":"table-0"},"390":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `fit`  | `scale-down` (default) is `w` and `h` that never enlarge, `contain` is the same with `upscale=1`, `cover` is `resize` with `upscale=1`, `crop` is `resize`, and `pad` is `lb` with `upscale=1`. `cover`, `crop` and `pad` need both `width` and `height`, and with one of them they scale like `scale-down` (`crop`) or `contain` (`cover` and `pad`). |","table":"table-0"},"391":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | `left`, `right`, `top` and `bottom` are `west`, `east`, `north` and `south`, `auto` and `face` are `attention`, and `center` and coordinates like `0.5x0.3` are the center. |","table":"table-0"},"392":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                               |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `quality` | `quality`, as a number from 1 to 100. |","table":"table-0"},"393":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option   | Maps to                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `auto`, `avif`, `webp`, `jpeg`, `png` and `gif` are `format`, and `baseline-jpeg` is `jpeg`. `json` is a `400`. |","table":"table-0"},"394":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to               |\n| ------ | --------------------- |\n| `dpr`  | `zoom`, from 1 to 10. |","table":"table-0"},"395":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option     | Maps to                                                                            |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `keep` is `strip=none`, `copyright` is `strip=metadata` and `none` is `strip=all`. |","table":"table-0"},"396":{"id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/latest/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option       | Maps to                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `background` | The `lb` color for `fit=pad`, as 3 or 6 hex digits with an optional `#` (encoded as `%23` in a URL). |","table":"table-0"},"397":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"page","content":"Reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.1.0"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html"},"398":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#requests","content":"Requests"},"399":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Query scheme arguments"},"400":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"URL schemes"},"401":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"`cloudflare`"},"402":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"Output format"},"403":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"Quality and size"},"404":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#responses","content":"Responses"},"405":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#caching","content":"Caching"},"406":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#limits","content":"Limits"},"407":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"Settings"},"408":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Interfaces"},"409":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","content":"How Chop behaves, in short. The IDs in parentheses, like `R-OP-8`, are what the tests refer to in their names. Chop is MIT licensed and was implemented from a written behavior specification and the repository conventions, without reference to the source code of any other image server."},"410":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#requests","content":"`GET` and `HEAD` are answered, other methods get `405` with `Allow: GET, HEAD` (R-REQ-1)."},"411":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#requests","content":"The path selects the original under the data directory, and a URL scheme selects the operations (R-REQ-2, S-1). Unknown arguments are ignored, so cache busters like `ver=3` are harmless."},"412":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#requests","content":"`/healthz` answers `200 ok` without touching the data directory (R-REQ-3)."},"413":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#requests","content":"The same URL and `Accept` header give the same bytes (R-REQ-4)."},"414":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#requests","content":"Path segments are percent-decoded once. `.`, `..`, empty segments and segments with `/`, `\\` or a NUL byte are a `400`, and a broken escape is a `400` (R-PATH-1)."},"415":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#requests","content":"The real path, with symbolic links resolved, must be inside the real data directory. A missing file, a directory and an escape are all the same `404` (R-PATH-2)."},"416":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#requests","content":"A file over `maxInputBytes` is a `413`, checked before the read and again after it (R-PATH-3)."},"417":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"This is the default scheme, named `query`. All arguments are optional, and a malformed value of a known argument is a `400` that names it."},"418":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `w`, `h` | Width or height in pixels. With one, scale to it. With both, fit inside the box without cropping or padding (R-OP-2). |","table":"table-0"},"419":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                           |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit=w,h` | The same as `w` and `h` together, and it wins over them (R-OP-3). |","table":"table-0"},"420":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument     | Meaning                                                                    |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resize=w,h` | Cover the box and crop to exactly `w` by `h`. It wins over `fit` (R-OP-4). |","table":"table-0"},"421":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                                             |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | Where `resize` crops: `center` (default), `north`, `south`, `east`, `west` or `attention` (R-OP-5). |","table":"table-0"},"422":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument       | Meaning                                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `crop=x,y,w,h` | A region of the oriented original, before scaling. Numbers are percentages, or pixels with a `px` suffix. The region is clipped to the image (R-OP-6). |","table":"table-0"},"423":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument         | Meaning                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lb=w,h[,color]` | Fit inside the box and pad to exactly `w` by `h`. `color` is 3 or 6 hex digits, default `ffffff` (R-OP-7). |","table":"table-0"},"424":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `zoom`   | Device pixel ratio from 1 to 10, which multiplies the sizes (R-OP-9). |","table":"table-0"},"425":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument    | Meaning                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `upscale=1` | Allow enlarging, up to `maxUpscaleDimension` (R-OP-8). |","table":"table-0"},"426":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                   |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `quality` | 1 to 100, with values below 20 raised to 20 for lossy encoders (R-QLT-1). |","table":"table-0"},"427":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                             |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `auto` (default), `jpeg`, `png`, `webp`, `avif` or `gif` (R-FMT-2). |","table":"table-0"},"428":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                            |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lossy=1` | Allow lossy output for lossless sources (R-QLT-5). |","table":"table-0"},"429":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `strip`  | `metadata` (default, keeps the ICC profile), `all` or `none` (R-QLT-6). |","table":"table-0"},"430":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Operations run in a fixed order, whatever the order in the URL: orientation, `crop`, size, `lb`, then encoding. Sizes always refer to the displayed (oriented) image (R-OP-1)."},"431":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-33","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Without `upscale=1` nothing is enlarged: sizes clamp to the original, `resize` crops at the largest size with the requested aspect ratio, and `lb` pads without enlarging (R-OP-8). The output can't exceed `maxOutputDimension` (R-OP-12)."},"432":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-34","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Animated sources keep all frames for `crop` and sizes. `lb` and `gravity=attention` are ignored for them (R-OP-13). Image adjustments (R-OP-10) and filters (R-OP-11) aren't supported, and their arguments are ignored."},"433":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-35","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme turns a URL into the path of the original and the operations. All the schemes produce the same operations, so every scheme gets the same negotiation, limits and path safety."},"434":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-36","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Schemes are tried in the configured order, and the first one that recognizes the URL wins. The default is `query` only (S-1). The `query` scheme recognizes every URL, so it has to be listed last when it's enabled with others. The `cloudflare` scheme only recognizes URLs that start with `/cdn-cgi/image/`."},"435":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-37","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme's path segments go through the same checks as any other path, so no scheme can read outside the data directory (S-2)."},"436":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-38","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A URL that no enabled scheme recognizes is a `404` (S-3)."},"437":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-39","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme ignores the options that Chop doesn't support, and a malformed value of one that it supports is a `400` (S-4)."},"438":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-40","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Different schemes that give the same operations give the same bytes and `ETag` (S-5)."},"439":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-41","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"The `/cdn-cgi/image/<options>/<path>` form of Cloudflare Image Resizing, with comma separated `name=value` options."},"440":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-42","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option            | Maps to         |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `width`, `height` | `w`, `h` (S-6). |","table":"table-1"},"441":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-43","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit`  | `scale-down` (default) is `w`/`h` that never enlarges, `contain` is the same with `upscale`, `cover` is `resize` with `upscale`, `crop` is `resize`, and `pad` is `lb` with `upscale` (S-7). |","table":"table-1"},"442":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-44","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | `left`, `right`, `top`, `bottom` are `west`, `east`, `north`, `south`, and `auto` and `face` are `attention`. Coordinates like `0.5x0.3` are ignored (S-8). |","table":"table-1"},"443":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-45","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to          |\n| --------- | ---------------- |\n| `quality` | `quality` (S-9). |","table":"table-1"},"444":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-46","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option   | Maps to                                                                                                |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `format` | `auto`, `avif`, `webp`, `jpeg`, `png`, `gif`, and `baseline-jpeg` as `jpeg`. `json` is a `400` (S-10). |","table":"table-1"},"445":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-47","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to        |\n| ------ | -------------- |\n| `dpr`  | `zoom` (S-11). |","table":"table-1"},"446":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-48","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option     | Maps to                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `keep` is `strip=none`, `copyright` is `strip=metadata`, `none` is `strip=all` (S-12). |","table":"table-1"},"447":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-49","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option       | Maps to                                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `background` | The `lb` color for `fit=pad`, as hex digits (S-13). |","table":"table-1"},"448":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-50","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"Other Cloudflare options, like `trim`, `rotate`, `blur`, `sharpen` and `onerror`, are ignored. Remote source URLs aren't supported and are a `404`."},"449":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-51","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"`Accept` is parsed per RFC 9110. Only a listed `image/avif` or `image/webp` makes those formats acceptable, so `image/*` and `*/*` don't (R-FMT-1)."},"450":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-52","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"An explicit `format` is used even when `Accept` doesn't list it. Transparency is flattened onto white for formats that can't hold it (R-FMT-2)."},"451":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-53","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"With `auto`, a still image is AVIF if enabled and accepted and the output is lossy, else WebP if accepted and within its size limit, else the fallback format: GIF for GIF sources, PNG for lossless or transparent output, and JPEG otherwise (R-FMT-3)."},"452":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-54","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"An animated source becomes an animated WebP if accepted, otherwise a GIF, and never AVIF (R-FMT-4)."},"453":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-55","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"PNG, GIF and lossless WebP sources stay lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given (R-FMT-5). JPEG, lossy WebP and AVIF sources produce lossy output (R-FMT-6)."},"454":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-56","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"Every response that depends on `Accept` has `Vary: Accept` (R-FMT-7)."},"455":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-57","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP and AVIF are read, detected from the content. Other content is a `415`, and unreadable or corrupt files are a `422` (R-FMT-8)."},"456":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-58","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"The defaults are JPEG 82, WebP 80 and AVIF 55, lowered to the estimated quality of a JPEG source, so that a recompressed JPEG never gets a higher quality than it has. The estimate compares the file's luminance quantization table with the standard table scaled for each quality. An explicit `quality` is used as given (R-QLT-2, R-QLT-3)."},"457":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-59","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"A request that changes nothing about the pixels and keeps the source format sends the original bytes when the re-encoded image isn't smaller, and with `strip=none` it always sends them (R-QLT-4)."},"458":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-60","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#responses","content":"`200` has the output `Content-Type`, `Content-Length`, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=<maxAge>`, `Vary: Accept`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a strong SHA-256 `ETag` (R-RES-1). `X-Bytes-Saved` appears when the output is smaller than the original (R-RES-3)."},"459":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-61","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#responses","content":"`If-None-Match` that matches, including weak comparison, lists and `*`, gets a `304` without a body (R-RES-2)."},"460":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-62","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#responses","content":"Errors are plain text with `Cache-Control: no-store` and no file system paths: `400` invalid request, `404` not found, `405` method, `413` original too large, `415` unsupported type, `422` unreadable image, `500` unexpected, `503` busy (R-RES-4)."},"461":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-63","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#caching","content":"Responses depend on `Accept` and the URL only, so a cache can key on the URL and a bucket of `Accept`: `image/avif`, `image/webp` or neither. Send the bucket as `Accept` upstream so that the body matches the key. The README has an nginx recipe."},"462":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-64","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#limits","content":"At most `maxConcurrency` images are processed at once and `maxQueue` more wait in order. A request that finds the queue full gets `503` with `Retry-After: 1`, and a failing request frees its slot (R-LIM-1, R-LIM-2)."},"463":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-65","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#limits","content":"Decoding is limited by `maxInputPixels` (R-LIM-3)."},"464":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-66","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#limits","content":"`allowedWidths` optionally restricts the output widths to a list (R-LIM-4)."},"465":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-67","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#limits","content":"Chop never writes to disk and makes no network requests (R-LIM-5)."},"466":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-68","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `dataDir` | `CHOP_DATA_DIR`      | `/data` |","table":"table-2"},"467":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-69","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable             | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `schemes` | `CHOP_SCHEMES` (comma separated) | `query` |","table":"table-2"},"468":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-70","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default    |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxAge` | `CHOP_MAX_AGE`       | `31536000` |","table":"table-2"},"469":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-71","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable   | Default        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | -------------- |\n| `maxConcurrency` | `CHOP_MAX_CONCURRENCY` | number of CPUs |","table":"table-2"},"470":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-72","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable | Default |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxQueue` | `CHOP_MAX_QUEUE`     | `64`    |","table":"table-2"},"471":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-73","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable   | Default    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxInputBytes` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_BYTES` | `52428800` |","table":"table-2"},"472":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-74","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable    | Default     |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | ----------- |\n| `maxInputPixels` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_PIXELS` | `120000000` |","table":"table-2"},"473":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-75","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxOutputDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_OUTPUT_DIMENSION` | `8192`  |","table":"table-2"},"474":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-76","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable         | Default |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxUpscaleDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_UPSCALE_DIMENSION` | `4096`  |","table":"table-2"},"475":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-77","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                     | Environment variable                                          | Default          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `jpegQuality`, `webpQuality`, `avifQuality` | `CHOP_JPEG_QUALITY`, `CHOP_WEBP_QUALITY`, `CHOP_AVIF_QUALITY` | `82`, `80`, `55` |","table":"table-2"},"476":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-78","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avif`  | `CHOP_AVIF`          | `true`  |","table":"table-2"},"477":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-79","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avifEffort` | `CHOP_AVIF_EFFORT`   | `4`     |","table":"table-2"},"478":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-80","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                    | Default |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `allowedWidths` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_WIDTHS` (comma separated) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"479":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-81","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createHandler( settings? )` returns `( request ) => Promise< Response >` with `{ method, url, headers }` in and `{ status, headers, body }` out. It never throws for a request, never uses `node:http` and reports unexpected errors to an optional `onError` (R-API-1)."},"480":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-82","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createConfig()`, `configFromEnv( env )`, `parseQuery()`, `createServer()`, the URL schemes `queryScheme` and `cloudflareScheme` with their `SCHEMES` registry and the `UrlScheme` type (`{ name, parse( url ) }`, where `parse` returns `{ segments, ops }` or `null`), and the other types are exported too (R-API-2, S-1)."},"481":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-83","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Errors are `ChopError` with a `code` from `CHOP_ERROR_CODES`, checked with `isChopError()` (R-API-3)."},"482":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html-84","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"The CLI is `chop [--data <dir>] [--port <n>] [--host <address>] [--scheme <name>] [--help]`, with flags overriding `CHOP_*` variables. Exit codes are `0`, `1` for a failure and `2` for invalid options. `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` stop it gracefully, and `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG=1` prints one JSON line per request (R-CLI-1 to R-CLI-4)."},"483":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"page","content":"Reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.1.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html"},"484":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#requests","content":"Requests"},"485":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Query scheme arguments"},"486":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"URL schemes"},"487":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"`cloudflare`"},"488":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"Output format"},"489":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"Quality and size"},"490":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#responses","content":"Responses"},"491":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#caching","content":"Caching"},"492":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#limits","content":"Limits"},"493":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"Settings"},"494":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Interfaces"},"495":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","content":"How chop behaves, in short. The IDs in parentheses, like `R-OP-8`, are what the tests refer to in their names. chop is MIT licensed and was implemented from a written behavior specification and the repository conventions, without reference to the source code of any other image server."},"496":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#requests","content":"`GET` and `HEAD` are answered, other methods get `405` with `Allow: GET, HEAD` (R-REQ-1)."},"497":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#requests","content":"The path selects the original under the data directory, and a URL scheme selects the operations (R-REQ-2, S-1). Unknown arguments are ignored, so cache busters like `ver=3` are harmless."},"498":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#requests","content":"`/healthz` answers `200 ok` without touching the data directory (R-REQ-3)."},"499":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#requests","content":"The same URL and `Accept` header give the same bytes (R-REQ-4)."},"500":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#requests","content":"Path segments are percent-decoded once. `.`, `..`, empty segments and segments with `/`, `\\` or a NUL byte are a `400`, and a broken escape is a `400` (R-PATH-1)."},"501":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#requests","content":"The real path, with symbolic links resolved, must be inside the real data directory. A missing file, a directory and an escape are all the same `404` (R-PATH-2)."},"502":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#requests","content":"A file over `maxInputBytes` is a `413`, checked before the read and again after it (R-PATH-3)."},"503":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"This is the default scheme, named `query`. All arguments are optional, and a malformed value of a known argument is a `400` that names it."},"504":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `w`, `h` | Width or height in pixels. With one, scale to it. With both, fit inside the box without cropping or padding (R-OP-2). |","table":"table-0"},"505":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                           |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit=w,h` | The same as `w` and `h` together, and it wins over them (R-OP-3). |","table":"table-0"},"506":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument     | Meaning                                                                    |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resize=w,h` | Cover the box and crop to exactly `w` by `h`. It wins over `fit` (R-OP-4). |","table":"table-0"},"507":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                                             |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | Where `resize` crops: `center` (default), `north`, `south`, `east`, `west` or `attention` (R-OP-5). |","table":"table-0"},"508":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument       | Meaning                                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `crop=x,y,w,h` | A region of the oriented original, before scaling. Numbers are percentages, or pixels with a `px` suffix. The region is clipped to the image (R-OP-6). |","table":"table-0"},"509":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument         | Meaning                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lb=w,h[,color]` | Fit inside the box and pad to exactly `w` by `h`. `color` is 3 or 6 hex digits, default `ffffff` (R-OP-7). |","table":"table-0"},"510":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `zoom`   | Device pixel ratio from 1 to 10, which multiplies the sizes (R-OP-9). |","table":"table-0"},"511":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument    | Meaning                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `upscale=1` | Allow enlarging, up to `maxUpscaleDimension` (R-OP-8). |","table":"table-0"},"512":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                   |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `quality` | 1 to 100, with values below 20 raised to 20 for lossy encoders (R-QLT-1). |","table":"table-0"},"513":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                             |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `auto` (default), `jpeg`, `png`, `webp`, `avif` or `gif` (R-FMT-2). |","table":"table-0"},"514":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                            |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lossy=1` | Allow lossy output for lossless sources (R-QLT-5). |","table":"table-0"},"515":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `strip`  | `metadata` (default, keeps the ICC profile), `all` or `none` (R-QLT-6). |","table":"table-0"},"516":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Operations run in a fixed order, whatever the order in the URL: orientation, `crop`, size, `lb`, then encoding. Sizes always refer to the displayed (oriented) image (R-OP-1)."},"517":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-33","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Without `upscale=1` nothing is enlarged: sizes clamp to the original, `resize` crops at the largest size with the requested aspect ratio, and `lb` pads without enlarging (R-OP-8). The output can't exceed `maxOutputDimension` (R-OP-12)."},"518":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-34","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Animated sources keep all frames for `crop` and sizes. `lb` and `gravity=attention` are ignored for them (R-OP-13). Image adjustments (R-OP-10) and filters (R-OP-11) aren't supported, and their arguments are ignored."},"519":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-35","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme turns a URL into the path of the original and the operations. All the schemes produce the same operations, so every scheme gets the same negotiation, limits and path safety."},"520":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-36","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Schemes are tried in the configured order, and the first one that recognizes the URL wins. The default is `query` only (S-1). The `query` scheme recognizes every URL, so it has to be listed last when it's enabled with others. The `cloudflare` scheme only recognizes URLs that start with `/cdn-cgi/image/`."},"521":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-37","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme's path segments go through the same checks as any other path, so no scheme can read outside the data directory (S-2)."},"522":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-38","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A URL that no enabled scheme recognizes is a `404` (S-3)."},"523":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-39","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme ignores the options that chop doesn't support, and a malformed value of one that it supports is a `400` (S-4)."},"524":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-40","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Different schemes that give the same operations give the same bytes and `ETag` (S-5)."},"525":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-41","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"The `/cdn-cgi/image/<options>/<path>` form of Cloudflare Image Resizing, with comma separated `name=value` options."},"526":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-42","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option            | Maps to         |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `width`, `height` | `w`, `h` (S-6). |","table":"table-1"},"527":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-43","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit`  | `scale-down` (default) is `w`/`h` that never enlarges, `contain` is the same with `upscale`, `cover` is `resize` with `upscale`, `crop` is `resize`, and `pad` is `lb` with `upscale` (S-7). |","table":"table-1"},"528":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-44","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | `left`, `right`, `top`, `bottom` are `west`, `east`, `north`, `south`, and `auto` and `face` are `attention`. Coordinates like `0.5x0.3` are ignored (S-8). |","table":"table-1"},"529":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-45","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to          |\n| --------- | ---------------- |\n| `quality` | `quality` (S-9). |","table":"table-1"},"530":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-46","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option   | Maps to                                                                                                |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `format` | `auto`, `avif`, `webp`, `jpeg`, `png`, `gif`, and `baseline-jpeg` as `jpeg`. `json` is a `400` (S-10). |","table":"table-1"},"531":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-47","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to        |\n| ------ | -------------- |\n| `dpr`  | `zoom` (S-11). |","table":"table-1"},"532":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-48","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option     | Maps to                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `keep` is `strip=none`, `copyright` is `strip=metadata`, `none` is `strip=all` (S-12). |","table":"table-1"},"533":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-49","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option       | Maps to                                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `background` | The `lb` color for `fit=pad`, as hex digits (S-13). |","table":"table-1"},"534":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-50","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"Other Cloudflare options, like `trim`, `rotate`, `blur`, `sharpen` and `onerror`, are ignored. Remote source URLs aren't supported and are a `404`."},"535":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-51","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"`Accept` is parsed per RFC 9110. Only a listed `image/avif` or `image/webp` makes those formats acceptable, so `image/*` and `*/*` don't (R-FMT-1)."},"536":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-52","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"An explicit `format` is used even when `Accept` doesn't list it. Transparency is flattened onto white for formats that can't hold it (R-FMT-2)."},"537":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-53","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"With `auto`, a still image is AVIF if enabled and accepted and the output is lossy, else WebP if accepted and within its size limit, else the fallback format: GIF for GIF sources, PNG for lossless or transparent output, and JPEG otherwise (R-FMT-3)."},"538":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-54","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"An animated source becomes an animated WebP if accepted, otherwise a GIF, and never AVIF (R-FMT-4)."},"539":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-55","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"PNG, GIF and lossless WebP sources stay lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given (R-FMT-5). JPEG, lossy WebP and AVIF sources produce lossy output (R-FMT-6)."},"540":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-56","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"Every response that depends on `Accept` has `Vary: Accept` (R-FMT-7)."},"541":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-57","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP and AVIF are read, detected from the content. Other content is a `415`, and unreadable or corrupt files are a `422` (R-FMT-8)."},"542":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-58","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"The defaults are JPEG 82, WebP 80 and AVIF 55, lowered to the estimated quality of a JPEG source, so that a recompressed JPEG never gets a higher quality than it has. The estimate compares the file's luminance quantization table with the standard table scaled for each quality. An explicit `quality` is used as given (R-QLT-2, R-QLT-3)."},"543":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-59","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"A request that changes nothing about the pixels and keeps the source format sends the original bytes when the re-encoded image isn't smaller, and with `strip=none` it always sends them (R-QLT-4)."},"544":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-60","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#responses","content":"`200` has the output `Content-Type`, `Content-Length`, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=<maxAge>`, `Vary: Accept`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a strong SHA-256 `ETag` (R-RES-1). `X-Bytes-Saved` appears when the output is smaller than the original (R-RES-3)."},"545":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-61","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#responses","content":"`If-None-Match` that matches, including weak comparison, lists and `*`, gets a `304` without a body (R-RES-2)."},"546":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-62","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#responses","content":"Errors are plain text with `Cache-Control: no-store` and no file system paths: `400` invalid request, `404` not found, `405` method, `413` original too large, `415` unsupported type, `422` unreadable image, `500` unexpected, `503` busy (R-RES-4)."},"547":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-63","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#caching","content":"Responses depend on `Accept` and the URL only, so a cache can key on the URL and a bucket of `Accept`: `image/avif`, `image/webp` or neither. Send the bucket as `Accept` upstream so that the body matches the key. The README has an nginx recipe."},"548":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-64","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#limits","content":"At most `maxConcurrency` images are processed at once and `maxQueue` more wait in order. A request that finds the queue full gets `503` with `Retry-After: 1`, and a failing request frees its slot (R-LIM-1, R-LIM-2)."},"549":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-65","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#limits","content":"Decoding is limited by `maxInputPixels` (R-LIM-3)."},"550":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-66","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#limits","content":"`allowedWidths` optionally restricts the output widths to a list (R-LIM-4)."},"551":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-67","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#limits","content":"chop never writes to disk and makes no network requests (R-LIM-5)."},"552":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-68","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `dataDir` | `CHOP_DATA_DIR`      | `/data` |","table":"table-2"},"553":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-69","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable             | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `schemes` | `CHOP_SCHEMES` (comma separated) | `query` |","table":"table-2"},"554":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-70","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default    |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxAge` | `CHOP_MAX_AGE`       | `31536000` |","table":"table-2"},"555":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-71","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable   | Default        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | -------------- |\n| `maxConcurrency` | `CHOP_MAX_CONCURRENCY` | number of CPUs |","table":"table-2"},"556":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-72","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable | Default |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxQueue` | `CHOP_MAX_QUEUE`     | `64`    |","table":"table-2"},"557":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-73","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable   | Default    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxInputBytes` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_BYTES` | `52428800` |","table":"table-2"},"558":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-74","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable    | Default     |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | ----------- |\n| `maxInputPixels` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_PIXELS` | `120000000` |","table":"table-2"},"559":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-75","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxOutputDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_OUTPUT_DIMENSION` | `8192`  |","table":"table-2"},"560":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-76","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable         | Default |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxUpscaleDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_UPSCALE_DIMENSION` | `4096`  |","table":"table-2"},"561":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-77","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                     | Environment variable                                          | Default          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `jpegQuality`, `webpQuality`, `avifQuality` | `CHOP_JPEG_QUALITY`, `CHOP_WEBP_QUALITY`, `CHOP_AVIF_QUALITY` | `82`, `80`, `55` |","table":"table-2"},"562":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-78","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avif`  | `CHOP_AVIF`          | `true`  |","table":"table-2"},"563":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-79","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avifEffort` | `CHOP_AVIF_EFFORT`   | `4`     |","table":"table-2"},"564":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-80","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                    | Default |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `allowedWidths` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_WIDTHS` (comma separated) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"565":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-81","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createHandler( settings? )` returns `( request ) => Promise< Response >` with `{ method, url, headers }` in and `{ status, headers, body }` out. It never throws for a request, never uses `node:http` and reports unexpected errors to an optional `onError` (R-API-1)."},"566":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-82","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createConfig()`, `configFromEnv( env )`, `parseQuery()`, `createServer()`, the URL schemes `queryScheme` and `cloudflareScheme` with their `SCHEMES` registry and the `UrlScheme` type (`{ name, parse( url ) }`, where `parse` returns `{ segments, ops }` or `null`), and the other types are exported too (R-API-2, S-1)."},"567":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-83","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Errors are `ChopError` with a `code` from `CHOP_ERROR_CODES`, checked with `isChopError()` (R-API-3)."},"568":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html-84","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.1.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"The CLI is `chop [--data <dir>] [--port <n>] [--host <address>] [--scheme <name>] [--help]`, with flags overriding `CHOP_*` variables. Exit codes are `0`, `1` for a failure and `2` for invalid options. `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` stop it gracefully, and `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG=1` prints one JSON line per request (R-CLI-1 to R-CLI-4)."},"569":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"page","content":"Reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.0"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html"},"570":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#requests","content":"Requests"},"571":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"Sources"},"572":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"S3 origin"},"573":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Query scheme arguments"},"574":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"URL schemes"},"575":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"`cloudflare`"},"576":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"Output format"},"577":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"Quality and size"},"578":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#responses","content":"Responses"},"579":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#caching","content":"Caching"},"580":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#limits","content":"Limits"},"581":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"Settings"},"582":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Interfaces"},"583":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","content":"How chop behaves, in short. The IDs in parentheses, like `R-OP-8`, are what the tests refer to in their names. chop is MIT licensed and was implemented from a written behavior specification and the repository conventions, without reference to the source code of any other image server."},"584":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#requests","content":"`GET` and `HEAD` are answered, other methods get `405` with `Allow: GET, HEAD` (R-REQ-1)."},"585":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#requests","content":"The path selects the original under the data directory or the configured origin, and a URL scheme selects the operations (R-REQ-2, S-1). Unknown arguments are ignored, so cache busters like `ver=3` are harmless."},"586":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#requests","content":"`/healthz` answers `200 ok` without touching the data directory or the origin (R-REQ-3)."},"587":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#requests","content":"The same URL and `Accept` header give the same bytes (R-REQ-4)."},"588":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#requests","content":"Path segments are percent-decoded once. `.`, `..`, empty segments and segments with `/`, `\\` or a NUL byte are a `400`, and a broken escape is a `400` (R-PATH-1). This is for plain paths: in a URL source the embedded URL path is sent to the origin as written, so `//` in it is allowed, but dot segments and broken escapes are still a `400` (R-SRC-14)."},"589":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#requests","content":"The real path, with symbolic links resolved, must be inside the real data directory. A missing file, a directory and an escape are all the same `404` (R-PATH-2)."},"590":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#requests","content":"A file over `maxInputBytes` is a `413`, checked before the read and again after it (R-PATH-3). These checks are for the local data directory."},"591":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"Where the original comes from. The data directory is the default and its behavior is the one above."},"592":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"Plain paths go to the configured origin (`origin`, `CHOP_ORIGIN`) when there is one, and to the data directory when there isn't. A URL source goes to the HTTP fetcher with the allow-list (R-SRC-1)."},"593":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"The URL of a plain path is the origin base URL, its path without a trailing slash and the path segments, each percent-encoded again, so a segment can't change the host, the port, the query string or the path of the base (R-SRC-2)."},"594":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"The origin is `https://`, or `http://` with `originAllowHttp`, without user information, a query string or a fragment, and not an IP literal in a blocked range unless `originAllowPrivate` is set. The same scheme rule applies to URL sources, and a bad origin is an invalid setting at startup (R-SRC-3)."},"595":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"Before connecting, the address literal in the URL is checked, or the name is resolved, every address is checked and the socket only gets the addresses that were checked. If any address is blocked nothing is connected, and the connection is made to one of the addresses that were checked and not to a second DNS answer, so DNS rebinding can't swap the address. Blocked addresses are loopback, unspecified, private, link-local (including `169.254.169.254`), carrier-grade NAT, documentation, multicast and reserved ranges for IPv4 and IPv6, with IPv4-mapped and NAT64 addresses checked as the IPv4 address that they contain, 6to4 and Teredo blocked, and anything that can't be parsed blocked (R-SRC-4)."},"596":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"Redirects are not followed, and a `3xx` is a `502` (R-SRC-5)."},"597":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"The request is a `GET` with `Accept: image/*`, `Accept-Encoding: identity` and `User-Agent: chop`, and without any header of the client. `originAuth` is sent as `Authorization` to the configured origin only. A response with a `Content-Encoding` is a `502` (R-SRC-6)."},"598":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"The body is limited to `maxInputBytes` while it is read, whether or not there is a `Content-Length`, and a `Content-Length` over the limit is a `413` before the body is read (R-SRC-7)."},"599":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"Connecting must finish within `originConnectTimeout` and the whole download within `originTimeout`, or the answer is a `504`. Upstream failures, a `5xx` or other unexpected status, a redirect and a body that ends early are a `502`, and the body of a response that is not a `200` is dropped without being read. A name that can't be resolved is a `502` for the configured origin, so the operator sees a broken origin, and a plain `404` for a URL source, so that a client can't tell which names exist (R-SRC-8)."},"600":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"An upstream `404` or `410`, an upstream `401`, `403` or `407`, a URL source that is not allowed and a blocked destination are all the same plain `404`. The reason is only given to the `onOriginError` callback, which the command writes to the standard error, and it is made of the host, a status code or an error code and never an error message (R-SRC-9)."},"601":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"The type is found from the content, and the `Content-Type` of the origin is not used (R-SRC-10)."},"602":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"The headers of the origin, like `Cache-Control` and `ETag`, don't change the response, and the original is not cached (R-SRC-11)."},"603":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-33","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"A `HEAD` request downloads and processes the original like a `GET`, since it must have the same headers, including `Content-Length` (R-REQ-1), so a proxy should not forward `HEAD` requests for remote originals unless it needs them (R-SRC-12)."},"604":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-34","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"At most `originConcurrency` downloads run at once and `originQueue` more wait, outside of the processing slots, and a full queue is a `503` with `Retry-After: 1` (R-SRC-12)."},"605":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-35","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"A URL source is a URL after `/` in the `query` scheme or after the options in the `cloudflare` scheme, written `https://host/path`, `https:/host/path` or `https%3A//host/path`. It is a `404` unless `allowedHosts` is not empty and names its host, and the match is on the lower case host without a trailing dot, and the port (R-SRC-13)."},"606":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-36","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"A URL source with user information, a fragment, or a query string of its own (a `400` in the `cloudflare` scheme, and not possible in the `query` scheme where the query is chop's arguments) is a `400`, and dot segments are a `400` as for any path. A port other than the default of the scheme must be in the entry (R-SRC-14)."},"607":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-37","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"`allowedHosts` entries are `host`, `*.example.com` (subdomains on a dot boundary, not the apex), either with `:port`, or `*` for every host on the default ports. `*` can't be mixed with other entries, and it is a warning at startup. Even with `*` everything else of this section applies, and `originAllowPrivate` never applies to a URL source (R-SRC-15)."},"608":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-38","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#sources","content":"A data directory that is set explicitly and an origin together are an invalid setting (R-SRC-16)."},"609":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-39","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`origin` set to `s3://bucket[/prefix]` reads the originals from an S3 bucket or an S3-compatible service. It is the HTTP origin of the section above for requests of the bucket, with signed requests, and every rule of that section applies unless it is changed here."},"610":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-40","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`origin` is parsed into a bucket and a prefix: the bucket has 3 to 63 lower case letters, digits, dots and hyphens and isn't an IP address, and the prefix can't have empty, `.` or `..` segments, a query string or a fragment. `http://` and `https://` origins are unchanged, and a data directory that is set explicitly together with an `s3://` origin is an invalid setting (R-S3-1)."},"611":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-41","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The region is `s3Region` (`CHOP_S3_REGION`, then `AWS_REGION`). On AWS, which is without `s3Endpoint`, it is required and a missing one is an invalid setting at startup. With an endpoint it defaults to `us-east-1`, and `auto` is allowed for R2 (R-S3-2)."},"612":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-42","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"On AWS the bucket is in the host, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`, unless `s3PathStyle` is true or the bucket name has dots, which use `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`. A custom endpoint is `endpoint/bucket/key` unless `s3PathStyle` is false, which uses `bucket.endpoint-host`. The endpoint is checked like the origin: https, or http with `originAllowHttp`, no user information, query string or fragment, and no blocked address without `originAllowPrivate` (R-S3-3)."},"613":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-43","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"With `s3AccessKeyId` and `s3SecretAccessKey` every request to the bucket is signed with AWS Signature Version 4 with a fresh date, and the signed host is the `Host` header that is sent, with its port. A session token is sent and signed as `x-amz-security-token`. Without a key and a secret requests are unsigned and there is a warning at startup, and a key without a secret, a secret without a key and a token alone are invalid settings (R-S3-4)."},"614":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-44","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The key is the prefix and the validated segments of the path, and each segment is percent-encoded once, keeping only `A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~`, and sent exactly as it is signed. The path is not normalized (R-S3-5)."},"615":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-45","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The errors are those of the HTTP origin: `404` and `403` from the bucket are a plain `404`, a `5xx`, a network or TLS error and a redirect are a `502`, a timeout is a `504`, and an object over `maxInputBytes` is a `413` (R-S3-6)."},"616":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-46","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"For the operator only, the first 2048 bytes of the body of an error from the bucket are read (for at most two seconds), and the `<Code>` of the XML, like `SignatureDoesNotMatch`, `AccessDenied`, `RequestTimeTooSkewed`, `ExpiredToken` or `InvalidAccessKeyId`, is given to `onOriginError` in the detail of the error. `NoSuchKey` is not reported, since it is an ordinary miss. A `301` or `307` is a `502` with the detail `bucket is in another region (check CHOP_S3_REGION)` and isn't followed. The body of an error of any other origin is still dropped without being read (R-S3-7)."},"617":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-47","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"Requests for URL sources are never signed and never get the credentials, and the URL sources of `allowedHosts` keep working (R-S3-8)."},"618":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-48","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The secret key and the session token are only read from the environment by the command, and are not in any error message, warning or log line (R-S3-9)."},"619":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-49","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`, `CHOP_S3_REGION`, `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE`, `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` and `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN` are read, with `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` and `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` as the fallbacks, and `--origin s3://bucket` works. Credentials are read once at startup and aren't refreshed (R-S3-10)."},"620":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-50","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"This is the default scheme, named `query`. All arguments are optional, and a malformed value of a known argument is a `400` that names it."},"621":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-51","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `w`, `h` | Width or height in pixels. With one, scale to it. With both, fit inside the box without cropping or padding (R-OP-2). |","table":"table-0"},"622":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-52","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                           |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit=w,h` | The same as `w` and `h` together, and it wins over them (R-OP-3). |","table":"table-0"},"623":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-53","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument     | Meaning                                                                    |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resize=w,h` | Cover the box and crop to exactly `w` by `h`. It wins over `fit` (R-OP-4). |","table":"table-0"},"624":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-54","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                                             |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | Where `resize` crops: `center` (default), `north`, `south`, `east`, `west` or `attention` (R-OP-5). |","table":"table-0"},"625":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-55","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument       | Meaning                                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `crop=x,y,w,h` | A region of the oriented original, before scaling. Numbers are percentages, or pixels with a `px` suffix. The region is clipped to the image (R-OP-6). |","table":"table-0"},"626":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-56","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument         | Meaning                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lb=w,h[,color]` | Fit inside the box and pad to exactly `w` by `h`. `color` is 3 or 6 hex digits, default `ffffff` (R-OP-7). |","table":"table-0"},"627":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-57","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `zoom`   | Device pixel ratio from 1 to 10, which multiplies the sizes (R-OP-9). |","table":"table-0"},"628":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-58","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument    | Meaning                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `upscale=1` | Allow enlarging, up to `maxUpscaleDimension` (R-OP-8). |","table":"table-0"},"629":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-59","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                   |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `quality` | 1 to 100, with values below 20 raised to 20 for lossy encoders (R-QLT-1). |","table":"table-0"},"630":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-60","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                             |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `auto` (default), `jpeg`, `png`, `webp`, `avif` or `gif` (R-FMT-2). |","table":"table-0"},"631":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-61","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                            |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lossy=1` | Allow lossy output for lossless sources (R-QLT-5). |","table":"table-0"},"632":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-62","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `strip`  | `metadata` (default, keeps the ICC profile), `all` or `none` (R-QLT-6). |","table":"table-0"},"633":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-63","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Operations run in a fixed order, whatever the order in the URL: orientation, `crop`, size, `lb`, then encoding. Sizes always refer to the displayed (oriented) image (R-OP-1)."},"634":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-64","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Without `upscale=1` nothing is enlarged: sizes clamp to the original, `resize` crops at the largest size with the requested aspect ratio, and `lb` pads without enlarging (R-OP-8). The output can't exceed `maxOutputDimension` (R-OP-12)."},"635":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-65","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Animated sources keep all frames for `crop` and sizes. `lb` and `gravity=attention` are ignored for them (R-OP-13). Image adjustments (R-OP-10) and filters (R-OP-11) aren't supported, and their arguments are ignored."},"636":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-66","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme turns a URL into the path of the original and the operations. All the schemes produce the same operations, so every scheme gets the same negotiation, limits and path safety."},"637":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-67","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Schemes are tried in the configured order, and the first one that recognizes the URL wins. The default is `query` only (S-1). The `query` scheme recognizes every URL, so it has to be listed last when it's enabled with others. The `cloudflare` scheme only recognizes URLs that start with `/cdn-cgi/image/`."},"638":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-68","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme's path segments go through the same checks as any other path, so no scheme can read outside the data directory (S-2)."},"639":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-69","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A URL that no enabled scheme recognizes is a `404` (S-3)."},"640":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-70","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme ignores the options that chop doesn't support, and a malformed value of one that it supports is a `400` (S-4)."},"641":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-71","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Different schemes that give the same operations give the same bytes and `ETag` (S-5)."},"642":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-72","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"The `/cdn-cgi/image/<options>/<path>` form of Cloudflare Image Resizing, with comma separated `name=value` options."},"643":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-73","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option            | Maps to         |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `width`, `height` | `w`, `h` (S-6). |","table":"table-1"},"644":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-74","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit`  | `scale-down` (default) is `w`/`h` that never enlarges, `contain` is the same with `upscale`, `cover` is `resize` with `upscale`, `crop` is `resize`, and `pad` is `lb` with `upscale` (S-7). |","table":"table-1"},"645":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-75","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | `left`, `right`, `top`, `bottom` are `west`, `east`, `north`, `south`, and `auto` and `face` are `attention`. Coordinates like `0.5x0.3` are ignored (S-8). |","table":"table-1"},"646":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-76","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to          |\n| --------- | ---------------- |\n| `quality` | `quality` (S-9). |","table":"table-1"},"647":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-77","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option   | Maps to                                                                                                |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `format` | `auto`, `avif`, `webp`, `jpeg`, `png`, `gif`, and `baseline-jpeg` as `jpeg`. `json` is a `400` (S-10). |","table":"table-1"},"648":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-78","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to        |\n| ------ | -------------- |\n| `dpr`  | `zoom` (S-11). |","table":"table-1"},"649":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-79","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option     | Maps to                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `keep` is `strip=none`, `copyright` is `strip=metadata`, `none` is `strip=all` (S-12). |","table":"table-1"},"650":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-80","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option       | Maps to                                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `background` | The `lb` color for `fit=pad`, as hex digits (S-13). |","table":"table-1"},"651":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-81","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"Other Cloudflare options, like `trim`, `rotate`, `blur`, `sharpen` and `onerror`, are ignored. A source that starts with `http://` or `https://` is a URL source (see Sources) and is a `404` without `allowedHosts`."},"652":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-82","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"`Accept` is parsed per RFC 9110. Only a listed `image/avif` or `image/webp` makes those formats acceptable, so `image/*` and `*/*` don't (R-FMT-1)."},"653":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-83","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"An explicit `format` is used even when `Accept` doesn't list it. Transparency is flattened onto white for formats that can't hold it (R-FMT-2)."},"654":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-84","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"With `auto`, a still image is the negotiated format from `autoFormats` (R-FMT-10): AVIF if the output is lossy, or WebP if the output is within its size limit. Without an accepted candidate it is the fallback format: GIF for GIF sources, PNG for lossless or transparent output, and JPEG otherwise (R-FMT-3)."},"655":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-85","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"An animated source becomes an animated WebP if accepted and in `autoFormats`, otherwise a GIF, and never AVIF (R-FMT-4)."},"656":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-86","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"PNG, GIF and lossless WebP sources stay lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given (R-FMT-5). JPEG, lossy WebP and AVIF sources produce lossy output (R-FMT-6)."},"657":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-87","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"Every response that depends on `Accept` has `Vary: Accept` (R-FMT-7)."},"658":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-88","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP and AVIF are read, detected from the content. Other content is a `415`, and unreadable or corrupt files are a `422` (R-FMT-8)."},"659":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-89","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"A source whose detected format isn't in `allowedInputFormats` is a `415` with the same message as other unsupported content, which doesn't tell which formats are allowed. The check follows the header detection and comes before any pixel decoding or processing (R-FMT-9)."},"660":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-90","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#output-format","content":"`autoFormats` lists the formats (`avif`, `webp`) that `auto` can negotiate, in order of preference. Among the listed formats that `Accept` lists with `q` above 0 (and that pass the checks of R-FMT-3), the one with the highest `q` is used, and the earlier entry of `autoFormats` wins a tie. An empty list disables the upgrades. An explicit `format` is not restricted by `autoFormats`, and `avif: false` removes AVIF from the list (R-FMT-10)."},"661":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-91","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"The defaults are JPEG 82, WebP 80 and AVIF 55, lowered to the estimated quality of a JPEG source, so that a recompressed JPEG never gets a higher quality than it has. The estimate compares the file's luminance quantization table with the standard table scaled for each quality. An explicit `quality` is used as given (R-QLT-2, R-QLT-3)."},"662":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-92","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"A request that changes nothing about the pixels and keeps the source format sends the original bytes when the re-encoded image isn't smaller, and with `strip=none` it always sends them (R-QLT-4)."},"663":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-93","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#responses","content":"`200` has the output `Content-Type`, `Content-Length`, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=<maxAge>`, `Vary: Accept`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a strong SHA-256 `ETag` (R-RES-1). `X-Bytes-Saved` appears when the output is smaller than the original (R-RES-3)."},"664":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-94","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#responses","content":"`If-None-Match` that matches, including weak comparison, lists and `*`, gets a `304` without a body (R-RES-2)."},"665":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-95","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#responses","content":"Errors are plain text with `Cache-Control: no-store` and no file system paths: `400` invalid request, `404` not found, `405` method, `413` original too large, `415` unsupported type, `422` unreadable image, `500` unexpected, `502` the origin failed, `503` busy and `504` the origin was too slow (R-RES-4)."},"666":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-96","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#caching","content":"Responses depend on `Accept` and the URL only, so a cache can key on the URL and a bucket of `Accept`: `image/avif`, `image/webp` or neither. Send the bucket as `Accept` upstream so that the body matches the key. The README has an nginx recipe."},"667":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-97","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#limits","content":"At most `maxConcurrency` images are processed at once and `maxQueue` more wait in order. A request that finds the queue full gets `503` with `Retry-After: 1`, and a failing request frees its slot (R-LIM-1, R-LIM-2)."},"668":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-98","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#limits","content":"Decoding is limited by `maxInputPixels` (R-LIM-3)."},"669":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-99","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#limits","content":"`allowedWidths` optionally restricts the output widths to a list (R-LIM-4)."},"670":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-100","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#limits","content":"chop never writes to disk, and makes no network requests unless an origin or `allowedHosts` is configured, and then only to those hosts (R-LIM-5)."},"671":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-101","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `dataDir` | `CHOP_DATA_DIR`      | `/data` |","table":"table-2"},"672":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-102","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable             | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `schemes` | `CHOP_SCHEMES` (comma separated) | `query` |","table":"table-2"},"673":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-103","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default    |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxAge` | `CHOP_MAX_AGE`       | `31536000` |","table":"table-2"},"674":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-104","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable   | Default        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | -------------- |\n| `maxConcurrency` | `CHOP_MAX_CONCURRENCY` | number of CPUs |","table":"table-2"},"675":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-105","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable | Default |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxQueue` | `CHOP_MAX_QUEUE`     | `64`    |","table":"table-2"},"676":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-106","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable   | Default    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxInputBytes` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_BYTES` | `52428800` |","table":"table-2"},"677":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-107","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable    | Default     |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | ----------- |\n| `maxInputPixels` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_PIXELS` | `120000000` |","table":"table-2"},"678":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-108","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxOutputDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_OUTPUT_DIMENSION` | `8192`  |","table":"table-2"},"679":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-109","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable         | Default |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxUpscaleDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_UPSCALE_DIMENSION` | `4096`  |","table":"table-2"},"680":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-110","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                     | Environment variable                                          | Default          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `jpegQuality`, `webpQuality`, `avifQuality` | `CHOP_JPEG_QUALITY`, `CHOP_WEBP_QUALITY`, `CHOP_AVIF_QUALITY` | `82`, `80`, `55` |","table":"table-2"},"681":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-111","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avif`  | `CHOP_AVIF`          | `true`  |","table":"table-2"},"682":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-112","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avifEffort` | `CHOP_AVIF_EFFORT`   | `4`     |","table":"table-2"},"683":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-113","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                    | Default |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `allowedWidths` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_WIDTHS` (comma separated) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"684":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-114","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable                                        | Default |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `origin` | `CHOP_ORIGIN` (an `https://` URL or `s3://bucket[/prefix]`) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"685":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-115","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                 | Environment variable                                  | Default          |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `originAllowHttp`, `originAllowPrivate` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` | `false`, `false` |","table":"table-2"},"686":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-116","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default     |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ----------- |\n| `s3Endpoint` | `CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`   | unset (AWS) |","table":"table-2"},"687":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-117","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable           | Default                                               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Region` | `CHOP_S3_REGION`, `AWS_REGION` | unset (required on AWS), `us-east-1` with an endpoint |","table":"table-2"},"688":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-118","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default                                 |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `s3PathStyle` | `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE` | `true` with an endpoint, `false` on AWS |","table":"table-2"},"689":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-119","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                                | Environment variable                                                                                      | Default |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `s3AccessKeyId`, `s3SecretAccessKey`, `s3SessionToken` | `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN`, with the `AWS_*` fallbacks | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"690":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-120","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `originAuth` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH`   | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"691":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-121","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                 | Environment variable                                 | Default         |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `originConnectTimeout`, `originTimeout` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONNECT_TIMEOUT`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_TIMEOUT` | `3000`, `10000` |","table":"table-2"},"692":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-122","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                            | Environment variable                           | Default   |\n| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | --------- |\n| `originConcurrency`, `originQueue` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_QUEUE` | `4`, `32` |","table":"table-2"},"693":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-123","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting        | Environment variable                   | Default |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `allowedHosts` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (comma separated) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"694":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-124","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable                           | Default                  |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `allowedInputFormats` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_INPUT_FORMATS` (comma separated) | `jpeg,png,gif,webp,avif` |","table":"table-2"},"695":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-125","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable                             | Default     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ----------- |\n| `autoFormats` | `CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS` (comma separated, or `none`) | `avif,webp` |","table":"table-2"},"696":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-126","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createHandler( settings? )` returns `( request ) => Promise< Response >` with `{ method, url, headers }` in and `{ status, headers, body }` out. It never throws for a request, never uses `node:http` and reports unexpected errors to an optional `onError`, risky settings to `onWarning` and the failures of an origin to `onOriginError` (R-API-1)."},"697":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-127","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createConfig()`, `configFromEnv( env )`, `configWarnings()`, the `Origin` interface with `createOrigin()`, `createLocalOrigin()` and `createHttpOrigin()`, `createS3Origin()`, `isBlockedAddress()`, `parseQuery()`, `createServer()`, the URL schemes `queryScheme` and `cloudflareScheme` with their `SCHEMES` registry and the `UrlScheme` type (`{ name, parse( url, options ) }`, where `parse` returns `{ segments, ops }`, with `url` set for a URL source, or `null`), and the other types are exported too (R-API-2, S-1)."},"698":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-128","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Errors are `ChopError` with a `code` from `CHOP_ERROR_CODES`, checked with `isChopError()` (R-API-3)."},"699":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html-129","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.0/reference.html#interfaces","content":"The CLI is `chop [--data <dir> | --origin <url or s3://bucket>] [--port <n>] [--host <address>] [--scheme <name>] [--help]`, with flags overriding `CHOP_*` variables. A flag replaces the other source from the environment (`--origin` over `CHOP_DATA_DIR`, `--data` over `CHOP_ORIGIN`). Warnings about risky settings and the reasons for refused origin requests go to the standard error. Exit codes are `0`, `1` for a failure and `2` for invalid options. `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` stop it gracefully, and `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG=1` prints one JSON line per request (R-CLI-1 to R-CLI-4)."},"700":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","type":"page","content":"Caching","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html"},"701":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Caching with nginx"},"702":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#cdn-and-caching","content":"CDN and caching"},"703":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Put an nginx cache in front of chop. Responses depend on the `Accept` header, and `Vary: Accept` alone makes nginx cache a separate copy for every distinct `Accept` string. Browsers send dozens of them, but chop only produces three variants of an image: AVIF, WebP and the source format. Collapse the header into those three buckets, use the bucket in the cache key, and send the same bucket upstream, so that the body in the cache always matches its key:"},"704":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"How it works:"},"705":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"A request without `image/avif` or `image/webp`, or with `q=0` for them, is the `original` bucket, and chop answers in the source format, as it would for any client without `Accept`."},"706":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"`image/*` and `*/*` don't select a bucket, the same as in chop, so a client that only accepts wildcards gets a format that it can display."},"707":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"A cached response always has the format that its bucket gets from chop, since the key and the upstream header come from the same variable."},"708":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Only the `Accept` header and the URL select a variant, so a purge needs three keys per URL, one for each bucket, like `$host$uri$is_args$args|avif`."},"709":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"chop's strong `ETag` and `If-None-Match` handling work through the cache, and the `ETag` of an image is the same for every `Accept` that gets the same bytes."},"710":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Cache only `200` and `404`, as the recipe does, and not `any`. A `502` or `504` means that the origin failed for a moment, and caching it would keep a broken image for as long as the `proxy_cache_valid` time. chop sends `Cache-Control: no-store` with every error, which nginx respects unless you ignore that header."},"711":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"For remote originals, `proxy_cache_lock on` makes concurrent requests for the same variant wait for one fetch, and `proxy_cache_min_uses 2` keeps one-off requests for unusual sizes out of the cache. See Securing remote origins."},"712":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"If you disable AVIF in chop (`CHOP_AVIF=false`), the `avif` bucket holds WebP, which is correct but caches the same image twice. Remove the AVIF line from the first `map` then."},"713":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#caching-with-nginx","content":"Pass the `Accept` buckets on to any CDN in front of nginx in the same way, with a custom cache key built from a normalized header, and see CDN and caching."},"714":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#cdn-and-caching","content":"The nginx recipe covers the cache next to chop. Responses depend on the `Accept` header, so the CDN must use it in the cache key, or at least whether it lists `image/avif` and `image/webp`. Every response has `Vary: Accept`, but many CDNs ignore `Vary` unless configured, and without it a cached AVIF can be sent to a browser that can't display it. Normalizing `Accept` at the edge to a small set of values (`image/avif,image/webp`, `image/webp` and none) keeps the number of cached variants low."},"715":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/caching.html#cdn-and-caching","content":"The responses are immutable by design (`Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000` by default and a strong `ETag`), so change the URL, for example with `?ver=3`, when an original changes, which also holds for a remote origin, since chop doesn't cache originals and doesn't look at the cache headers of the origin. Set `allowedWidths` to the widths of your `srcset` so that the server can't be used to generate unbounded variants, and put the server behind the CDN only. Use `/healthz` for health checks."},"716":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","type":"page","content":"CLI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html"},"717":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"The `chop` command runs the server. Give it a data directory or an origin, and a port:"},"718":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Argument             | Description                                                                                                       | Example                   |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `-d`, `--data <dir>` | Directory with the original images. Defaults to `CHOP_DATA_DIR`, then `/data`. Can't be combined with `--origin`. | `chop --data /srv/images` |","table":"table-0"},"719":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Argument               | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | Example                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `-o`, `--origin <url>` | Serve the images of this `https://` origin, like `https://uploads.example.com/base`, or of an S3 bucket, like `s3://my-bucket/uploads`, instead of a directory. Defaults to `CHOP_ORIGIN`. See Sources and S3 and S3-compatible storage. | `chop --origin https://uploads.example.com` |","table":"table-0"},"720":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Argument           | Description                                                                                    | Example        |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `-p`, `--port <n>` | Port to listen on. Defaults to `PORT`, then `CHOP_PORT`, then `8080`. Use `0` for a free port. | `chop -p 3000` |","table":"table-0"},"721":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Argument           | Description                                                    | Example                 |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `--host <address>` | Address to listen on. Defaults to `CHOP_HOST`, then `0.0.0.0`. | `chop --host 127.0.0.1` |","table":"table-0"},"722":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Argument          | Description                                                                                                                                         | Example                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `--scheme <name>` | URL scheme, `query` or `cloudflare`. Repeat it to enable several, tried in order, and list `query` last. Overrides `CHOP_SCHEMES`. See URL schemes. | `chop --scheme cloudflare --scheme query` |","table":"table-0"},"723":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Argument       | Description     | Example       |\n| -------------- | --------------- | ------------- |\n| `-h`, `--help` | Show the usage. | `chop --help` |","table":"table-0"},"724":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"Flags override environment variables, and `--origin` replaces `CHOP_DATA_DIR` while `--data` replaces `CHOP_ORIGIN`, so the flag works in an environment that sets the other one. Setting both a data directory and an origin is an invalid setting. The other settings are read from `CHOP_*` environment variables (see Settings), and a number or boolean that can't be parsed is reported with the name of the variable. Startup prints one line with the address and the data directory or origin, and a warning line on the standard error for each risky setting (`CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=*`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` and an S3 origin without credentials). When an origin refuses a request or fails, the reason is written to the standard error as `origin <code>: <reason>`, since the client only gets a plain `404`, `502` or `504`. `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG=1` prints one JSON line per request to the standard output, with `method`, `path`, `status`, `duration` (milliseconds) and `bytes`."},"725":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"The exit code is `0` after a clean shutdown, `1` when the server can't start (a missing data directory or a port that is in use), and `2` for invalid options or settings. On `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` the server stops accepting connections, closes idle ones, waits for running requests and exits with `0`."},"726":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","type":"page","content":"Configuration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html"},"727":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"Settings come from the `CHOP_*` environment variables of the command, from the options of `createConfig()`, or from a few command line flags. A number or boolean that can't be parsed is reported with the name of the variable, and a value that can't be used is an invalid setting."},"728":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable | Default | Description                                              |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dataDir` | `CHOP_DATA_DIR`      | `/data` | Directory with the originals, when there is no `origin`. |","table":"table-0"},"729":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable             | Default | Description                                                                      |\n| --------- | -------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `schemes` | `CHOP_SCHEMES` (comma separated) | `query` | Names of the URL schemes, tried in order. An unknown name is an invalid setting. |","table":"table-0"},"730":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default    | Description                          |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `maxAge` | `CHOP_MAX_AGE`       | `31536000` | Seconds in `Cache-Control: max-age`. |","table":"table-0"},"731":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable   | Default        | Description                        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `maxConcurrency` | `CHOP_MAX_CONCURRENCY` | number of CPUs | Images processed at the same time. |","table":"table-0"},"732":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                        |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `maxQueue` | `CHOP_MAX_QUEUE`     | `64`    | Requests that wait for a slot, in arrival order. More are a `503`. |","table":"table-0"},"733":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable   | Default    | Description                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------- |\n| `maxInputBytes` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_BYTES` | `52428800` | Largest original in bytes. |","table":"table-0"},"734":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable    | Default     | Description                                                  |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `maxInputPixels` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_PIXELS` | `120000000` | Largest original in pixels, which stops decompression bombs. |","table":"table-0"},"735":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default | Description                     |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `maxOutputDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_OUTPUT_DIMENSION` | `8192`  | Largest output width or height. |","table":"table-0"},"736":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable         | Default | Description                                              |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `maxUpscaleDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_UPSCALE_DIMENSION` | `4096`  | Largest long side of an enlarged image with `upscale=1`. |","table":"table-0"},"737":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default | Description           |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `jpegQuality` | `CHOP_JPEG_QUALITY`  | `82`    | Default JPEG quality. |","table":"table-0"},"738":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default | Description                 |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | --------------------------- |\n| `webpQuality` | `CHOP_WEBP_QUALITY`  | `80`    | Default lossy WebP quality. |","table":"table-0"},"739":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default | Description           |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `avifQuality` | `CHOP_AVIF_QUALITY`  | `55`    | Default AVIF quality. |","table":"table-0"},"740":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                                                                              |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `avif`  | `CHOP_AVIF`          | `true`  | Whether AVIF output is enabled. `false` removes `avif` from `autoFormats`, and doesn't affect an explicit `format=avif`. |","table":"table-0"},"741":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default | Description                                     |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `avifEffort` | `CHOP_AVIF_EFFORT`   | `4`     | AVIF encoder effort from 0 (fast) to 9 (small). |","table":"table-0"},"742":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                    | Default | Description                                                      |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedWidths` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_WIDTHS` (comma separated) | unset   | When set, the output width of every request must be in the list. |","table":"table-0"},"743":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `origin` | `CHOP_ORIGIN`        | unset   | Base URL that plain paths are appended to, instead of the data directory, or `s3://bucket[/prefix]` for an S3 bucket. Can't be combined with an explicit `dataDir`. |","table":"table-0"},"744":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting           | Environment variable     | Default | Description                                         |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originAllowHttp` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP` | `false` | Allow `http://` for the origin and for URL sources. |","table":"table-0"},"745":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default | Description                                                                                             |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originAllowPrivate` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` | `false` | Allow the configured origin at a loopback, private or link-local address. Never applies to URL sources. |","table":"table-0"},"746":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                  |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `originAuth` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH`   | unset   | `Authorization` header value for the configured origin only. |","table":"table-0"},"747":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default | Description                                                                  |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Endpoint` | `CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`   | unset   | Base URL of an S3-compatible service for an `s3://` origin. Unset means AWS. |","table":"table-0"},"748":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable           | Default | Description                                                                       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Region` | `CHOP_S3_REGION`, `AWS_REGION` | unset   | Region to sign for. Required on AWS, `us-east-1` with an endpoint, `auto` for R2. |","table":"table-0"},"749":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default                                 | Description                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3PathStyle` | `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE` | `true` with an endpoint, `false` on AWS | Put the bucket in the path instead of the host. Buckets with dots on AWS are always path-style. |","table":"table-0"},"750":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                         | Default | Description                                                   |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3AccessKeyId` | `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | unset   | Access key. Without a key and a secret requests are unsigned. |","table":"table-0"},"751":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting             | Environment variable                                 | Default | Description                                               |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3SecretAccessKey` | `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | unset   | Secret of the access key. Environment only, never logged. |","table":"table-0"},"752":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable                         | Default | Description                                                                            |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3SessionToken` | `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN`, `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` | unset   | Token of temporary credentials, which isn't refreshed. Environment only, never logged. |","table":"table-0"},"753":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting                | Environment variable          | Default | Description                                             |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originConnectTimeout` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONNECT_TIMEOUT` | `3000`  | Milliseconds to connect, including TLS, before a `504`. |","table":"table-0"},"754":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable  | Default | Description                                         |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originTimeout` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_TIMEOUT` | `10000` | Milliseconds for the whole download before a `504`. |","table":"table-0"},"755":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting             | Environment variable      | Default | Description                                                  |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `originConcurrency` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY` | `4`     | Downloads at the same time, outside of the processing slots. |","table":"table-0"},"756":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default | Description                                       |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originQueue` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_QUEUE`  | `32`    | Downloads that wait for a slot. More are a `503`. |","table":"table-0"},"757":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting        | Environment variable                   | Default | Description                                                                                               |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedHosts` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (comma separated) | unset   | Hosts that URL sources may name: `host`, `*.example.com`, `host:port` or `*`. Unset means no URL sources. |","table":"table-0"},"758":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable                           | Default                  | Description                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedInputFormats` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_INPUT_FORMATS` (comma separated) | `jpeg,png,gif,webp,avif` | The formats of the originals that are processed (`jpeg` or `jpg`, `png`, `gif`, `webp`, `avif`). Others are a `415`. An empty list or an unknown name is an invalid setting. |","table":"table-0"},"759":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/configuration.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable                             | Default     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `autoFormats` | `CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS` (comma separated, or `none`) | `avif,webp` | The formats that `format=auto` can negotiate, in order of preference (`avif`, `webp`). An empty list (`none` in the environment) disables the upgrades. Unknown or repeated names are an invalid setting. |","table":"table-0"},"760":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html","type":"page","content":"Development","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html"},"761":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html#license","content":"License"},"762":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html","content":"Run these from the repository root:"},"763":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html","content":"The source runs directly with Node's type stripping through the `wpelevator-source` export condition, and `dist` is only for publishing. Tests are co-located `*.test.ts` files that use `node:test`, and each test name starts with the requirement ID of the specification that it covers, like `R-FMT-3`. `src/test-fixtures.ts` creates temporary data directories and generates the images with sharp, so there are no binary fixtures."},"764":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/development.html#license","content":"MIT. chop was implemented from a written behavior specification and the repository conventions, without reference to the source code of any other image server. The reference summarizes that behavior."},"765":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","type":"page","content":"Formats and quality","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html"},"766":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#restricting-formats","content":"Restricting formats"},"767":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"Quality and size"},"768":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"Choices where the specification is silent"},"769":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","content":"With `format=auto` (the default), the format is chosen from the `Accept` header for a still image among the formats of `autoFormats` (`avif,webp` by default): AVIF if it's listed and the output is lossy, or WebP if it's listed and the output fits the 16383 pixel limit of WebP, otherwise the fallback format. When the client lists both, the format with the highest `q` is used, and the earlier format of `autoFormats` wins a tie. Browsers send no `q` for image types, so they get the first format of `autoFormats` that they accept, as before, while a header like `image/avif;q=0.5,image/webp` now gives WebP. The fallback is GIF for a GIF source, PNG for lossless or transparent output, and JPEG otherwise."},"770":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","content":"The header is parsed per RFC 9110, ignoring whitespace and case, and a type with `q=0` is not accepted. `image/*` and `*/*` never make AVIF or WebP acceptable: only a listed `image/avif` or `image/webp` does, so clients that don't list them get a format that they can display. An explicit `format` is used even if `Accept` doesn't list it, and it isn't restricted by `autoFormats`, which only governs the negotiation."},"771":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","content":"| Source                 | `Accept` lists `image/avif` and `image/webp` | `Accept` lists `image/webp` | No `Accept`, or `image/*`    |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| JPEG, lossy WebP, AVIF | AVIF                                         | WebP                        | JPEG (PNG with transparency) |","table":"table-0"},"772":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","content":"| Source             | `Accept` lists `image/avif` and `image/webp` | `Accept` lists `image/webp` | No `Accept`, or `image/*` |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| PNG, lossless WebP | Lossless WebP                                | Lossless WebP               | PNG                       |","table":"table-0"},"773":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","content":"| Source | `Accept` lists `image/avif` and `image/webp` | `Accept` lists `image/webp` | No `Accept`, or `image/*` |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| GIF    | Lossless WebP                                | Lossless WebP               | GIF                       |","table":"table-0"},"774":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","content":"| Source               | `Accept` lists `image/avif` and `image/webp` | `Accept` lists `image/webp` | No `Accept`, or `image/*` |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Animated GIF or WebP | Animated WebP                                | Animated WebP               | GIF                       |","table":"table-0"},"775":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","content":"PNG, GIF and lossless WebP sources stay lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given. Lossy output of a lossless source is AVIF, WebP or a palette PNG. A JPEG, lossy WebP or AVIF source always gives lossy output. An animated source is never AVIF. With an explicit format that can't hold the image (JPEG for an image with transparency, or any format other than WebP and GIF for an animation), transparency is flattened onto white and only the first frame is kept. Sources are detected from the content, not the extension. Other content is a `415` and an unreadable or corrupt file is a `422`."},"776":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","content":"Every successful response has `Vary: Accept`, also when it ends up in the source format."},"777":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#restricting-formats","content":"`CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS=webp` never negotiates AVIF, which avoids its encode cost. `CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS=none` disables all upgrades, so `auto` always gives the fallback format. `CHOP_AVIF=false` is a shorthand that removes `avif` from the list, also when `autoFormats` lists it. An explicit `format=avif` still works with either."},"778":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#restricting-formats","content":"`CHOP_ALLOWED_INPUT_FORMATS=jpeg,png,webp` is for a site that only serves those. The format is detected from the content of the file, never the extension, and `jpg` is accepted as an alias of `jpeg`. A source in another format is a `415` with the message of any unsupported file, which doesn't tell which formats are allowed. It's rejected after the header is read and before any pixel is decoded or processed."},"779":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"`quality` is raised to 20 when it's lower, for lossy encoders. `quality=100` on WebP is lossless WebP."},"780":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"Without `quality` the defaults are JPEG 82, WebP 80 and AVIF 55 (configurable). A palette PNG uses `quality` or 80. PNG output of a lossless source is lossless with maximum compression."},"781":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"A JPEG source isn't re-encoded with a higher quality than it has: the quality of the source is estimated from its luminance quantization table, and the default is lowered to it when it's lower."},"782":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"When a request changes nothing about the pixels (no `crop`, size or `lb`, and no orientation to apply), the output format equals the source format and the source has no metadata that `strip` would remove, the original bytes are sent if the re-encoded image isn't smaller. With `strip=none` an untouched request in the source format sends the original bytes without re-encoding."},"783":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"Pixel values are never converted to another color space because of `strip`: the ICC profile is kept or dropped, and the pixels stay as they are. CMYK sources are always converted to sRGB."},"784":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#quality-and-size","content":"Responses have `X-Bytes-Saved` when the output is smaller than the original."},"785":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"An explicit `quality` or `lossy=1` turns off the `strip=none` shortcut that sends the original bytes, because the client asked for a re-encoding. The \"never larger\" check still applies."},"786":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The source quality cap of a JPEG applies when `quality` is absent. An explicit `quality` is used as given (with the floor of 20)."},"787":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"Transparency means that the source has an alpha channel, even if every pixel is opaque."},"788":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"An explicit `format=png` is lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given, also for a JPEG source. An explicit `format=avif` or `format=jpeg` is always lossy."},"789":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"`contrast`, `brightness` and `filter` arguments are not parsed at all, so a malformed value of one of them is not an error."},"790":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"Repeated arguments use the first value. Crop numbers are non-negative and `zoom` may have up to three decimals."},"791":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"An empty segment in the path (`//` or a trailing slash) is a `400`."},"792":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"With `strip=none`, EXIF, XMP, IPTC and the profile are kept when the encoder can write them. CMYK sources only keep EXIF and XMP."},"793":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The `Accept` entries that have an invalid `q` are ignored. A listed type counts as accepted only if every entry of it has `q` above 0."},"794":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The encoders use the sharp defaults, except for progressive JPEG, WebP `effort` 4 and PNG `compressionLevel` 9."},"795":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"`maxConcurrency` defaults to the number of CPUs and `CHOP_PORT`, `CHOP_HOST` and `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG` are CLI-only variables."},"796":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"A first path segment of `http:` or `https:` always starts a URL source, so a directory with that name can't be addressed by a plain path, and with an empty allow-list it is a `404`."},"797":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The credentials of `CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH` are never sent to a URL source, not even to the host of the configured origin. A URL source of that host is fetched like any other, with the address checks."},"798":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"`*` allows every host on the default ports, and a custom port needs its own entry. An allow-list entry is a name or an IPv4 address and not an IPv6 literal, so only `*` allows an IPv6 literal, and the address checks still apply to it."},"799":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-33","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"An empty segment inside a URL source (`//` in its path) is sent to the origin as it is, while it's a `400` in a plain path."},"800":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-34","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"The `Accept` header of the client is not forwarded to the origin, so the origin can't vary its answer, and the bytes of an original don't depend on who asked."},"801":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html-35","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/formats.html#choices-where-the-specification-is-silent","content":"A `HEAD` request downloads and processes the original like a `GET`, since it has the same headers, including `Content-Length`, which depend on the output bytes. Don't forward `HEAD` requests for remote originals or URL sources from a proxy unless you need them, since each one costs a download and a conversion."},"802":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","type":"page","content":"chop","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html"},"803":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","content":"An HTTP image server for responsive images, with AVIF and WebP chosen from the Accept header."},"804":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#install","content":"Install"},"805":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#start-the-server","content":"Start the server"},"806":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Guides"},"807":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","content":"`@wpelevator/chop` is an HTTP image server for responsive images. It serves resized, converted and optimized copies of originals from a local data directory, from an HTTP(S) origin or from an S3 bucket, and chooses AVIF, WebP or the original format from the `Accept` header of each request. It's built on sharp, which is its only runtime dependency, and works as a command line server or as a library with a request handler that doesn't depend on an HTTP framework."},"808":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","content":"It's read-only: it never writes to the data directory or any other directory. With a data directory, which is the default, it makes no network requests. Remote originals are opt-in, are fetched with strict safeguards, and only from the configured origin or from hosts that you list. Authentication, URL signing and per-client rate limits are left to a CDN or a reverse proxy. The behavior is summarized in the reference."},"809":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#install","content":"Requires Node.js 22.12 or later. There is also a container image, `ghcr.io/wpelevator/chop`, described in the chop Docker README."},"810":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#start-the-server","content":"Then request `http://localhost:8080/2026/05/photo.jpg?w=300` to get `<data>/2026/05/photo.jpg` at 300 pixels wide, as AVIF or WebP when the `Accept` header of the client lists them. The CLI page lists the options and exit codes."},"811":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"CLI"},"812":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Requests and query arguments"},"813":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"URL schemes"},"814":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Sources: data directory, HTTP origin and URL sources"},"815":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"S3 and S3-compatible storage"},"816":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Securing remote origins"},"817":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Formats and quality"},"818":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Responses and errors"},"819":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Caching with nginx and a CDN"},"820":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Configuration"},"821":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Library API"},"822":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Development"},"823":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/index.html#guides","content":"Reference"},"824":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","type":"page","content":"Library API","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html"},"825":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"The request handler doesn't depend on an HTTP framework, so it can run in a `node:http` server, a serverless function or a test. Install the package as described in the overview."},"826":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                       | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createHandler( settings? )` | Returns `( request ) => Promise< Response >`. The request is `{ method, url, headers }`, where `url` is the path and query string and `headers` is a plain object with lower-case names. The response is `{ status, headers, body }` with a `Buffer` body. It doesn't depend on `node:http`, never throws for a request (errors become responses) and takes optional callbacks, because the library never logs: `onError( error )` for unexpected errors, `onWarning( message )` for each risky setting (like `allowedHosts: [ '*' ]`) when the handler is created, and `onOriginError( error )` for a refused or failed origin, where `error.detail` says why and has no credentials. Give it the same settings that you give `createConfig()`: a settings object that `createConfig()` returned has a `dataDir`, which counts as set. |","table":"table-0"},"827":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                                                     | Description                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createConfig( overrides? )`, `configWarnings( settings )` | Settings with defaults, checked, and the list of warnings for the risky settings in them. Throws a `ChopError` with `ERR_INVALID_SETTING` for a value that can't be used. |","table":"table-0"},"828":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                 | Description                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `configFromEnv( env )` | The settings that the `CHOP_*` variables in an environment object set. It doesn't read `process`. |","table":"table-0"},"829":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                       | Description                                       |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parseQuery( searchParams )` | Parses a `URLSearchParams` into typed operations. |","table":"table-0"},"830":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                                                    | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `queryScheme`, `cloudflareScheme`, `SCHEMES`, `UrlScheme` | The built-in URL schemes, the registry of them by name, and the type of a scheme: `{ name, parse( url, options ) }`, where `parse` returns `{ segments, ops }`, with `url` set instead of `segments` for a URL source, or `null` for a URL that it doesn't recognize. `options.urlSources` tells whether URL sources are enabled. |","table":"table-0"},"831":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                                                                            | Description                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createOrigin( settings )`, `createLocalOrigin()`, `createHttpOrigin()`, `Origin` | The sources of originals: an `Origin` has `open( reference )`, which finds an original and returns its size and a `read()` for its bytes. The HTTP origin does the downloads and their checks. |","table":"table-0"},"832":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                                                                                        | Description                                                                          |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `isBlockedAddress( address )`, `createBlockList()`, `parseAllowedHosts()`, `parseSourceUrl()` | The building blocks of the safeguards, for code that wants to apply the same checks. |","table":"table-0"},"833":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                      | Description                                                                                        |\n| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createServer( settings? )` | A `node:http` server around the handler, with an `onResponse( summary )` callback for access logs. |","table":"table-0"},"834":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export            | Description                                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `run( args, io )` | The command, which returns an exit code. `io` has `stdout`, `stderr`, `env`, `cwd` and `signals`, all replaceable in tests. |","table":"table-0"},"835":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Export                                                                       | Description                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ChopError`, `isChopError( value )`, `CHOP_ERROR_CODES`, `CHOP_ERROR_STATUS` | Errors with a `code`. `isChopError` checks the code instead of `instanceof`. |","table":"table-0"},"836":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code            | HTTP status |\n| --------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_INVALID_REQUEST` | 400         |","table":"table-1"},"837":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code      | HTTP status |\n| --------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_NOT_FOUND` | 404         |","table":"table-1"},"838":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code               | HTTP status |\n| ------------------------ | ----------- |\n| `ERR_METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED` | 405         |","table":"table-1"},"839":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code            | HTTP status |\n| --------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_INPUT_TOO_LARGE` | 413         |","table":"table-1"},"840":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code             | HTTP status |\n| ---------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE` | 415         |","table":"table-1"},"841":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code             | HTTP status |\n| ---------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_UNREADABLE_IMAGE` | 422         |","table":"table-1"},"842":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code     | HTTP status |\n| -------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_UPSTREAM` | 502         |","table":"table-1"},"843":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code             | HTTP status |\n| ---------------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT` | 504         |","table":"table-1"},"844":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code | HTTP status |\n| ---------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_BUSY` | 503         |","table":"table-1"},"845":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code            | HTTP status                                       |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ERR_INVALID_SETTING` | 500 (reported by the CLI at startup, exit code 2) |","table":"table-1"},"846":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/library.html","content":"| Error code     | HTTP status |\n| -------------- | ----------- |\n| `ERR_INTERNAL` | 500         |","table":"table-1"},"847":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"page","content":"Reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html"},"848":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#requests","content":"Requests"},"849":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"Sources"},"850":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"S3 origin"},"851":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Query scheme arguments"},"852":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"URL schemes"},"853":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"`cloudflare`"},"854":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"Output format"},"855":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"Quality and size"},"856":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#responses","content":"Responses"},"857":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#caching","content":"Caching"},"858":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#limits","content":"Limits"},"859":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"Settings"},"860":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Interfaces"},"861":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","content":"How chop behaves, in short. The guides describe each area in more detail: requests, sources, URL schemes, formats and quality, responses and configuration. The IDs in parentheses, like `R-OP-8`, are what the tests refer to in their names. chop is MIT licensed and was implemented from a written behavior specification and the repository conventions, without reference to the source code of any other image server."},"862":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#requests","content":"`GET` and `HEAD` are answered, other methods get `405` with `Allow: GET, HEAD` (R-REQ-1)."},"863":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#requests","content":"The path selects the original under the data directory or the configured origin, and a URL scheme selects the operations (R-REQ-2, S-1). Unknown arguments are ignored, so cache busters like `ver=3` are harmless."},"864":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#requests","content":"`/healthz` answers `200 ok` without touching the data directory or the origin (R-REQ-3)."},"865":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#requests","content":"The same URL and `Accept` header give the same bytes (R-REQ-4)."},"866":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#requests","content":"Path segments are percent-decoded once. `.`, `..`, empty segments and segments with `/`, `\\` or a NUL byte are a `400`, and a broken escape is a `400` (R-PATH-1). This is for plain paths: in a URL source the embedded URL path is sent to the origin as written, so `//` in it is allowed, but dot segments and broken escapes are still a `400` (R-SRC-14)."},"867":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#requests","content":"The real path, with symbolic links resolved, must be inside the real data directory. A missing file, a directory and an escape are all the same `404` (R-PATH-2)."},"868":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#requests","content":"A file over `maxInputBytes` is a `413`, checked before the read and again after it (R-PATH-3). These checks are for the local data directory."},"869":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"Where the original comes from. The data directory is the default and its behavior is the one above."},"870":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"Plain paths go to the configured origin (`origin`, `CHOP_ORIGIN`) when there is one, and to the data directory when there isn't. A URL source goes to the HTTP fetcher with the allow-list (R-SRC-1)."},"871":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"The URL of a plain path is the origin base URL, its path without a trailing slash and the path segments, each percent-encoded again, so a segment can't change the host, the port, the query string or the path of the base (R-SRC-2)."},"872":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"The origin is `https://`, or `http://` with `originAllowHttp`, without user information, a query string or a fragment, and not an IP literal in a blocked range unless `originAllowPrivate` is set. The same scheme rule applies to URL sources, and a bad origin is an invalid setting at startup (R-SRC-3)."},"873":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"Before connecting, the address literal in the URL is checked, or the name is resolved, every address is checked and the socket only gets the addresses that were checked. If any address is blocked nothing is connected, and the connection is made to one of the addresses that were checked and not to a second DNS answer, so DNS rebinding can't swap the address. Blocked addresses are loopback, unspecified, private, link-local (including `169.254.169.254`), carrier-grade NAT, documentation, multicast and reserved ranges for IPv4 and IPv6, with IPv4-mapped and NAT64 addresses checked as the IPv4 address that they contain, 6to4 and Teredo blocked, and anything that can't be parsed blocked (R-SRC-4)."},"874":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"Redirects are not followed, and a `3xx` is a `502` (R-SRC-5)."},"875":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"The request is a `GET` with `Accept: image/*`, `Accept-Encoding: identity` and `User-Agent: chop`, and without any header of the client. `originAuth` is sent as `Authorization` to the configured origin only. A response with a `Content-Encoding` is a `502` (R-SRC-6)."},"876":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-28","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"The body is limited to `maxInputBytes` while it is read, whether or not there is a `Content-Length`, and a `Content-Length` over the limit is a `413` before the body is read (R-SRC-7)."},"877":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-29","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"Connecting must finish within `originConnectTimeout` and the whole download within `originTimeout`, or the answer is a `504`. Upstream failures, a `5xx` or other unexpected status, a redirect and a body that ends early are a `502`, and the body of a response that is not a `200` is dropped without being read. A name that can't be resolved is a `502` for the configured origin, so the operator sees a broken origin, and a plain `404` for a URL source, so that a client can't tell which names exist (R-SRC-8)."},"878":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-30","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"An upstream `404` or `410`, an upstream `401`, `403` or `407`, a URL source that is not allowed and a blocked destination are all the same plain `404`. The reason is only given to the `onOriginError` callback, which the command writes to the standard error, and it is made of the host, a status code or an error code and never an error message (R-SRC-9)."},"879":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-31","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"The type is found from the content, and the `Content-Type` of the origin is not used (R-SRC-10)."},"880":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-32","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"The headers of the origin, like `Cache-Control` and `ETag`, don't change the response, and the original is not cached (R-SRC-11)."},"881":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-33","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"A `HEAD` request downloads and processes the original like a `GET`, since it must have the same headers, including `Content-Length` (R-REQ-1), so a proxy should not forward `HEAD` requests for remote originals unless it needs them (R-SRC-12)."},"882":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-34","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"At most `originConcurrency` downloads run at once and `originQueue` more wait, outside of the processing slots, and a full queue is a `503` with `Retry-After: 1` (R-SRC-12)."},"883":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-35","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"A URL source is a URL after `/` in the `query` scheme or after the options in the `cloudflare` scheme, written `https://host/path`, `https:/host/path` or `https%3A//host/path`. It is a `404` unless `allowedHosts` is not empty and names its host, and the match is on the lower case host without a trailing dot, and the port (R-SRC-13)."},"884":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-36","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"A URL source with user information, a fragment, or a query string of its own (a `400` in the `cloudflare` scheme, and not possible in the `query` scheme where the query is chop's arguments) is a `400`, and dot segments are a `400` as for any path. A port other than the default of the scheme must be in the entry (R-SRC-14)."},"885":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-37","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"`allowedHosts` entries are `host`, `*.example.com` (subdomains on a dot boundary, not the apex), either with `:port`, or `*` for every host on the default ports. `*` can't be mixed with other entries, and it is a warning at startup. Even with `*` everything else of this section applies, and `originAllowPrivate` never applies to a URL source (R-SRC-15)."},"886":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-38","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#sources","content":"A data directory that is set explicitly and an origin together are an invalid setting (R-SRC-16)."},"887":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-39","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`origin` set to `s3://bucket[/prefix]` reads the originals from an S3 bucket or an S3-compatible service. It is the HTTP origin of the section above for requests of the bucket, with signed requests, and every rule of that section applies unless it is changed here."},"888":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-40","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`origin` is parsed into a bucket and a prefix: the bucket has 3 to 63 lower case letters, digits, dots and hyphens and isn't an IP address, and the prefix can't have empty, `.` or `..` segments, a query string or a fragment. `http://` and `https://` origins are unchanged, and a data directory that is set explicitly together with an `s3://` origin is an invalid setting (R-S3-1)."},"889":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-41","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The region is `s3Region` (`CHOP_S3_REGION`, then `AWS_REGION`). On AWS, which is without `s3Endpoint`, it is required and a missing one is an invalid setting at startup. With an endpoint it defaults to `us-east-1`, and `auto` is allowed for R2 (R-S3-2)."},"890":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-42","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"On AWS the bucket is in the host, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`, unless `s3PathStyle` is true or the bucket name has dots, which use `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`. A custom endpoint is `endpoint/bucket/key` unless `s3PathStyle` is false, which uses `bucket.endpoint-host`. The endpoint is checked like the origin: https, or http with `originAllowHttp`, no user information, query string or fragment, and no blocked address without `originAllowPrivate` (R-S3-3)."},"891":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-43","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"With `s3AccessKeyId` and `s3SecretAccessKey` every request to the bucket is signed with AWS Signature Version 4 with a fresh date, and the signed host is the `Host` header that is sent, with its port. A session token is sent and signed as `x-amz-security-token`. Without a key and a secret requests are unsigned and there is a warning at startup, and a key without a secret, a secret without a key and a token alone are invalid settings (R-S3-4)."},"892":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-44","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The key is the prefix and the validated segments of the path, and each segment is percent-encoded once, keeping only `A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~`, and sent exactly as it is signed. The path is not normalized (R-S3-5)."},"893":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-45","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The errors are those of the HTTP origin: `404` and `403` from the bucket are a plain `404`, a `5xx`, a network or TLS error and a redirect are a `502`, a timeout is a `504`, and an object over `maxInputBytes` is a `413` (R-S3-6)."},"894":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-46","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"For the operator only, the first 2048 bytes of the body of an error from the bucket are read (for at most two seconds), and the `<Code>` of the XML, like `SignatureDoesNotMatch`, `AccessDenied`, `RequestTimeTooSkewed`, `ExpiredToken` or `InvalidAccessKeyId`, is given to `onOriginError` in the detail of the error. `NoSuchKey` is not reported, since it is an ordinary miss. A `301` or `307` is a `502` with the detail `bucket is in another region (check CHOP_S3_REGION)` and isn't followed. The body of an error of any other origin is still dropped without being read (R-S3-7)."},"895":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-47","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"Requests for URL sources are never signed and never get the credentials, and the URL sources of `allowedHosts` keep working (R-S3-8)."},"896":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-48","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"The secret key and the session token are only read from the environment by the command, and are not in any error message, warning or log line (R-S3-9)."},"897":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-49","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#s3-origin","content":"`CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`, `CHOP_S3_REGION`, `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE`, `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` and `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN` are read, with `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` and `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` as the fallbacks, and `--origin s3://bucket` works. Credentials are read once at startup and aren't refreshed (R-S3-10)."},"898":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-50","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"This is the default scheme, named `query`. All arguments are optional, and a malformed value of a known argument is a `400` that names it."},"899":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-51","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `w`, `h` | Width or height in pixels. With one, scale to it. With both, fit inside the box without cropping or padding (R-OP-2). |","table":"table-0"},"900":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-52","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                           |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit=w,h` | The same as `w` and `h` together, and it wins over them (R-OP-3). |","table":"table-0"},"901":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-53","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument     | Meaning                                                                    |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resize=w,h` | Cover the box and crop to exactly `w` by `h`. It wins over `fit` (R-OP-4). |","table":"table-0"},"902":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-54","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                                             |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | Where `resize` crops: `center` (default), `north`, `south`, `east`, `west` or `attention` (R-OP-5). |","table":"table-0"},"903":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-55","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument       | Meaning                                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `crop=x,y,w,h` | A region of the oriented original, before scaling. Numbers are percentages, or pixels with a `px` suffix. The region is clipped to the image (R-OP-6). |","table":"table-0"},"904":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-56","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument         | Meaning                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lb=w,h[,color]` | Fit inside the box and pad to exactly `w` by `h`. `color` is 3 or 6 hex digits, default `ffffff` (R-OP-7). |","table":"table-0"},"905":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-57","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `zoom`   | Device pixel ratio from 1 to 10, which multiplies the sizes (R-OP-9). |","table":"table-0"},"906":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-58","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument    | Meaning                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `upscale=1` | Allow enlarging, up to `maxUpscaleDimension` (R-OP-8). |","table":"table-0"},"907":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-59","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                                                   |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `quality` | 1 to 100, with values below 20 raised to 20 for lossy encoders (R-QLT-1). |","table":"table-0"},"908":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-60","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                             |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `auto` (default), `jpeg`, `png`, `webp`, `avif` or `gif` (R-FMT-2). |","table":"table-0"},"909":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-61","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument  | Meaning                                            |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lossy=1` | Allow lossy output for lossless sources (R-QLT-5). |","table":"table-0"},"910":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-62","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"| Argument | Meaning                                                                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `strip`  | `metadata` (default, keeps the ICC profile), `all` or `none` (R-QLT-6). |","table":"table-0"},"911":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-63","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Operations run in a fixed order, whatever the order in the URL: orientation, `crop`, size, `lb`, then encoding. Sizes always refer to the displayed (oriented) image (R-OP-1)."},"912":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-64","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Without `upscale=1` nothing is enlarged: sizes clamp to the original, `resize` crops at the largest size with the requested aspect ratio, and `lb` pads without enlarging (R-OP-8). The output can't exceed `maxOutputDimension` (R-OP-12)."},"913":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-65","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#query-scheme-arguments","content":"Animated sources keep all frames for `crop` and sizes. `lb` and `gravity=attention` are ignored for them (R-OP-13). Image adjustments (R-OP-10) and filters (R-OP-11) aren't supported, and their arguments are ignored."},"914":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-66","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme turns a URL into the path of the original and the operations. All the schemes produce the same operations, so every scheme gets the same negotiation, limits and path safety."},"915":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-67","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Schemes are tried in the configured order, and the first one that recognizes the URL wins. The default is `query` only (S-1). The `query` scheme recognizes every URL, so it has to be listed last when it's enabled with others. The `cloudflare` scheme only recognizes URLs that start with `/cdn-cgi/image/`."},"916":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-68","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme's path segments go through the same checks as any other path, so no scheme can read outside the data directory (S-2)."},"917":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-69","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A URL that no enabled scheme recognizes is a `404` (S-3)."},"918":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-70","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"A scheme ignores the options that chop doesn't support, and a malformed value of one that it supports is a `400` (S-4)."},"919":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-71","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#url-schemes","content":"Different schemes that give the same operations give the same bytes and `ETag` (S-5)."},"920":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-72","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"The `/cdn-cgi/image/<options>/<path>` form of Cloudflare Image Resizing, with comma separated `name=value` options."},"921":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-73","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option            | Maps to         |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `width`, `height` | `w`, `h` (S-6). |","table":"table-1"},"922":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-74","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit`  | `scale-down` (default) is `w`/`h` that never enlarges, `contain` is the same with `upscale`, `cover` is `resize` with `upscale`, `crop` is `resize`, and `pad` is `lb` with `upscale` (S-7). |","table":"table-1"},"923":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-75","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | `left`, `right`, `top`, `bottom` are `west`, `east`, `north`, `south`, and `auto` and `face` are `attention`. Coordinates like `0.5x0.3` are ignored (S-8). |","table":"table-1"},"924":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-76","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to          |\n| --------- | ---------------- |\n| `quality` | `quality` (S-9). |","table":"table-1"},"925":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-77","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option   | Maps to                                                                                                |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `format` | `auto`, `avif`, `webp`, `jpeg`, `png`, `gif`, and `baseline-jpeg` as `jpeg`. `json` is a `400` (S-10). |","table":"table-1"},"926":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-78","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to        |\n| ------ | -------------- |\n| `dpr`  | `zoom` (S-11). |","table":"table-1"},"927":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-79","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option     | Maps to                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `keep` is `strip=none`, `copyright` is `strip=metadata`, `none` is `strip=all` (S-12). |","table":"table-1"},"928":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-80","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option       | Maps to                                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `background` | The `lb` color for `fit=pad`, as hex digits (S-13). |","table":"table-1"},"929":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-81","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#cloudflare","content":"Other Cloudflare options, like `trim`, `rotate`, `blur`, `sharpen` and `onerror`, are ignored. A source that starts with `http://` or `https://` is a URL source (see Sources) and is a `404` without `allowedHosts`."},"930":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-82","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"`Accept` is parsed per RFC 9110. Only a listed `image/avif` or `image/webp` makes those formats acceptable, so `image/*` and `*/*` don't (R-FMT-1)."},"931":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-83","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"An explicit `format` is used even when `Accept` doesn't list it. Transparency is flattened onto white for formats that can't hold it (R-FMT-2)."},"932":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-84","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"With `auto`, a still image is the negotiated format from `autoFormats` (R-FMT-10): AVIF if the output is lossy, or WebP if the output is within its size limit. Without an accepted candidate it is the fallback format: GIF for GIF sources, PNG for lossless or transparent output, and JPEG otherwise (R-FMT-3)."},"933":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-85","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"An animated source becomes an animated WebP if accepted and in `autoFormats`, otherwise a GIF, and never AVIF (R-FMT-4)."},"934":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-86","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"PNG, GIF and lossless WebP sources stay lossless unless `lossy=1` or a `quality` below 100 is given (R-FMT-5). JPEG, lossy WebP and AVIF sources produce lossy output (R-FMT-6)."},"935":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-87","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"Every response that depends on `Accept` has `Vary: Accept` (R-FMT-7)."},"936":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-88","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP and AVIF are read, detected from the content. Other content is a `415`, and unreadable or corrupt files are a `422` (R-FMT-8)."},"937":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-89","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"A source whose detected format isn't in `allowedInputFormats` is a `415` with the same message as other unsupported content, which doesn't tell which formats are allowed. The check follows the header detection and comes before any pixel decoding or processing (R-FMT-9)."},"938":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-90","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#output-format","content":"`autoFormats` lists the formats (`avif`, `webp`) that `auto` can negotiate, in order of preference. Among the listed formats that `Accept` lists with `q` above 0 (and that pass the checks of R-FMT-3), the one with the highest `q` is used, and the earlier entry of `autoFormats` wins a tie. An empty list disables the upgrades. An explicit `format` is not restricted by `autoFormats`, and `avif: false` removes AVIF from the list (R-FMT-10)."},"939":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-91","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"The defaults are JPEG 82, WebP 80 and AVIF 55, lowered to the estimated quality of a JPEG source, so that a recompressed JPEG never gets a higher quality than it has. The estimate compares the file's luminance quantization table with the standard table scaled for each quality. An explicit `quality` is used as given (R-QLT-2, R-QLT-3)."},"940":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-92","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#quality-and-size","content":"A request that changes nothing about the pixels and keeps the source format sends the original bytes when the re-encoded image isn't smaller, and with `strip=none` it always sends them (R-QLT-4)."},"941":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-93","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#responses","content":"`200` has the output `Content-Type`, `Content-Length`, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=<maxAge>`, `Vary: Accept`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a strong SHA-256 `ETag` (R-RES-1). `X-Bytes-Saved` appears when the output is smaller than the original (R-RES-3)."},"942":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-94","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#responses","content":"`If-None-Match` that matches, including weak comparison, lists and `*`, gets a `304` without a body (R-RES-2)."},"943":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-95","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#responses","content":"Errors are plain text with `Cache-Control: no-store` and no file system paths: `400` invalid request, `404` not found, `405` method, `413` original too large, `415` unsupported type, `422` unreadable image, `500` unexpected, `502` the origin failed, `503` busy and `504` the origin was too slow (R-RES-4)."},"944":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-96","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#caching","content":"Responses depend on `Accept` and the URL only, so a cache can key on the URL and a bucket of `Accept`: `image/avif`, `image/webp` or neither. Send the bucket as `Accept` upstream so that the body matches the key. The caching guide has an nginx recipe."},"945":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-97","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#limits","content":"At most `maxConcurrency` images are processed at once and `maxQueue` more wait in order. A request that finds the queue full gets `503` with `Retry-After: 1`, and a failing request frees its slot (R-LIM-1, R-LIM-2)."},"946":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-98","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#limits","content":"Decoding is limited by `maxInputPixels` (R-LIM-3)."},"947":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-99","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#limits","content":"`allowedWidths` optionally restricts the output widths to a list (R-LIM-4)."},"948":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-100","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#limits","content":"chop never writes to disk, and makes no network requests unless an origin or `allowedHosts` is configured, and then only to those hosts (R-LIM-5)."},"949":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-101","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `dataDir` | `CHOP_DATA_DIR`      | `/data` |","table":"table-2"},"950":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-102","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting   | Environment variable             | Default |\n| --------- | -------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `schemes` | `CHOP_SCHEMES` (comma separated) | `query` |","table":"table-2"},"951":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-103","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable | Default    |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxAge` | `CHOP_MAX_AGE`       | `31536000` |","table":"table-2"},"952":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-104","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable   | Default        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | -------------- |\n| `maxConcurrency` | `CHOP_MAX_CONCURRENCY` | number of CPUs |","table":"table-2"},"953":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-105","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable | Default |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxQueue` | `CHOP_MAX_QUEUE`     | `64`    |","table":"table-2"},"954":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-106","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable   | Default    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------- | ---------- |\n| `maxInputBytes` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_BYTES` | `52428800` |","table":"table-2"},"955":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-107","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable    | Default     |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | ----------- |\n| `maxInputPixels` | `CHOP_MAX_INPUT_PIXELS` | `120000000` |","table":"table-2"},"956":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-108","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting              | Environment variable        | Default |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxOutputDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_OUTPUT_DIMENSION` | `8192`  |","table":"table-2"},"957":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-109","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable         | Default |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- |\n| `maxUpscaleDimension` | `CHOP_MAX_UPSCALE_DIMENSION` | `4096`  |","table":"table-2"},"958":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-110","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                     | Environment variable                                          | Default          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `jpegQuality`, `webpQuality`, `avifQuality` | `CHOP_JPEG_QUALITY`, `CHOP_WEBP_QUALITY`, `CHOP_AVIF_QUALITY` | `82`, `80`, `55` |","table":"table-2"},"959":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-111","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avif`  | `CHOP_AVIF`          | `true`  |","table":"table-2"},"960":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-112","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `avifEffort` | `CHOP_AVIF_EFFORT`   | `4`     |","table":"table-2"},"961":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-113","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                    | Default |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `allowedWidths` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_WIDTHS` (comma separated) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"962":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-114","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting  | Environment variable                                        | Default |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `origin` | `CHOP_ORIGIN` (an `https://` URL or `s3://bucket[/prefix]`) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"963":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-115","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                 | Environment variable                                  | Default          |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `originAllowHttp`, `originAllowPrivate` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` | `false`, `false` |","table":"table-2"},"964":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-116","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default     |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ----------- |\n| `s3Endpoint` | `CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`   | unset (AWS) |","table":"table-2"},"965":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-117","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable           | Default                                               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Region` | `CHOP_S3_REGION`, `AWS_REGION` | unset (required on AWS), `us-east-1` with an endpoint |","table":"table-2"},"966":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-118","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Default                                 |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `s3PathStyle` | `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE` | `true` with an endpoint, `false` on AWS |","table":"table-2"},"967":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-119","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                                | Environment variable                                                                                      | Default |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `s3AccessKeyId`, `s3SecretAccessKey`, `s3SessionToken` | `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN`, with the `AWS_*` fallbacks | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"968":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-120","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Default |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `originAuth` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH`   | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"969":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-121","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                                 | Environment variable                                 | Default         |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `originConnectTimeout`, `originTimeout` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONNECT_TIMEOUT`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_TIMEOUT` | `3000`, `10000` |","table":"table-2"},"970":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-122","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting                            | Environment variable                           | Default   |\n| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | --------- |\n| `originConcurrency`, `originQueue` | `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY`, `CHOP_ORIGIN_QUEUE` | `4`, `32` |","table":"table-2"},"971":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-123","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting        | Environment variable                   | Default |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `allowedHosts` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (comma separated) | unset   |","table":"table-2"},"972":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-124","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting               | Environment variable                           | Default                  |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `allowedInputFormats` | `CHOP_ALLOWED_INPUT_FORMATS` (comma separated) | `jpeg,png,gif,webp,avif` |","table":"table-2"},"973":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-125","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#settings","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable                             | Default     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ----------- |\n| `autoFormats` | `CHOP_AUTO_FORMATS` (comma separated, or `none`) | `avif,webp` |","table":"table-2"},"974":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-126","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createHandler( settings? )` returns `( request ) => Promise< Response >` with `{ method, url, headers }` in and `{ status, headers, body }` out. It never throws for a request, never uses `node:http` and reports unexpected errors to an optional `onError`, risky settings to `onWarning` and the failures of an origin to `onOriginError` (R-API-1)."},"975":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-127","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"`createConfig()`, `configFromEnv( env )`, `configWarnings()`, the `Origin` interface with `createOrigin()`, `createLocalOrigin()` and `createHttpOrigin()`, `createS3Origin()`, `isBlockedAddress()`, `parseQuery()`, `createServer()`, the URL schemes `queryScheme` and `cloudflareScheme` with their `SCHEMES` registry and the `UrlScheme` type (`{ name, parse( url, options ) }`, where `parse` returns `{ segments, ops }`, with `url` set for a URL source, or `null`), and the other types are exported too (R-API-2, S-1)."},"976":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-128","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"Errors are `ChopError` with a `code` from `CHOP_ERROR_CODES`, checked with `isChopError()` (R-API-3)."},"977":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html-129","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/reference.html#interfaces","content":"The CLI is `chop [--data <dir> | --origin <url or s3://bucket>] [--port <n>] [--host <address>] [--scheme <name>] [--help]`, with flags overriding `CHOP_*` variables. A flag replaces the other source from the environment (`--origin` over `CHOP_DATA_DIR`, `--data` over `CHOP_ORIGIN`). Warnings about risky settings and the reasons for refused origin requests go to the standard error. Exit codes are `0`, `1` for a failure and `2` for invalid options. `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` stop it gracefully, and `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG=1` prints one JSON line per request (R-CLI-1 to R-CLI-4)."},"978":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","type":"page","content":"Requests","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html"},"979":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"Differences from Photon query arguments"},"980":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"The URL path selects the original, like `/2026/05/photo.jpg` for `<data>/2026/05/photo.jpg` or for `<origin>/2026/05/photo.jpg` when an origin is configured, and a URL scheme selects the operations. The default `query` scheme reads them from the query string. Unknown arguments are ignored, so cache-busting arguments like `ver=3` are harmless. A malformed value of a known argument is a `400` with a message that names the argument. `GET /healthz` answers `ok` without touching the data directory or the origin. Only `GET` and `HEAD` are allowed."},"981":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"Operations run in a fixed order, whatever the order in the URL: orientation, `crop`, size, `lb`, then encoding. The EXIF orientation is always applied to the pixels first, so every size and offset refers to the displayed image, and the output has no orientation tag."},"982":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument | Description                                                                                                  | Example                  |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------ |\n| `w`, `h` | Width and height in pixels. One keeps the aspect ratio, both fit inside the box without cropping or padding. | `?w=800`, `?w=800&h=600` |","table":"table-0"},"983":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument  | Description                                           | Example        |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `fit=w,h` | The same as `w` and `h` together, and wins over them. | `?fit=800,600` |","table":"table-0"},"984":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument     | Description                                                                                               | Example           |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `resize=w,h` | Cover `w` by `h` and crop the overflow, so the result is exactly that size. Wins over `fit`, `w` and `h`. | `?resize=400,400` |","table":"table-0"},"985":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument  | Description                                                                                          | Example                         |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | Where `resize` keeps the image: `center` (default), `north`, `south`, `east`, `west` or `attention`. | `?resize=400,400&gravity=north` |","table":"table-0"},"986":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument       | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Example                                          |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `crop=x,y,w,h` | A region of the oriented original, applied before scaling. Numbers are percentages of the width (`x`, `w`) or the height (`y`, `h`), with decimals allowed, or pixels with a `px` suffix. A region past the edge is clipped, and one with no area is a `400`. | `?crop=10,10,50,50`, `?crop=0px,0px,600px,400px` |","table":"table-0"},"987":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument         | Description                                                                                                                                                                       | Example                    |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `lb=w,h[,color]` | Letterbox: fit the image in the box, then pad it with `color` (3 or 6 hex digits, optional `#`, default `ffffff`) to exactly `w` by `h`, centered. Runs after the size operation. | `?w=300&lb=400,400,f5f5f5` |","table":"table-0"},"988":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument    | Description                                                    | Example             |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `upscale=1` | Allow enlarging, up to `maxUpscaleDimension` on the long side. | `?w=1200&upscale=1` |","table":"table-0"},"989":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument | Description                                                                                                         | Example         |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `zoom=N` | Device pixel ratio from 1 to 10, which multiplies `w`, `h`, `fit`, `resize` and `lb` sizes before the limits apply. | `?w=300&zoom=2` |","table":"table-0"},"990":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument | Description                                               | Example        |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `format` | `auto` (default), `jpeg`, `png`, `webp`, `avif` or `gif`. | `?format=webp` |","table":"table-0"},"991":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument  | Description            | Example       |\n| --------- | ---------------------- | ------------- |\n| `quality` | Integer from 1 to 100. | `?quality=70` |","table":"table-0"},"992":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument  | Description                                                        | Example    |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------- |\n| `lossy=1` | Allow lossy output of a lossless source (PNG, GIF, lossless WebP). | `?lossy=1` |","table":"table-0"},"993":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"| Argument | Description                                                                                                                                         | Example      |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `strip`  | `metadata` (default) removes EXIF, XMP and IPTC and keeps the ICC profile, `all` removes everything, `none` keeps everything the encoder can write. | `?strip=all` |","table":"table-0"},"994":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"Nothing enlarges the image unless `upscale=1`. When a requested size is larger than the image, `w`, `h` and `fit` clamp to the original size, `resize` crops to the requested aspect ratio at the largest size that fits, and `lb` pads without enlarging the image inside. With `upscale=1` the long side of a result may be as large as `maxUpscaleDimension`, but never less than the long side of the image itself. The output may not exceed `maxOutputDimension` in either dimension, which is checked after clamping and is a `400` when a request asks for more. When `allowedWidths` is set, the width of the output must be in the list or the request is a `400`."},"995":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","content":"For an animated source (GIF or animated WebP), `crop`, `w`, `h`, `fit` and `resize` apply to every frame and keep all frames and their timing, while `lb` and `gravity=attention` are ignored."},"996":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"chop has its own small set of arguments, and it isn't a drop-in replacement for the Photon image service. These arguments are not supported, are not an error and are ignored like any unknown argument:"},"997":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"`brightness` and `contrast` (no image adjustments)."},"998":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"`filter`, with its `grayscale`, `sepia`, `negate`, `blur` and `sharpen` names (no image filters)."},"999":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"`colorize` and `smooth`, and `ulb` (a letterbox with a color that is also scaled), which the specification doesn't have."},"1000":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"`webp` and `ssl`: the output format follows the `Accept` header, or `format`, and the server is not a proxy for other hosts."},"1001":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/requests.html#differences-from-photon-query-arguments","content":"Originals are only read from the data directory, the configured origin and the hosts that you allow, and `strip` has the values `metadata`, `all` and `none`."},"1002":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","type":"page","content":"Responses","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html"},"1003":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"A success is `200` with the `Content-Type` of the output, `Content-Length`, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=<maxAge>`, `Vary: Accept`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a strong `ETag` that is a SHA-256 of the body. An `If-None-Match` that matches the `ETag` (weak comparison, lists and `*`) gets `304` with the same `ETag`, `Cache-Control` and `Vary` and no body. A `HEAD` response has the headers of the `GET` response, including `Content-Length`, and no body."},"1004":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"Errors are plain text with a short message that doesn't reveal file system paths, `Cache-Control: no-store` and `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`."},"1005":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                                                                                           |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `400`  | Invalid request: an unsafe path, a malformed argument, a size over `maxOutputDimension` or a width that isn't in `allowedWidths`. |","table":"table-0"},"1006":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `404`  | Not found: a missing file, a directory, or a path that resolves outside the data directory, which all look the same. For a remote origin also an upstream `404`, `410`, `401`, `403` or `407`, a URL source that isn't allowed and a destination at a blocked address. |","table":"table-0"},"1007":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                        |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `405`  | A method other than `GET` and `HEAD`, with `Allow: GET, HEAD`. |","table":"table-0"},"1008":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                                         |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `413`  | The original is over `maxInputBytes`, which is checked before the file is read. |","table":"table-0"},"1009":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                               |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `415`  | The file is not a JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP or AVIF image. |","table":"table-0"},"1010":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                         |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `422`  | The image is corrupt, or has more than `maxInputPixels` pixels. |","table":"table-0"},"1011":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `502`  | The origin failed: it couldn't be reached, it answered with a `5xx` or another unexpected status, it redirected, or it sent a compressed or incomplete body. |","table":"table-0"},"1012":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                        |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `504`  | The origin was too slow to connect or to send the whole image. |","table":"table-0"},"1013":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning              |\n| ------ | -------------------- |\n| `500`  | An unexpected error. |","table":"table-0"},"1014":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"| Status | Meaning                                                             |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `503`  | The queue of images or of downloads is full, with `Retry-After: 1`. |","table":"table-0"},"1015":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/responses.html","content":"The error statuses `502` and `504` also have `Cache-Control: no-store`, as every error does. Each path segment is percent-decoded once, and a segment that is `.` or `..`, is empty, or contains `/`, `\\` or a NUL byte after decoding is a `400`. The real path of the file, with symbolic links resolved, must be inside the real path of the data directory."},"1016":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","type":"page","content":"S3 and S3-compatible storage","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html"},"1017":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"`CHOP_ORIGIN=s3://bucket` or `CHOP_ORIGIN=s3://bucket/prefix` reads the originals from a bucket, and `--origin s3://bucket` works too. The path of a request is appended to the prefix to make the key, so with `s3://my-bucket/uploads` the request `/2026/05/photo.jpg` reads the key `uploads/2026/05/photo.jpg`. Each segment is percent-encoded once, which is what S3 signs, so spaces, `+`, `!`, `*`, `'`, `(`, `)` and non-ASCII names work. The bucket name follows the S3 rules (3 to 63 lower case letters, digits, dots and hyphens), and a prefix can't have empty, `.` or `..` segments. An `s3://` origin can't be combined with an explicit `CHOP_DATA_DIR` or `--data`."},"1018":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"chop signs every request to the bucket with AWS Signature Version 4, using only `node:crypto`. Everything else is the same as for an HTTP origin: the pinned DNS lookup and address checks, no redirects, the size cap while reading, the timeouts, and the fetch limit and queue. `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP` and `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE` apply to the endpoint, and URL sources from `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` still work next to an S3 origin. They are fetched without a signature, and the credentials are never sent to them."},"1019":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"| Setting      | Environment variable | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Endpoint` | `CHOP_S3_ENDPOINT`   | Base URL of an S3-compatible service, like `http://seaweedfs:8333`. Unset means AWS. It is checked like an origin: `https://`, or `http://` with `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP`, without user information, a query string or a fragment, and a loopback, private or link-local address needs `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE`. |","table":"table-0"},"1020":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"| Setting    | Environment variable                | Description                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3Region` | `CHOP_S3_REGION`, then `AWS_REGION` | Region that requests are signed for. Required for AWS, and an invalid setting at startup without it. With an endpoint it defaults to `us-east-1`, and Cloudflare R2 uses `auto`. |","table":"table-0"},"1021":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"| Setting       | Environment variable | Description                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3PathStyle` | `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE` | `true` puts the bucket in the path (`https://host/bucket/key`), `false` in the host (`https://bucket.host/key`). Defaults to `true` with an endpoint and `false` for AWS. |","table":"table-0"},"1022":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"| Setting         | Environment variable                              | Description |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `s3AccessKeyId` | `CHOP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, then `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | Access key. |","table":"table-0"},"1023":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"| Setting             | Environment variable                                      | Description                                                                           |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3SecretAccessKey` | `CHOP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, then `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | Secret of the access key. Environment only, there is no flag, and it is never logged. |","table":"table-0"},"1024":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"| Setting          | Environment variable                              | Description                                                                                                          |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3SessionToken` | `CHOP_S3_SESSION_TOKEN`, then `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` | Token of temporary credentials, sent and signed as `x-amz-security-token`. Environment only, and it is never logged. |","table":"table-0"},"1025":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"On AWS the default is the virtual-hosted form, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`. A bucket name with dots falls back to the path-style form, `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`, because the wildcard certificate of AWS doesn't cover dotted names, and `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE=true` forces it. With an endpoint the default is `endpoint/bucket/key`, and `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE=false` uses `bucket.endpoint-host` instead, which needs a host name that can have subdomains and not an IP address."},"1026":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"Credentials need both a key and a secret. With only one of them, or with a session token alone, chop doesn't start (an invalid setting, which names the settings and not their values). With neither, requests are sent unsigned, which only works for a bucket with public read access, and chop prints a warning on startup that there are no credentials."},"1027":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"AWS or Lambda, with the credentials of the execution role that Lambda puts in the environment:"},"1028":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"SeaweedFS with its S3 gateway on the private network, over plain http:"},"1029":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"Cloudflare R2:"},"1030":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"A public bucket, without credentials (and with the warning):"},"1031":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"SeaweedFS can also serve a bucket through its filer over plain HTTP, which needs no signature and no S3 settings. That is the HTTP origin with the filer URL, `CHOP_ORIGIN=http://seaweedfs:8888/buckets/<bucket>`, together with `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP=1` and `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE=1`. Use it when the filer isn't exposed to anyone else, and the S3 origin when you want access keys."},"1032":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"Errors are answered like those of an HTTP origin. A missing key (`NoSuchKey`), a `403` and a `404` are a plain `404` for the client, a `5xx`, a network or TLS error and a redirect are a `502`, a timeout is a `504` and an object over `maxInputBytes` is a `413`. S3 explains an error in an XML body, and because a signature problem, a wrong key and a missing permission all look like a missing image to the client, chop reads at most the first 2048 bytes of the body of an error (and waits at most two seconds for them) and writes the `<Code>` to the standard error, like `origin ERR_NOT_FOUND: s3.example.com answered 403 SignatureDoesNotMatch`. Look there first when images are missing. Other codes to know are `AccessDenied`, `InvalidAccessKeyId`, `ExpiredToken`, `RequestTimeTooSkewed`, `NoSuchBucket` and `AuthorizationHeaderMalformed` (the region is wrong). The codes never reach the client, and neither do the credentials, which are not in any log, warning or error message. A `301` or `307` from S3 means that the bucket is in another region, which chop reports as `bucket is in another region (check CHOP_S3_REGION)` and doesn't follow."},"1033":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"**Clock skew.** S3 rejects a signature when the clock of the server is more than 15 minutes off, with `RequestTimeTooSkewed` or a `403`. That looks like a permission error, so check the code in the standard error and the time of the container."},"1034":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"**Credentials from the environment.** They are for Lambda and for static keys. chop reads them once at startup and doesn't refresh them, so temporary credentials with a session token stop working when they expire in a long-running process. Restart chop when they rotate, or use static keys for a server. It doesn't read instance metadata, shared credential files or web identity."},"1035":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"**Interface VPC endpoints.** A private endpoint for S3 resolves to private addresses, which chop blocks unless `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE=1` is set. With a custom endpoint that is a host name, set it together with the endpoint."},"1036":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/s3.html","content":"**GET only.** chop reads whole objects with a signed `GET`. It doesn't list buckets, use ranges or presigned URLs."},"1037":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","type":"page","content":"Securing remote origins","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html"},"1038":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"Putting chop behind a trusted proxy or a CDN limits who can send requests to it, and that's worth having. It doesn't decide where chop connects: the proxy still passes the path of the request to chop, so the protection against reaching internal hosts has to be in chop, and it is. Don't assume that a proxy rule is the only thing between a client and an internal address."},"1039":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"Prefer the configured origin. The host is fixed by you, so a client can only choose a path under it, and there is nothing to allow-list. Use `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` only when a client has to choose the host, and list the hosts that you mean. Every host on the list is reachable by every client that can reach chop."},"1040":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"`CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=*` makes chop an open image proxy: anyone who can send a request to chop can make it fetch and process images from any public host. The address checks, https, the size and time limits and the fetch limit still apply, but they can't stop someone from using your server and your bandwidth to fetch from the public internet, or from reaching a service that only accepts connections from your server's network, at a public address. The protection that matters then is outside of chop. If you use `*`:"},"1041":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"Run chop with an egress firewall that only allows what it needs, so that a mistake in an address range can't reach your network."},"1042":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"Set `allowedWidths` to the widths of your `srcset`, so that the output sizes are bounded, and keep `maxInputBytes`, `maxInputPixels` and the `CHOP_ORIGIN_*` limits low."},"1043":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"Cache in front: `proxy_cache_min_uses 2` in the nginx recipe keeps one-off URLs out of the cache, and `proxy_cache_lock on` limits the fetches to one for each variant."},"1044":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"Let only the proxy reach chop, and authenticate or sign the URLs there."},"1045":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"More to know about remote originals:"},"1046":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"chop doesn't cache originals. The proxy caches the output, and a request that isn't cached downloads the original again. An original that changes at the same URL stays stale until the cached outputs expire or are purged, so use new URLs for new versions (WordPress uploads do), or a short `CHOP_MAX_AGE`. The upstream `Cache-Control`, `ETag` and `Last-Modified` headers are ignored, and the output headers are the same as for local files."},"1047":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"A `502` and a `504` have `Cache-Control: no-store`, and the proxy must not cache them. The nginx recipe only caches `200` and `404`."},"1048":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"Redirects are not followed, so an origin that redirects (a CDN that moves an object, a trailing slash redirect) needs the final URL in `CHOP_ORIGIN`."},"1049":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"Only HTTP/1.1 is used and TLS certificates are always verified. A private CA is added to Node.js with `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`."},"1050":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/security.html","content":"An alternative that keeps chop local-only is to let nginx `proxy_pass` to the origin and store the files in a directory that chop serves, or to mount the bucket with rclone or s3fs (or to use the S3 origin, which needs no mount). That needs a second hop and a shared directory, but chop makes no network requests then."},"1051":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","type":"page","content":"Sources","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html"},"1052":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"What chop does for every remote fetch"},"1053":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"An original comes from one of four places, and every request reads exactly one of them:"},"1054":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"**The data directory.** The default. A plain path like `/2026/05/photo.jpg` is a file under `dataDir`, with the path checks of Responses."},"1055":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"**The configured origin.** With `CHOP_ORIGIN=https://uploads.example.com/base`, the same plain path is appended to the base URL: `/2026/05/photo.jpg` is fetched from `https://uploads.example.com/base/2026/05/photo.jpg`. Clients never supply a host. This is the recommended way to use a remote origin, and plain paths go to the origin instead of the data directory, so `CHOP_ORIGIN` can't be combined with an explicitly set `CHOP_DATA_DIR` or `--data`. The origin must be an `https://` URL without user information, a query string or a fragment, or `http://` with `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP=1`."},"1056":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"**An S3 bucket.** With `CHOP_ORIGIN=s3://my-bucket/uploads`, the plain path `/2026/05/photo.jpg` is the object `uploads/2026/05/photo.jpg` of the bucket, which chop reads with signed `GET` requests. It works with AWS S3 and with services that have an S3 API, like SeaweedFS, MinIO and Cloudflare R2, and it follows all the rules of the configured origin. See S3 and S3-compatible storage."},"1057":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"**URL sources.** With `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` set, a request can name the full URL of the original, and chop fetches it if the host is on the list. Plain paths keep their meaning, and only a path that starts with `http://` or `https://` is a URL source. Without the setting, which is the default, these URLs are a `404`."},"1058":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"URL sources work in both schemes. In the `query` scheme the URL is the path and the query string is chop's arguments, and in the `cloudflare` scheme the URL comes after the options:"},"1059":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"A proxy that merges slashes turns `https://` into `https:/`, and some clients escape it as `https%3A//`. chop understands all three forms, with any number of slashes after the colon. A URL source can't have user information, a fragment or a query string of its own: the query string of the `query` scheme is chop's arguments, so the source can't have one, and in the `cloudflare` scheme a query string on a URL source is a `400` rather than a guess about which part it belongs to. User information and fragments are a `400` too. Ports other than 80 and 443 must be named in the allow-list."},"1060":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"Each entry of `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` is a comma separated list item:"},"1061":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"| Entry                 | Matches                                       |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `uploads.example.com` | That host, on the default port of the scheme. |","table":"table-0"},"1062":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"| Entry           | Matches                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `*.example.com` | Any subdomain at any depth, on a dot boundary, so `a.example.com` and `a.b.example.com` match, but `example.com` and `evilexample.com` don't. List the apex too if you need it. |","table":"table-0"},"1063":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"| Entry                      | Matches                                              |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `uploads.example.com:8443` | That host on that port, and not on the default port. |","table":"table-0"},"1064":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"| Entry | Matches                                                                                                                                  |\n| ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `*`   | Every host, on the default ports. It can't be mixed with other entries, and it prints a warning on startup. See Securing remote origins. |","table":"table-0"},"1065":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"Hosts are compared in lower case and without a trailing dot. International names must be written in punycode (`xn--...`). An empty list means no URL sources."},"1066":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","content":"Whatever the source, the original is downloaded into memory, up to `maxInputBytes`, before it is processed. `X-Bytes-Saved` is measured against the downloaded size, the `ETag` is still a hash of the output, and when re-encoding doesn't make the image smaller, the downloaded bytes are sent as they are. The type of the image is found from its content, and the `Content-Type` that the origin states is ignored."},"1067":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-15","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"These apply to the configured origin and to URL sources, with any allow-list, including `*`:"},"1068":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-16","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"Only `https` is used, unless `CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_HTTP` is set."},"1069":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-17","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"The request is a `GET` with fresh headers: `Accept: image/*`, `Accept-Encoding: identity` and `User-Agent: chop`. No cookie, `Authorization`, `Referer` or other header of the client is forwarded. A compressed response is a `502`."},"1070":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-18","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"Redirects are not followed. A `3xx` from the origin is a `502`."},"1071":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-19","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"The host name is resolved once, every address is checked, and the connection is made to one of the addresses that were checked, so DNS rebinding can't swap the address between the check and the connection. An address literal in a URL is checked too, in any notation (`2130706433`, `0x7f.1`, `[::ffff:7f00:1]`). Loopback, private, link-local (including the cloud metadata address `169.254.169.254`), carrier-grade NAT, documentation, multicast and reserved ranges are never connected to, for IPv4 and IPv6, including IPv4-mapped and NAT64 forms. If a name resolves to several addresses and any of them is blocked, the request is not made."},"1072":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-20","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"The body is cut off at `maxInputBytes` while it is read, whether or not the origin sends `Content-Length`, and a larger `Content-Length` is a `413` before the body is read."},"1073":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-21","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"Connecting, including the TLS handshake, must finish within `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONNECT_TIMEOUT` (3000 ms) and the whole download within `CHOP_ORIGIN_TIMEOUT` (10000 ms), or the answer is a `504`."},"1074":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-22","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"At most `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY` downloads (4) run at the same time and `CHOP_ORIGIN_QUEUE` (32) wait. More are a `503` with `Retry-After: 1`. Downloads don't use a processing slot, so a slow origin doesn't stop images from being processed, but the memory in use can reach `CHOP_ORIGIN_CONCURRENCY` times `maxInputBytes`, so lower one of them on a small machine."},"1075":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-23","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"The body of a response that isn't a `200` is dropped without being read. The only exception is an S3 bucket, where chop reads the first 2048 bytes of the body of an error, for at most two seconds, to find the error code for the operator."},"1076":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-24","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"A host name that can't be resolved is a `502` for the configured origin and the same plain `404` for a URL source, so that a client can't tell which names exist. The reason is only written to the standard error, as a host and an error code, never an error message."},"1077":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-25","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"Upstream `404` and `410` are a `404`. A `401`, `403` or `407` from the origin and a destination that isn't allowed are the same plain `404`, so that a client can't tell which hosts exist, which are blocked or whether the origin needs credentials. The reason is only written to the standard error. An origin that fails or answers with another status is a `502`."},"1078":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-26","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"`CHOP_ORIGIN_AUTH` is the value of an `Authorization` header, like `Bearer <token>`, for a private origin. It is only sent to the configured origin and never to URL sources, it is read from the environment only, and it is never logged. A value with a line break or a control character is an invalid setting."},"1079":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html-27","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/sources.html#what-chop-does-for-every-remote-fetch","content":"`CHOP_ORIGIN_ALLOW_PRIVATE=1` lets the configured origin be at a loopback, private or link-local address, like another container or a service on your private network. It applies only to the configured origin, never to a URL that a client supplied, and chop prints a warning on startup. Without it, an origin whose address is an IP literal in a blocked range is an invalid setting, and one whose name resolves to a blocked range is a `404`."},"1080":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","type":"page","content":"URL schemes","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","chop","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html"},"1081":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-0","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#query","content":"`query`"},"1082":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-1","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"`cloudflare`"},"1083":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-2","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","content":"A URL scheme turns the URL of a request into the path of the original and the operations to run on it. All the schemes produce the same operations, so every scheme gets the same format negotiation, limits and path safety, and different schemes that give the same operations give the same bytes and `ETag`. Enable them with `schemes` in the settings, `CHOP_SCHEMES` or `--scheme`, which can be repeated."},"1084":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-3","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","content":"The schemes are tried in the configured order, and the first one that recognizes the URL wins. A URL that none of them recognizes is a `404`. `/healthz` doesn't depend on the schemes. The `query` scheme recognizes every URL, so when it's enabled together with other schemes, list it last. The path of a scheme goes through the same checks as any path: dot segments, empty segments, slashes, backslashes and NUL bytes in a decoded segment are a `400`, and the real path must stay inside the data directory. A scheme can also find a URL source in the URL."},"1085":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-4","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","content":"With `Accept: image/avif`, both of these URLs give the same AVIF bytes."},"1086":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-5","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#query","content":"The default scheme. The path is the path of the original and the arguments in Requests are in the query string. A path that starts with `http://` or `https://` (also `https:/` and `https%3A//`) is a URL source, like `/https://uploads.example.com/photo.jpg?w=300`, and the query string is still chop's arguments, so the source URL can't have its own."},"1087":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-6","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"The `/cdn-cgi/image/<options>/<path>` form of Cloudflare Image Resizing, with comma separated `name=value` options. It only recognizes URLs that start with `/cdn-cgi/image/`. Options that chop doesn't support, like `trim`, `rotate`, `blur`, `sharpen` and `onerror`, are ignored, and a malformed value of a supported option is a `400` that names the option. The first value wins when an option repeats. A source after the options that starts with `http://` or `https://` (also `https:/` and `https%3A//`) is a URL source, which is a `404` unless `CHOP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` is set. A query string on a URL source is a `400`, and on a path under the origin it is ignored."},"1088":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-7","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option            | Maps to   |\n| ----------------- | --------- |\n| `width`, `height` | `w`, `h`. |","table":"table-0"},"1089":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-8","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `fit`  | `scale-down` (default) is `w` and `h` that never enlarge, `contain` is the same with `upscale=1`, `cover` is `resize` with `upscale=1`, `crop` is `resize`, and `pad` is `lb` with `upscale=1`. `cover`, `crop` and `pad` need both `width` and `height`, and with one of them they scale like `scale-down` (`crop`) or `contain` (`cover` and `pad`). |","table":"table-0"},"1090":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-9","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gravity` | `left`, `right`, `top` and `bottom` are `west`, `east`, `north` and `south`, `auto` and `face` are `attention`, and `center` and coordinates like `0.5x0.3` are the center. |","table":"table-0"},"1091":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-10","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option    | Maps to                               |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `quality` | `quality`, as a number from 1 to 100. |","table":"table-0"},"1092":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-11","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option   | Maps to                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `auto`, `avif`, `webp`, `jpeg`, `png` and `gif` are `format`, and `baseline-jpeg` is `jpeg`. `json` is a `400`. |","table":"table-0"},"1093":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-12","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option | Maps to               |\n| ------ | --------------------- |\n| `dpr`  | `zoom`, from 1 to 10. |","table":"table-0"},"1094":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-13","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option     | Maps to                                                                            |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `keep` is `strip=none`, `copyright` is `strip=metadata` and `none` is `strip=all`. |","table":"table-0"},"1095":{"id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html-14","page_id":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/chop/v0.2.1/url-schemes.html#cloudflare","content":"| Option       | Maps to                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `background` | The `lb` color for `fit=pad`, as 3 or 6 hex digits with an optional `#` (encoded as `%23` in a URL). |","table":"table-0"},"1096":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html","type":"page","content":"Caching","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html"},"1097":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html","content":"Every run splits the whole history again. `--git-dir-cache` remembers the results in `.git/subtree-split-cache/`, so the next run only processes the commits that are new. On gutenberg that takes `packages/components` from 1.7 seconds to 0.3. On a small repository it makes no difference."},"1098":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html-1","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html","content":"A fresh CI checkout has no cache. Give `--cache` a file that you save and restore between runs, or set it once with `SUBTREE_SPLIT_CACHE`."},"1099":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html-2","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/caching.html","content":"A cache that is missing, belongs to another prefix, or has commits that were garbage collected is ignored and the history is split again, so it only costs time. To start over, delete the file."},"1100":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","type":"page","content":"CLI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html"},"1101":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","content":"| Option                 | Description                                                           |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-P`, `--prefix <dir>` | Directory to split, relative to the root of the repository. Required. |","table":"table-0"},"1102":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html-1","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","content":"| Option                 | Description                                        |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-r`, `--ref <commit>` | Commit to split the history of, `HEAD` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1103":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html-2","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","content":"| Option        | Description                                                    |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--cwd <dir>` | Directory in the repository, the current directory by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1104":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html-3","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","content":"| Option            | Description                                                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--git-dir-cache` | Remember the split commits in a file named after the prefix in the Git directory, like `.git/subtree-split-cache/packages-my-library.json`. |","table":"table-0"},"1105":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html-4","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","content":"| Option           | Description                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--cache <file>` | Remember the split commits in this file instead. Defaults to the path in the `SUBTREE_SPLIT_CACHE` environment variable. |","table":"table-0"},"1106":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html-5","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","content":"| Option            | Description                                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--github-output` | Set the outputs of a GitHub Actions step. Needs the `GITHUB_OUTPUT` variable that GitHub Actions sets, and fails before splitting without it. |","table":"table-0"},"1107":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html-6","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","content":"| Option         | Description     |\n| -------------- | --------------- |\n| `-h`, `--help` | Show the usage. |","table":"table-0"},"1108":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html-7","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/cli.html","content":"The exit code is 0 for a split and 1 when it fails or the directory doesn't exist at the ref, like for `git subtree split`. It's 2 for invalid options. Errors go to the standard error output."},"1109":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","type":"page","content":"Compatibility with git subtree split","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html"},"1110":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html#limits","content":"Limits"},"1111":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html-1","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html#how-it-matches-git-subtree-split","content":"How it matches git subtree split"},"1112":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html-2","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html#limits","content":"Git 2.29 or later. The rules of `git subtree split` for merges changed in Git 2.20, and older versions make other commits that this package doesn't reproduce."},"1113":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html-3","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html#limits","content":"One prefix per call. There is no `--rejoin`, `--squash`, `--onto` or `--annotate`, and the `git-subtree-*` trailers of earlier `git subtree add` and `split --rejoin` commands aren't read."},"1114":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html-4","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html#limits","content":"A name with a backslash, or a commit in an encoding that `TextDecoder` doesn't know, may differ from what the shell script writes."},"1115":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html-5","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html#how-it-matches-git-subtree-split","content":"The package is a port of the rules of `process_split_commit` and `copy_or_skip` in `git-subtree.sh`, including its oddities. A commit that doesn't have the directory but whose parents do maps to itself, and a commit is only dropped in favor of a parent with the same tree when no history of another branch would be lost. Commits are written with the author, committer, dates and message of the original, without signatures and other extra headers, and with the names cleaned like `git commit-tree` does. The hashes are calculated in Node and written with one `git fast-import` process, which checks that Git wrote the same hash."},"1116":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html-6","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html#how-it-matches-git-subtree-split","content":"The tests in `src` run both implementations on the same repositories and compare the tips and the commit objects. They cover linear history, merges where one or both sides touch the directory, branches that make the same change, octopus merges, a directory that is added late, removed and added back or renamed, empty commits, authors that differ from committers, time zones, names with punctuation, messages without a trailing newline, a commit in another encoding, signed commits, and random histories of branches and merges built to often end up with the same tree."},"1117":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html-7","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/compatibility.html#how-it-matches-git-subtree-split","content":"The default run has 10 random histories, and the variable sets how many there are. The monorepo check splits every package of this repository with both implementations. It takes a few minutes because of `git subtree split`, so it runs on demand."},"1118":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html","type":"page","content":"Development","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html"},"1119":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html#license","content":"License"},"1120":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html-1","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html","content":"`npm run bench` clones a repository to a temporary directory and times `git subtree split` and this package, cold, from the cache and after one new commit."},"1121":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html-2","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/development.html#license","content":"MIT"},"1122":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/github-actions.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/github-actions.html","type":"page","content":"GitHub Actions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/github-actions.html"},"1123":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/github-actions.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/github-actions.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/github-actions.html","content":"`--github-output` sets the `hash`, `prefix`, `ref` and `result` outputs of the step. `result` has all of them as JSON."},"1124":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","type":"page","content":"subtree-split","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html"},"1125":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","content":"Split a monorepo directory into its own history, with the same commit hashes as git subtree split."},"1126":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-1","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#install","content":"Install"},"1127":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-2","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"1128":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-3","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Guides"},"1129":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-4","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","content":"Split a directory of a monorepo into its own history, with the same commit hashes as `git subtree split`, in about a tenth of a second instead of several seconds."},"1130":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-5","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","content":"In a monorepo with 477 commits, `git subtree split` takes 6 to 8 seconds for one package and `subtree-split` takes 0.1 seconds. On WordPress/gutenberg (43,568 commits) it splits `packages/components` in 1.7 seconds. The hashes are the same as `git subtree split` makes, so a repository that you already split that way keeps its history when you switch."},"1131":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-6","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","content":"`@wpelevator/wp-release` uses it for `deploy git --split-prefix`."},"1132":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-7","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#install","content":"It needs Node.js 22.12 or later, Git 2.29 or later, and the full history of the repository. It works in a bare clone, and it fails with a message on a shallow one, so in CI check out with `fetch-depth: 0`."},"1133":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-8","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#quick-start","content":"Run it in the monorepo, with the directory that you want to split:"},"1134":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-9","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#quick-start","content":"It prints the hash of the split commit and writes the commits to the repository. It doesn't change a branch, so you decide what to do with the hash. To publish it to the repository of the package:"},"1135":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-10","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#quick-start","content":"To keep it in a local branch instead, run `git update-ref refs/heads/split/my-library \"$tip\"`."},"1136":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-11","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#guides","content":"CLI"},"1137":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-12","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#guides","content":"GitHub Actions"},"1138":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-13","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Caching split results"},"1139":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-14","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Library API"},"1140":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-15","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Compatibility with git subtree split"},"1141":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html-16","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/index.html#guides","content":"Development"},"1142":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","type":"page","content":"Library API","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","Latest"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html"},"1143":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","content":"`splitHistory()` returns the hash of the split commit, or `null` when the directory doesn't exist at the ref. Like the command, it writes the commits to the repository and doesn't change a branch."},"1144":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html-1","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","content":"| Option   | Description                                                                              |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `prefix` | Directory to split, relative to the root of the repository. A trailing slash is removed. |","table":"table-0"},"1145":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html-2","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","content":"| Option | Description                                        |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ref`  | Commit to split the history of, `HEAD` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1146":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html-3","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","content":"| Option | Description                                                    |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cwd`  | Directory in the repository, the current directory by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1147":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html-4","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","content":"| Option  | Description                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cache` | `true` for the file in the Git directory, like `--git-dir-cache`, or the path of a cache file, like `--cache`. Without it, every call splits the whole history. |","table":"table-0"},"1148":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html-5","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/latest/library.html","content":"Invalid input and history that can't be split throw a `SubtreeSplitError` with a Node-style `code`: `ERR_INVALID_PREFIX`, `ERR_UNSUPPORTED_GIT`, `ERR_SHALLOW_REPOSITORY`, `ERR_GIT_FAILED`, `ERR_INVALID_COMMIT`, `ERR_INVALID_TREE_ENTRY` or `ERR_COMMIT_MISMATCH`. `isSubtreeSplitError( error )` checks for one, which also works when two copies of the package are installed, unlike `instanceof`. A directory that doesn't exist at the ref isn't an error, but a file at the prefix in any commit is, like in `git subtree split`. Other errors, like Git not being installed, are the original errors of Node.js."},"1149":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html","type":"page","content":"Caching","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html"},"1150":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html","content":"Every run splits the whole history again. `--git-dir-cache` remembers the results in `.git/subtree-split-cache/`, so the next run only processes the commits that are new. On gutenberg that takes `packages/components` from 1.7 seconds to 0.3. On a small repository it makes no difference."},"1151":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html-1","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html","content":"A fresh CI checkout has no cache. Give `--cache` a file that you save and restore between runs, or set it once with `SUBTREE_SPLIT_CACHE`."},"1152":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html-2","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/caching.html","content":"A cache that is missing, belongs to another prefix, or has commits that were garbage collected is ignored and the history is split again, so it only costs time. To start over, delete the file."},"1153":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","type":"page","content":"CLI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Js","subtree-split","v0.2.1"],"tags":[],"url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html"},"1154":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html-0","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Option                 | Description                                                           |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-P`, `--prefix <dir>` | Directory to split, relative to the root of the repository. Required. |","table":"table-0"},"1155":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html-1","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Option                 | Description                                        |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-r`, `--ref <commit>` | Commit to split the history of, `HEAD` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1156":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html-2","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Option        | Description                                                    |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--cwd <dir>` | Directory in the repository, the current directory by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1157":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html-3","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Option            | Description                                                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--git-dir-cache` | Remember the split commits in a file named after the prefix in the Git directory, like `.git/subtree-split-cache/packages-my-library.json`. |","table":"table-0"},"1158":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html-4","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Option           | Description                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--cache <file>` | Remember the split commits in this file instead. Defaults to the path in the `SUBTREE_SPLIT_CACHE` environment variable. |","table":"table-0"},"1159":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html-5","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Option            | Description                                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--github-output` | Set the outputs of a GitHub Actions step. Needs the `GITHUB_OUTPUT` variable that GitHub Actions sets, and fails before splitting without it. |","table":"table-0"},"1160":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html-6","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"| Option         | Description     |\n| -------------- | --------------- |\n| `-h`, `--help` | Show the usage. |","table":"table-0"},"1161":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html-7","page_id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/cli.html","content":"The exit code is 0 for a split and 1 when it fails or the directory doesn't exist at the ref, like for `git subtree split`. It's 2 for invalid options. Errors go to the standard error output."},"1162":{"id":"/js/subtree-split/v0.2.1/compatibility.ht