 When `allowedWidths` is set, the width of the output must be in the list or the request is a `400`."],[994,"Nothing enlarges the image unless `upscale=1`. When a requested size is larger than the image, `w`, `h` and `fit` clamp to the original size, `resize` crops to the requested aspect ratio at the largest size that fits, and `lb` pads without enlarging the image inside. With `upscale=1` the long side of a result may be as large as `maxUpscaleDimension`, but never less than the long side of the image itself. The output may not exceed `maxOutputDimension` in either dimension, which is checked after clamping and is a `400` when a request asks for more. When `allowedWidths` is set, the width of the output must be in the list or the request is a `400`."],[191,"On AWS the bucket is in the host, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`, unless `s3PathStyle` is true or the bucket name has dots, which use `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`. A custom endpoint is `endpoint/bucket/key` unless `s3PathStyle` is false, which uses `bucket.endpoint-host`. The endpoint is checked like the origin: https, or http with `originAllowHttp`, no user information, query string or fragment, and no blocked address without `originAllowPrivate` (R-S3-3)."],[612,"On AWS the bucket is in the host, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`, unless `s3PathStyle` is true or the bucket name has dots, which use `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`. A custom endpoint is `endpoint/bucket/key` unless `s3PathStyle` is false, which uses `bucket.endpoint-host`. The endpoint is checked like the origin: https, or http with `originAllowHttp`, no user information, query string or fragment, and no blocked address without `originAllowPrivate` (R-S3-3)."],[890,"On AWS the bucket is in the host, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`, unless `s3PathStyle` is true or the bucket name has dots, which use `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`. A custom endpoint is `endpoint/bucket/key` unless `s3PathStyle` is false, which uses `bucket.endpoint-host`. The endpoint is checked like the origin: https, or http with `originAllowHttp`, no user information, query string or fragment, and no blocked address without `originAllowPrivate` (R-S3-3)."],[326,"On AWS the default is the virtual-hosted form, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`. A bucket name with dots falls back to the path-style form, `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`, because the wildcard certificate of AWS doesn't cover dotted names, and `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE=true` forces it. With an endpoint the default is `endpoint/bucket/key`, and `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE=false` uses `bucket.endpoint-host` instead, which needs a host name that can have subdomains and not an IP address."],[1025,"On AWS the default is the virtual-hosted form, `bucket.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com`. A bucket name with dots falls back to the path-style form, `s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/bucket/key`, because the wildcard certificate of AWS doesn't cover dotted names, and `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE=true` forces it. With an endpoint the default is `endpoint/bucket/key`, and `CHOP_S3_PATH_STYLE=false` uses `bucket.endpoint-host` instead, which needs a host name that can have subdomains and not an IP address."],[1320,"On the release branch, preview with `changeset version --dry-run`, then run `changeset version` to update version targets and changelogs. By default, new Markdown entries go before the first version heading; `changelogInsertAfter` sets a literal insertion marker for `CHANGELOG.md` and, with `readmeChangelog`, the plugin readme. Put the marker in both files; a missing marker is an error. Without a marker, plugin readmes use the `== Changelog ==` heading. Failed updates are rolled back for safe retries."],[4288,"On the release branch, preview with `changeset version --dry-run`, then run `changeset version` to update version targets and changelogs. By default, new Markdown entries go before the first version heading; `changelogInsertAfter` sets a literal insertion marker for `CHAN