ll requests add changesets, open a release pull request whenever changesets are pending on `main`, and after it's merged, create the tag and GitHub release of every released package. Packagist picks up the new tags of Composer packages; add the WP Release Zip and WP Release Deploy SVN actions to the `release` job to ship a WordPress plugin."],[4922,"The command is `changeset` with subcommands, like `changeset add`, where `wp-release` has `changeset-add` among its other commands. Run `changeset --help` for the commands."],[1441,"The commands read the same headers as WordPress. The main plugin file is the top-level `.php` file with a `Plugin Name:` header in its first 8 KB, preferring `{slug}.php` when several files have one. A directory without a plugin file and with `Theme Name:` in `style.css` is a theme. The readme headers (`Stable tag`, `Tested up to`, …) come from `readme.txt`, or `readme.md` when there's no `readme.txt`."],[1863,"The commands read the same headers as WordPress. The main plugin file is the top-level `.php` file with a `Plugin Name:` header in its first 8 KB, preferring `{slug}.php` when several files have one. A directory without a plugin file and with `Theme Name:` in `style.css` is a theme. The readme headers (`Stable tag`, `Tested up to`, …) come from `readme.txt`, or `readme.md` when there's no `readme.txt`."],[2283,"The commands read the same headers as WordPress. The main plugin file is the top-level `.php` file with a `Plugin Name:` header in its first 8 KB, preferring `{slug}.php` when several files have one. A directory without a plugin file and with `Theme Name:` in `style.css` is a theme. The readme headers (`Stable tag`, `Tested up to`, …) come from `readme.txt`, or `readme.md` when there's no `readme.txt`."],[2705,"The commands read the same headers as WordPress. The main plugin file is the top-level `.php` file with a `Plugin Name:` header in its first 8 KB, preferring `{slug}.php` when several files have one. A directory without a